Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.57,0:01:15.12,中文,,0,0,0,,《猫鼠游戏》 
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.60,0:03:06.65,中文,,0,0,0,,这是一个真实故事的启发
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.81,0:03:07.94,中文,,0,0,0,,真真假假
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.27,0:03:11.03,中文,,0,0,0,,非常感谢 欢迎各位来到《真真假假》\N{\r外文}Thank you very much and welcome to To Tell the Truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.11,0:03:15.53,中文,,0,0,0,,我们的第一位客人 是我们这个节目 有史以来邀请过的\N{\r外文}Our first guest, he's made a career out of being the most outrageous impostor
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.61,0:03:19.78,中文,,0,0,0,,最无耻的以冒名顶替为生的骗子 你就会明白我的意思的\N{\r外文}that we've ever come across on this show. You'll see what I mean.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.91,0:03:22.37,中文,,0,0,0,,1号选手 请问你叫什么名字\N{\r外文}Number One, what is your name, please?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.45,0:03:24.46,中文,,0,0,0,,我叫弗兰克·威廉·阿巴戈内尔\N{\r外文}My name is Frank William Abagnale.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.54,0:03:27.96,中文,,0,0,0,,2号选手呢 我叫弗兰克·威廉·阿巴戈内尔\N{\r外文}Number Two? My name is Frank William Abagnale.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.13,0:03:31.46,中文,,0,0,0,,3号选手呢 我叫弗兰克·威廉·阿巴戈内尔\N{\r外文}Number Three? My name is Frank William Abagnale.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.63,0:03:34.38,中文,,0,0,0,,从1964年到1967年\N{\r外文}From 1964 to 1967,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.47,0:03:38.55,中文,,0,0,0,,我成功地冒充了泛美航空公司的飞行员\N{\r外文}I successfully impersonated an airline pilot for Pan Am Airways,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.64,0:03:41.47,中文,,0,0,0,,免费飞了3百多万公里\N{\r外文}and I flew over two million miles for free.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.60,0:03:42.72,中文,,0,0,0,,那段时间\N{\r外文}During that time,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.81,0:03:46.73,中文,,0,0,0,,我还是佐治亚州一家医院的儿科见习医生主管\N{\r外文}I was also the Chief Resident Paediatrician at a Georgia hospital
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.81,0:03:50.23,中文,,0,0,0,,及路易斯安那州首席检察官的一名助理\N{\r外文}and an Assistant Attorney General for the State of Louisiana.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.31,0:03:51.90,中文,,0,0,0,,我被逮捕时\N{\r外文}By the time I was caught,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.98,0:03:56.40,中文,,0,0,0,,我被认为是美国历史上 最年轻及最胆大的骗子\N{\r外文}I was considered the youngest and most daring con man in U.S. history.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.49,0:03:59.66,中文,,0,0,0,,我用伪造的支票套取了约4百万美元的现金\N{\r外文}I had cashed almost $4 million in fraudulent cheques
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.78,0:04:02.99,中文,,0,0,0,,在美国境外的26个国家和境内的50个州里\N{\r外文}in 26 foreign countries and all 50 states.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.08,0:04:06.33,中文,,0,0,0,,而所有这些都是在我19岁生日之前做的\N{\r外文}And I did it all before my 19th birthday.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.66,0:04:09.67,中文,,0,0,0,,我叫弗兰克·威廉·阿巴戈内尔\N{\r外文}My name is Frank William Abagnale.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.17,0:04:16.92,中文,,0,0,0,,所以 他今天要第一次讲真话了\N{\r外文}So, for the first time, he'll have to tell the truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.01,0:04:19.09,中文,,0,0,0,,首先由基蒂发问\N{\r外文}We'll start our questioning with Kitty.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.18,0:04:21.93,中文,,0,0,0,,1号选手 凭你的聪明才智\N{\r外文}Thank you. Number One, why, with all your talent,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.01,0:04:24.10,中文,,0,0,0,,你肯定是个非常聪明的家伙\N{\r外文}and you're obviously a very bright fellow,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.18,0:04:27.48,中文,,0,0,0,,你为什么不找个合法的职业谋生\N{\r外文}why didn't you go in for a legitimate profession?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.69,0:04:29.77,中文,,0,0,0,,是个挣钱多少的问题\N{\r外文}It was a question of dollars and cents.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.85,0:04:31.73,中文,,0,0,0,,我想这些职业\N{\r外文}When I was a young man, I needed the money,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.81,0:04:34.53,中文,,0,0,0,,是我挣钱的最简单的方法\N{\r外文}and I thought this list of careers was the easiest way to get it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.61,0:04:38.45,中文,,0,0,0,,明白了 2号选手 我发现这真奇妙\N{\r外文}I see. Number Two, I find this all very fascinating.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.53,0:04:41.16,中文,,0,0,0,,是谁最后抓住你的\N{\r外文}Who was it that finally caught you?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.03,0:04:43.70,中文,,0,0,0,,他叫卡尔·汉莱提\N{\r外文}His name was Carl Hanratty.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.41,0:04:48.75,中文,,0,0,0,,汉莱提\N{\r外文}Hanratty.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.71,0:04:53.80,中文,,0,0,0,,我叫\N{\r外文}I am
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.42,0:04:55.84,中文,,0,0,0,,卡尔·汉莱提\N{\r外文}Carl Hanratty.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.92,0:04:59.51,中文,,0,0,0,,我代表美国的联邦调查局\N{\r外文}I represent the F.B.I. from the United States of America.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.05,0:05:05.43,中文,,0,0,0,,我有官方许可来见那个美国囚犯 阿巴戈内尔\N{\r外文}I have orders to see the American prisoner, Abagnale.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.92,0:05:09.76,中文,,0,0,0,,法国马赛 圣诞前夜 1969年
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.17,0:05:35.67,中文,,0,0,0,,你坐这里\N{\r外文}You sit here.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.88,0:05:38.97,中文,,0,0,0,,不许开这扇门\N{\r外文}You do not open the door.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.05,0:05:41.97,中文,,0,0,0,,不许从这小孔\N{\r外文}You do not pass him
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.05,0:05:45.30,中文,,0,0,0,,递给他任何东西\N{\r外文}anything through the hole.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.36,0:05:58.57,中文,,0,0,0,,天啊\N{\r外文}Jesus.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.96,0:06:22.17,中文,,0,0,0,,你知道 我自己也有点感冒了\N{\r外文}You know, I've got a little bit of a cold myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.26,0:06:25.09,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰克 我是按照欧洲人权法庭\N{\r外文}Frank, I'm here to read the articles of extradition
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.18,0:06:27.97,中文,,0,0,0,,来宣读引渡条例的\N{\r外文}according to the European Court for Human Rights.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.06,0:06:29.39,中文,,0,0,0,,"第1款\N{\r外文}"Article One,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.47,0:06:32.77,中文,,0,0,0,,"引渡是为那些犯了"\N{\r外文}"extradition shall be granted in respect of offences..."
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.85,0:06:35.52,中文,,0,0,0,,救救我\N{\r外文}Help me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.02,0:06:38.32,中文,,0,0,0,,救救我\N{\r外文}Help me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.57,0:06:42.03,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰克 别这样\N{\r外文}Frank, stop it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.61,0:06:43.91,中文,,0,0,0,,救救我\N{\r外文}Help me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.28,0:06:48.58,中文,,0,0,0,,你没想骗我 是吧\N{\r外文}You don't think you're actually going to fool me, do you?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.33,0:06:53.50,中文,,0,0,0,,还有16页没读完呢 注意听 第2款\N{\r外文}Sixteen pages to go. Stay with me. "Article Two,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.62,0:06:56.75,中文,,0,0,0,,"如果引渡请求中包含了几种 不同的罪名\N{\r外文}"if the request for extradition includes separate offences...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.83,0:07:01.01,中文,,0,0,0,,"而其中的每一项都可以根据 请求方的法律进行判罪"\N{\r外文}"...each of which is punishable under the laws of the requesting party..."
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.92,0:07:03.13,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰克\N{\r外文}Frank?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.53,0:07:06.53,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰克\N{\r外文}Frank?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.47,0:07:08.85,中文,,0,0,0,,他妈的\N{\r外文}God damn it!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.97,0:07:12.18,中文,,0,0,0,,快找名医生来 我需要名医生\N{\r外文}Get me a doctor in here! I need a doctor!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.27,0:07:14.27,中文,,0,0,0,,是的 医生 现在就要\N{\r外文}Yes. Doctor! Now!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.35,0:07:16.98,中文,,0,0,0,,别紧张 我们马上给你找医生\N{\r外文}Don't sweat it. We'll get you right to a doctor.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.48,0:07:24.95,中文,,0,0,0,,如果你能听见我 别担心 我明天早晨就带你回美国\N{\r外文}If you can hear me, don't worry. I'll take you home in the morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.03,0:07:27.20,中文,,0,0,0,,明天早晨 弗兰克\N{\r外文}Home in the morning, Frank.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.79,0:07:33.45,中文,,0,0,0,,你在做什么 洗掉虱子\N{\r外文}What are you doing? Washing off the lice.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.54,0:07:36.79,中文,,0,0,0,,这个人应该坐上去美国的飞机 他得去见医生\N{\r外文}This man has to be on a plane for America. He has to see a doctor.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.87,0:07:38.96,中文,,0,0,0,,是的 医生明天来\N{\r外文}Yes, the doctor comes in tomorrow.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.04,0:07:42.38,中文,,0,0,0,,我花费了这么大的功夫才抓住他 你就这样把他夺走\N{\r外文}I've worked too long, too hard, for you to take this away from me.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.46,0:07:45.34,中文,,0,0,0,,如果他死了 我就叫你负责\N{\r外文}If he dies, I'm holding you responsible.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.06,0:07:59.31,中文,,0,0,0,,噢 弗兰克\N{\r外文}Oh, Frank.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.86,0:08:43.36,中文,,0,0,0,,好吧 卡尔\N{\r外文}Okay, Carl,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.73,0:08:45.28,中文,,0,0,0,,我们回美国吧\N{\r外文}let's go home.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.69,0:08:51.37,中文,,0,0,0,,新罗谢尔旋转俱乐部的历史可以 追溯到1919年\N{\r外文}The New Rochelle Rotary Club has a history that goes back to 1919.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.07,0:08:53.87,中文,,0,0,0,,从那时起\N{\r外文}In all those years,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.95,0:08:57.37,中文,,0,0,0,,只有少数几位先生\N{\r外文}we've only seen a handful of deserving gentlemen
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.46,0:08:59.75,中文,,0,0,0,,被荣幸接纳为终身会员\N{\r外文}inducted as lifetime members.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.54,0:09:04.71,中文,,0,0,0,,现已有57个名字\N{\r外文}It's an honour that has seen 57 names
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.92,0:09:06.96,中文,,0,0,0,,铭记在这荣誉之墙上了\N{\r外文}enshrined on the wall of honour.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.09,0:09:09.26,中文,,0,0,0,,而今晚又加上一位\N{\r外文}And tonight, we make it 58.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.09,0:09:11.80,中文,,0,0,0,,请站起来\N{\r外文}So please stand
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.97,0:09:16.43,中文,,0,0,0,,让我来介绍我的好朋友 一个总是把我们的铅笔磨尖\N{\r外文}as I present my very good friend, a man who keeps our pencils sharp
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.93,0:09:18.77,中文,,0,0,0,,把我们的钢笔充满墨水的人\N{\r外文}and our pens in ink.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.89,0:09:21.48,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰克·威廉·阿巴戈内尔\N{\r外文}Frank William Abagnale.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.28,0:09:33.07,中文,,0,0,0,,6年之前
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.52,0:09:36.42,中文,,0,0,0,,新罗谢尔 纽约1963年
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.83,0:09:42.92,中文,,0,0,0,,我有幸\N{\r外文}I stand here, humbled
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.67,0:09:46.59,中文,,0,0,0,,与罗伯特·瓦格纳市长\N{\r外文}by the presence of Mayor Robert Wagner
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.63,0:09:53.97,中文,,0,0,0,,及我们的俱乐部主席杰克·巴恩斯 一起站在这里\N{\r外文}and our club president, Jack Barnes.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.81,0:10:02.44,中文,,0,0,0,,最想说的就是 我荣幸地看见我的太太保拉\N{\r外文}Most of all, I'm honoured to see my loving wife, Paula
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.36,0:10:08.19,中文,,0,0,0,,和我的儿子小弗兰克\N{\r外文}and my son, Frank, Jr.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.36,0:10:09.69,中文,,0,0,0,,过来吧\N{\r外文}Come on.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.53,0:10:17.79,中文,,0,0,0,,被安排在前排座位\N{\r外文}Sitting in the front row.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.37,0:10:26.04,中文,,0,0,0,,2只小老鼠掉进一个奶油桶里\N{\r外文}Two little mice fell in a bucket of cream.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.88,0:10:30.67,中文,,0,0,0,,第1只老鼠很快放弃 被淹死了\N{\r外文}The first mouse quickly gave up and drowned.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.55,0:10:33.38,中文,,0,0,0,,第2只老鼠\N{\r外文}The second mouse
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.14,0:10:35.30,中文,,0,0,0,,不肯放弃\N{\r外文}wouldn't quit.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.39,0:10:37.68,中文,,0,0,0,,它拼命努力\N{\r外文}He struggled so hard
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.81,0:10:40.98,中文,,0,0,0,,竟然最后把奶油搅拌成黄油\N{\r外文}that eventually he churned that cream into butter
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.14,0:10:42.81,中文,,0,0,0,,爬了出来\N{\r外文}and crawled out.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.23,0:10:47.06,中文,,0,0,0,,先生们 此时我就是那第2只老鼠\N{\r外文}Gentlemen, as of this moment, I am that second mouse.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.83,0:11:07.17,中文,,0,0,0,,你比你父亲跳得好\N{\r外文}You're a better dancer than your father.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.25,0:11:09.09,中文,,0,0,0,,听见了吗 爸爸 开玩笑\N{\r外文}Hear that, Daddy? Like fun.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.21,0:11:11.51,中文,,0,0,0,,女孩们不知道她们遇到什么\N{\r外文}The girls don't know what they're in for.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.59,0:11:13.92,中文,,0,0,0,,给他看看我们刚遇到时是怎样跳舞的\N{\r外文}Show him the dance you were doing when we met.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.05,0:11:15.76,中文,,0,0,0,,谁还能记得住\N{\r外文}Who can remember?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.93,0:11:20.35,中文,,0,0,0,,那个法国小村庄的人见到美国人 是那么高兴\N{\r外文}The people in that little French village were so happy to see Americans,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.43,0:11:23.02,中文,,0,0,0,,他们决定给我们表演一场\N{\r外文}they decided to put on a show for us.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.10,0:11:26.85,中文,,0,0,0,,所以挤进来200个士兵 我们知道那个故事 爸爸\N{\r外文}So they crammed 200 soldiers... We know the story, Daddy.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.94,0:11:29.02,中文,,0,0,0,,挤到那个小活动厅里\N{\r外文}...into that tiny social hall,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.11,0:11:32.19,中文,,0,0,0,,而第一个上台的就是你母亲\N{\r外文}and the first person to walk on stage is your mother
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.28,0:11:34.28,中文,,0,0,0,,她开始跳舞\N{\r外文}and she starts to dance.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.61,0:11:36.95,中文,,0,0,0,,你知道 我们自从上次见到个女人\N{\r外文}You know, it had been months
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.03,0:11:40.70,中文,,0,0,0,,已经有几个月了 而这有位金发天使\N{\r外文}since we'd seen a woman, and here's this blond angel.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.78,0:11:42.54,中文,,0,0,0,,金发美人\N{\r外文}Blond bombshell.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.58,0:11:47.46,中文,,0,0,0,,那些男人都摒住了呼吸\N{\r外文}And the men are literally holding their breath.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.58,0:11:50.59,中文,,0,0,0,,为你摒住了呼吸 你听见了吗\N{\r外文}Holding their breath for you. Hear that?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.30,0:11:54.13,中文,,0,0,0,,我转过去对我的朋友们说\N{\r外文}I turned to my buddies and I said...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.22,0:11:56.80,中文,,0,0,0,,"不得到她我决不离开法国"\N{\r外文}"I will not leave France without her."
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.93,0:11:58.39,中文,,0,0,0,,而我真没离开\N{\r外文}And I didn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.47,0:11:59.93,中文,,0,0,0,,你没离开\N{\r外文}You didn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.64,0:12:01.97,中文,,0,0,0,,我没离开\N{\r外文}I didn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.47,0:12:04.77,中文,,0,0,0,,噢 该死的 地毯\N{\r外文}Oh, shit, the rug.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.31,0:12:06.98,中文,,0,0,0,,噢 妈 我怎么\N{\r外文}Oh, Mom. I can't believe I...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.10,0:12:08.06,中文,,0,0,0,,没关系\N{\r外文}It's nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.15,0:12:10.40,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰基 快去找毛巾 好\N{\r外文}Frankie, run and get a towel. Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.48,0:12:11.77,中文,,0,0,0,,快点\N{\r外文}Come on.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.65,0:12:18.49,中文,,0,0,0,,和我跳舞 保拉\N{\r外文}Dance with me, Paula.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.29,0:12:32.29,中文,,0,0,0,,每次我为你跳舞都有麻烦\N{\r外文}Whenever I dance for you, I get in trouble.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.14,0:12:48.60,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰克 醒醒 快点 我们走吧\N{\r外文}Frank. Wake up. Come on, let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.69,0:12:50.35,中文,,0,0,0,,起来 快点\N{\r外文}Get up, come on.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.52,0:12:53.27,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰克 醒醒 爸爸\N{\r外文}Frank, wake up. Dad.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.52,0:12:55.94,中文,,0,0,0,,你今天不用去上学 没关系\N{\r外文}You don't have to go to school today. It's okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.03,0:12:59.20,中文,,0,0,0,,为什么 在下雪吗 你有没有一套黑色礼服\N{\r外文}Why? Is it snowing? Do you have a black suit?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.36,0:13:01.37,中文,,0,0,0,,我又睡过头了\N{\r外文}I overslept again.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.49,0:13:04.70,中文,,0,0,0,,我们要到城里去参加一个重要会议 吃了它\N{\r外文}We have a very important meeting in the city. Eat that.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.79,0:13:06.04,中文,,0,0,0,,快点\N{\r外文}Come on.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.20,0:13:08.79,中文,,0,0,0,,夫人 开门 很重要\N{\r外文}Ma'am, open up, please. It's important.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.87,0:13:11.46,中文,,0,0,0,,噢 是吗\N{\r外文}What? Oh, gosh.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.63,0:13:15.46,中文,,0,0,0,,还有半个小时才开门 你就开门吧 很重要\N{\r外文}We don't open for half an hour. Just open the door. It's important.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.55,0:13:17.80,中文,,0,0,0,,对不起 我们还得过半小时开门\N{\r外文}I'm sorry, we don't open for half an hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.88,0:13:19.47,中文,,0,0,0,,你叫什么名字 夫人\N{\r外文}What's your name, ma'am?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.55,0:13:22.14,中文,,0,0,0,,达茜 达茜 是个好听的名字\N{\r外文}Darcy. Darcy. That's a pretty name.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.22,0:13:24.49,中文,,0,0,0,,我有点困难 我需要给我的孩子租套衣服\N{\r外文}I'm in a fix. I need a suit for my kid.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.49,0:13:25.56,中文,,0,0,0,,这是我儿子弗兰克\N{\r外文}This is my son, Frank.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.68,0:13:27.31,中文,,0,0,0,,他需要一套黑礼服\N{\r外文}He needs a black suit.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.39,0:13:31.73,中文,,0,0,0,,我家里有人死了 我的父亲 85岁 是战争英雄\N{\r外文}There was a death in the family. My father, 85 years old, war hero.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.15,0:13:34.98,中文,,0,0,0,,下午要举行葬礼 军式葬礼\N{\r外文}There's a funeral this afternoon, military funeral,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.07,0:13:38.15,中文,,0,0,0,,飞机头上飞 21响礼炮\N{\r外文}planes flying overhead, 21-gun salute.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.40,0:13:41.49,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰克需要租套衣服用几个小时\N{\r外文}Frank needs to borrow a suit for a couple of hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.57,0:13:44.24,中文,,0,0,0,,对不起 我们不租衣服也不开门\N{\r外文}I'm sorry, we don't loan suits and we're not open.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.37,0:13:47.37,中文,,0,0,0,,达茜 求你 回来\N{\r外文}Darcy, please. Come back.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.00,0:13:50.54,中文,,0,0,0,,达茜 这是你的吗\N{\r外文}Darcy, is this yours?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.09,0:13:58.71,中文,,0,0,0,,我刚才在停车场发现的\N{\r外文}I just found it in the parking lot.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.09,0:14:03.89,中文,,0,0,0,,一定是从你的脖子上滑落的\N{\r外文}Must have slipped right off your neck.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.43,0:14:08.27,中文,,0,0,0,,别开到路缘上\N{\r外文}Don't hit the kerb.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.94,0:14:16.65,中文,,0,0,0,,现在出来 从后边绕过来 给我开门\N{\r外文}Now get out, walk around the back and hold the door open for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.04,0:14:30.12,中文,,0,0,0,,然后呢 好 不要咧嘴笑\N{\r外文}What's next? Okay. Stop grinning.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.25,0:14:33.37,中文,,0,0,0,,我进去后 你回到车前座等我\N{\r外文}When I get inside, go back to the front seat and wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.46,0:14:37.88,中文,,0,0,0,,警察来开罚单也不要挪动车 明白吗\N{\r外文}Even if a cop comes and writes you a ticket, don't move the car, understood?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.96,0:14:39.71,中文,,0,0,0,,爸 这都是为什么\N{\r外文}Dad, what's all this for?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.80,0:14:41.92,中文,,0,0,0,,你知道为什么杨基队总是赢吗\N{\r外文}You know why the Yankees always win?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.63,0:14:43.72,中文,,0,0,0,,因为他们有米基·曼托\N{\r外文}Because they have Mickey Mantle?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.80,0:14:47.72,中文,,0,0,0,,不 是因为其它队 总是盯着他们队的条纹衣服看\N{\r外文}No, it's because the other teams can't stop staring at those damn pinstripes.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.81,0:14:51.31,中文,,0,0,0,,看 美国大通银行的经理\N{\r外文}Watch this. The manager of Chase Manhattan Bank
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.89,0:14:54.81,中文,,0,0,0,,要给你父亲开门了\N{\r外文}is about to open the door for your father.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.90,0:14:58.48,中文,,0,0,0,,阿巴戈内尔先生\N{\r外文}Mr Abagnale,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.15,0:15:01.24,中文,,0,0,0,,我们一般不贷款给那些跟税务局\N{\r外文}we don't usually loan money to people
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.32,0:15:03.90,中文,,0,0,0,,还有没解决问题的人\N{\r外文}who have unresolved business with the IRS.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.99,0:15:07.16,中文,,0,0,0,,那是个误会 我用错了记账的人\N{\r外文}That's a misunderstanding. I hired the wrong guy to do my books.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.28,0:15:09.49,中文,,0,0,0,,是个任何人都可能犯的错误\N{\r外文}A mistake anybody could make.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.58,0:15:12.33,中文,,0,0,0,,我只需要你们帮助我渡过难关\N{\r外文}I just need you guys to help me weather the storm.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.45,0:15:15.33,中文,,0,0,0,,你正因骗税问题被政府调查\N{\r外文}You're being investigated by the government for tax fraud.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.46,0:15:20.17,中文,,0,0,0,,我的商店在新罗谢尔很重要 我的客户遍布纽约\N{\r外文}My store is a landmark in New Rochelle. I have customers all over New York.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.50,0:15:22.38,中文,,0,0,0,,你不是美国大通银行的客户\N{\r外文}You're not a customer at Chase Manhattan.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.46,0:15:23.59,中文,,0,0,0,,我们不认识你\N{\r外文}We don't know you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.67,0:15:26.68,中文,,0,0,0,,我确信你在新罗谢尔的银行能帮你\N{\r外文}I'm sure your bank in New Rochelle could help you out.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.76,0:15:28.35,中文,,0,0,0,,我的银行倒闭了\N{\r外文}My bank went out of business.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.43,0:15:30.68,中文,,0,0,0,,像你们这样的银行使它们倒闭的\N{\r外文}Banks like this one put them out of business.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.76,0:15:35.10,中文,,0,0,0,,我知道我犯了个错误 我承认这点 但这些人是想吸血\N{\r外文}I know I made a mistake, I admit that. But these people want blood.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.19,0:15:38.98,中文,,0,0,0,,他们想要我的商店 他们威胁过我说要把我投入监狱\N{\r外文}They want my store. They've threatened to put me in jail.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.19,0:15:42.86,中文,,0,0,0,,这是美国 对吗 我不是罪犯\N{\r外文}This is America, right? I'm not a criminal.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.94,0:15:44.19,中文,,0,0,0,,我是荣誉奖章获得者\N{\r外文}I'm a Medal of Honour winner.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.28,0:15:46.57,中文,,0,0,0,,新罗谢尔旋转俱乐部成员\N{\r外文}A member of the New Rochelle Rotary Club.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.66,0:15:50.16,中文,,0,0,0,,我想求你做的就是帮我打败这些家伙\N{\r外文}All I'm asking is for you to help me beat these guys.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.37,0:15:53.87,中文,,0,0,0,,这不是个输赢问题 是个风险问题\N{\r外文}It's not a question of winning and losing, it's a question of risk.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.87,0:15:58.38,中文,,0,0,0,,你们是世界上最大的银行 哪来\N{\r外文}You're the largest bank in the world. Where's the...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.33,0:16:01.04,中文,,0,0,0,,风险在哪里\N{\r外文}Where's the risk?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.47,0:16:08.72,中文,,0,0,0,,你怎么让他就那样把车拿走了\N{\r外文}How could you let him take our car like that?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.84,0:16:12.64,中文,,0,0,0,,他没占便宜 我们占了 他多付了500美元\N{\r外文}He didn't take anything, we took him. He overpaid by 500.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.22,0:16:16.39,中文,,0,0,0,,得了 弗兰克 我们去换衣服吧\N{\r外文}Come on, Frank. Let's return the suit.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.94,0:16:25.11,中文,,0,0,0,,已售
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.36,0:16:26.82,中文,,0,0,0,,这地方不错\N{\r外文}This place is good.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.90,0:16:30.07,中文,,0,0,0,,挺小 但活儿少多了\N{\r外文}It's small, but it's gonna be a lot less work.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.74,0:16:32.78,中文,,0,0,0,,你的活儿少多了\N{\r外文}A lot less work for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.81,0:16:57.14,中文,,0,0,0,,嘿 爸爸\N{\r外文}Hey, Dad.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.02,0:16:59.10,中文,,0,0,0,,嗨\N{\r外文}Hi.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.02,0:17:04.65,中文,,0,0,0,,你母亲呢\N{\r外文}Where is your mother?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.86,0:17:07.36,中文,,0,0,0,,我不知道\N{\r外文}I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.82,0:17:11.11,中文,,0,0,0,,她说什么要去找工作\N{\r外文}She said something about going to look for a job.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.16,0:17:15.74,中文,,0,0,0,,她能做什么 在一个蜈蚣农场卖鞋\N{\r外文}What's she going to be, a shoe salesman at a centipede farm?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.29,0:17:23.09,中文,,0,0,0,,你在做什么\N{\r外文}What are you doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.29,0:17:26.26,中文,,0,0,0,,你想要薄饼吗\N{\r外文}You want some pancakes?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.34,0:17:29.51,中文,,0,0,0,,当晚餐 在我儿子16岁生日这天\N{\r外文}For dinner? On my son's 16th birthday?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.59,0:17:32.01,中文,,0,0,0,,我们不吃薄饼\N{\r外文}We're not going to eat pancakes.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.18,0:17:38.10,中文,,0,0,0,,你为什么那样看着我 你以为我忘了\N{\r外文}Why are you looking at me like that? You thought I forgot?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.18,0:17:41.27,中文,,0,0,0,,我没以为你忘了 我开了个支票账户\N{\r外文}I didn't think you forgot. I opened a checking account
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.35,0:17:42.85,中文,,0,0,0,,以你的名义\N{\r外文}in your name.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.23,0:17:46.40,中文,,0,0,0,,账户里存了25美元 这样你就可以随便买什么\N{\r外文}I put $25 in the account so you can buy whatever you want.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.48,0:17:48.65,中文,,0,0,0,,别告诉你母亲 我不会的\N{\r外文}Don't tell your mother. I won't.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.74,0:17:50.20,中文,,0,0,0,,多谢你 爸爸\N{\r外文}Thanks, Dad.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.61,0:17:53.82,中文,,0,0,0,,那家银行不是拒绝给你贷款了吗\N{\r外文}Didn't that bank turn you down for a loan?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.91,0:17:56.20,中文,,0,0,0,,是的 他们都拒绝我了\N{\r外文}Yes, they all turned me down.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.87,0:17:58.66,中文,,0,0,0,,那怎么还在那儿开户\N{\r外文}Then why you opening a banking account with them?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.75,0:18:01.58,中文,,0,0,0,,因为将来有一天你要从他们那里 得到点什么\N{\r外文}Because one day, you'll want something from these people.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.67,0:18:03.42,中文,,0,0,0,,贷款买房子 车\N{\r外文}A house, a car...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.88,0:18:05.92,中文,,0,0,0,,他们控制所有这些钱\N{\r外文}They have all the money.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.84,0:18:12.05,中文,,0,0,0,,这有50张支票 弗兰克\N{\r外文}There's 50 cheques there, Frank,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.13,0:18:14.55,中文,,0,0,0,,也就是说 从今天开始\N{\r外文}which means, from this day on,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.93,0:18:19.18,中文,,0,0,0,,你就加入了他们的小俱乐部\N{\r外文}you're in their little club.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.68,0:18:21.77,中文,,0,0,0,,我加入了他们的小俱乐部\N{\r外文}I'm in their little club.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.39,0:18:24.69,中文,,0,0,0,,有了那个 你就有了一切\N{\r外文}You got that, you got it all.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.27,0:18:27.19,中文,,0,0,0,,上边甚至有我的名字\N{\r外文}It's even got my name there.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.07,0:18:31.07,中文,,0,0,0,,一步登天\N{\r外文}To the moon. To the moon.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.74,0:18:34.20,中文,,0,0,0,,一步登天\N{\r外文}To the moon.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.25,0:18:45.54,中文,,0,0,0,,看见了吗 那只不过是所学校\N{\r外文}See that? It's just a school.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.17,0:18:48.38,中文,,0,0,0,,和西波恩中学没什么两样\N{\r外文}No different than Westbourne.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.46,0:18:51.34,中文,,0,0,0,,妈 你说过要戒烟的\N{\r外文}Ma, you said you were going to quit.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.01,0:18:58.31,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰基 在这儿你不用穿校服\N{\r外文}Frankie, you don't have to wear the uniform here.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.43,0:19:02.02,中文,,0,0,0,,为什么不脱了你的上衣呢\N{\r外文}Why don't you take off your jacket?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.35,0:19:03.94,中文,,0,0,0,,我习惯了\N{\r外文}I'm used to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.44,0:19:10.98,中文,,0,0,0,,对不起 什么事\N{\r外文}Excuse me. Yes?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.07,0:19:14.15,中文,,0,0,0,,你知道上法语课的17号教室在哪 是的\N{\r外文}Do you know where room 17, French is? Yeah...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.79,0:19:30.50,中文,,0,0,0,,你在卖百科全书吗\N{\r外文}You selling encyclopaedias?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.59,0:19:33.17,中文,,0,0,0,,他看上去像位代课老师\N{\r外文}He looks like a substitute teacher.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.90,0:19:50.65,中文,,0,0,0,,安静 各位\N{\r外文}Quiet down, people!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.94,0:19:52.98,中文,,0,0,0,,我叫阿巴戈内尔先生\N{\r外文}My name is Mr Abagnale!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.44,0:19:56.70,中文,,0,0,0,,是阿巴戈内尔 不是阿巴戈诺勒\N{\r外文}That's Abagnale, not Abagnolee,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:56.82,0:19:59.70,中文,,0,0,0,,也不是阿巴戈内勒 而是阿巴戈内尔\N{\r外文}not Abagnelee, but Abagnale.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.83,0:20:05.08,中文,,0,0,0,,现在 请哪位来告诉我 上次讲到教材哪里了\N{\r外文}Now, somebody please tell me where you left off in your textbooks.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.79,0:20:07.75,中文,,0,0,0,,对不起 如果我需要再说一遍的话\N{\r外文}Excuse me, people. If I need to ask again,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.83,0:20:09.17,中文,,0,0,0,,我就要告你们全班的状\N{\r外文}I'm gonna write up the entire class.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.25,0:20:10.92,中文,,0,0,0,,坐下\N{\r外文}Take your seats!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.55,0:20:17.09,中文,,0,0,0,,第7章\N{\r外文}Chapter seven.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.18,0:20:19.93,中文,,0,0,0,,请打开书到第8章\N{\r外文}Would you please open your textbooks to chapter eight
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.01,0:20:21.93,中文,,0,0,0,,我们开始吧\N{\r外文}and we'll get started.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.76,0:20:24.68,中文,,0,0,0,,对不起 你叫什么 布拉德\N{\r外文}Excuse me. What's your name? Brad.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.77,0:20:26.31,中文,,0,0,0,,你为什么不站起来\N{\r外文}Why don't you get up here
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.39,0:20:30.15,中文,,0,0,0,,到全班面前 朗读第5段对话\N{\r外文}in front of the class and read conversation number five?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.91,0:20:46.58,中文,,0,0,0,,他们派我来的\N{\r外文}They sent for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.66,0:20:49.54,中文,,0,0,0,,他们说他们需要给罗伯塔找个代课老师\N{\r外文}They said they needed a sub for Roberta.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.71,0:20:52.04,中文,,0,0,0,,我老远从狄克逊赶来\N{\r外文}I came all the way from Dixon.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.38,0:20:55.38,中文,,0,0,0,,我总是给罗伯塔代课\N{\r外文}I always sub for Roberta.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.46,0:20:57.67,中文,,0,0,0,,对不起 你为什么不读了\N{\r外文}Excuse me, why aren't you reading?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.13,0:21:02.55,中文,,0,0,0,,我再也不回贝拉明·杰斐逊中学代课了\N{\r外文}I'll never come back to Bellarmine-Jefferson again!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.80,0:21:04.60,中文,,0,0,0,,你告诉他们别给我打电话\N{\r外文}You tell them not to call me.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.68,0:21:07.06,中文,,0,0,0,,他们认为像我这样一把年纪的妇女\N{\r外文}Do they think it's easy for a woman my age
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.14,0:21:10.77,中文,,0,0,0,,还花了我那么多路费容易吗 他们什么都不给\N{\r外文}and all the money that it costs to travel? I tell you, they don't give a damn.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.85,0:21:12.44,中文,,0,0,0,,阿巴戈内尔先生 太太\N{\r外文}Mr and Mrs Abagnale,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.52,0:21:15.32,中文,,0,0,0,,这不是你们儿子的缺课问题\N{\r外文}this is not a question of your son's attendance.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.40,0:21:18.40,中文,,0,0,0,,我遗憾地告诉你们上一周\N{\r外文}I regret to inform you that for the past week,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.49,0:21:22.07,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰克在教格拉瑟太太的法语课\N{\r外文}Frank has been teaching Mrs Glasser's French class.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:23.95,0:21:25.24,中文,,0,0,0,,他什么\N{\r外文}He what?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.70,0:21:29.50,中文,,0,0,0,,你们的儿子假装成代课老师\N{\r外文}Your son has been pretending to be a substitute teacher.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.75,0:21:33.17,中文,,0,0,0,,给学生们讲课 布置作业\N{\r外文}Lecturing the students, giving out homework...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.67,0:21:35.84,中文,,0,0,0,,格拉瑟太太病了\N{\r外文}Mrs Glasser has been ill,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.92,0:21:39.09,中文,,0,0,0,,而真的代课老师无法上课\N{\r外文}and there was some confusion with the real sub.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.13,0:21:43.18,中文,,0,0,0,,昨天你们的儿子开了个家长会\N{\r外文}Your son held a teacher-parent conference yesterday
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.26,0:21:45.60,中文,,0,0,0,,准备安排实习\N{\r外文}and was planning a class field trip
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.68,0:21:48.39,中文,,0,0,0,,到特伦顿的一家法国面包厂\N{\r外文}to a French bread factory in Trenton.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.43,0:21:51.81,中文,,0,0,0,,你们明白了我们的问题吗\N{\r外文}Do you see the problem we have?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.69,0:21:57.73,中文,,0,0,0,,我有个假条 不能上第5 6节课 跟大夫有约\N{\r外文}I've a note to miss fifth and sixth period today. Doctor's appointment.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.82,0:22:00.40,中文,,0,0,0,,稍等一下 我马上回来\N{\r外文}One moment. I'll be right with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.86,0:22:05.28,中文,,0,0,0,,你应该折起来 什么\N{\r外文}You should fold it. What?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:05.87,0:22:08.83,中文,,0,0,0,,那个假条 是假的 对吗 你应该折起来\N{\r外文}That note. It's a fake, right? You should fold it.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:08.91,0:22:11.71,中文,,0,0,0,,是我妈妈写的假条 我跟医生有约\N{\r外文}It's a note from my mom. I have a doctor's appointment.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:11.79,0:22:14.63,中文,,0,0,0,,对 但纸没有折痕\N{\r外文}Yeah, but there's no crease in the paper.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:14.71,0:22:16.55,中文,,0,0,0,,你妈妈递给你请假的假条时\N{\r外文}When your mom hands you a note to miss school,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:16.63,0:22:20.55,中文,,0,0,0,,一般人首先折起来 再放进口袋里\N{\r外文}the first thing you do is fold it and put it in your pocket.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:20.63,0:22:23.13,中文,,0,0,0,,如果是真的 折痕在哪里\N{\r外文}If it's real, where's the crease?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:32.89,0:22:34.19,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰基\N{\r外文}Frankie.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:50.08,0:22:51.58,中文,,0,0,0,,妈 我回来了\N{\r外文}Ma, I'm home.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:54.54,0:22:57.88,中文,,0,0,0,,还记得我跟你谈过的那个女孩 乔安娜吗\N{\r外文}Remember that girl Joanna I was telling you about?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:58.25,0:23:00.17,中文,,0,0,0,,今天我跟她约会了\N{\r外文}I asked her out today.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:01.34,0:23:04.34,中文,,0,0,0,,我想我们要去参加3年级舞会\N{\r外文}Think we're going to go to the junior prom.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:05.43,0:23:07.85,中文,,0,0,0,,妈 这是我的驾驶执照吗\N{\r外文}Ma, is this my driver's licence?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:07.93,0:23:10.47,中文,,0,0,0,,只有这些 2间卧室\N{\r外文}That's all there is, two bedrooms.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:10.60,0:23:11.89,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰基\N{\r外文}Frankie.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:12.02,0:23:14.14,中文,,0,0,0,,你还记得爸爸的朋友吗\N{\r外文}You remember Dad's friend?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:14.56,0:23:16.86,中文,,0,0,0,,杰克·巴恩斯 俱乐部的\N{\r外文}Jack Barnes. From the club.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:17.15,0:23:18.11,中文,,0,0,0,,你好\N{\r外文}Hello.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:18.19,0:23:20.40,中文,,0,0,0,,他路过这里来找你父亲\N{\r外文}He came by looking for your father.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:20.48,0:23:23.03,中文,,0,0,0,,我带他看了房子\N{\r外文}I was giving him a tour of the apartment.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:23.11,0:23:26.03,中文,,0,0,0,,很宽敞 保拉\N{\r外文}It's very spacious, Paula.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:31.83,0:23:33.66,中文,,0,0,0,,爸爸在商店\N{\r外文}Dad is at the store.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:34.41,0:23:35.87,中文,,0,0,0,,那么 弗兰克\N{\r外文}So, Frank,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:36.75,0:23:40.42,中文,,0,0,0,,你长得越来越像你父亲了\N{\r外文}you're getting to look more like your old man every day.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:42.38,0:23:44.76,中文,,0,0,0,,谢谢你的三明治 保拉\N{\r外文}Thanks for the sandwich, Paula.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:45.68,0:23:47.80,中文,,0,0,0,,再见 等一下\N{\r外文}I'll see you later. Wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:53.31,0:23:54.85,中文,,0,0,0,,这是你的吗\N{\r外文}Is this yours?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:57.73,0:24:00.69,中文,,0,0,0,,谢谢 弗兰克 这是主席别针\N{\r外文}Thanks, Frank. That's the President's pin.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:02.07,0:24:04.82,中文,,0,0,0,,我要是丢了它 麻烦可就大了\N{\r外文}I'd be in deep trouble if I lost that.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:10.58,0:24:12.58,中文,,0,0,0,,再见\N{\r外文}I'll see you all later.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:22.38,0:24:25.72,中文,,0,0,0,,你饿了吗 弗兰基 我给你做三明治\N{\r外文}Are you hungry, Frankie? I'll make you a sandwich.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:34.68,0:24:37.81,中文,,0,0,0,,杰克想跟你父亲谈生意\N{\r外文}Jack wanted to talk business with your father.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:39.02,0:24:42.69,中文,,0,0,0,,他觉得我们应该找个律师控告政府\N{\r外文}He thinks we should get a lawyer and sue the government.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:43.48,0:24:46.65,中文,,0,0,0,,他们对我们做的不合法\N{\r外文}That it's not legal, what they're doing to us.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:49.49,0:24:51.87,中文,,0,0,0,,你怎么不说话\N{\r外文}Why aren't you saying anything?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:58.12,0:25:01.08,中文,,0,0,0,,你不会告诉他的 是吗\N{\r外文}You're not going to tell him, are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:02.63,0:25:03.71,中文,,0,0,0,,不会\N{\r外文}No.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:04.59,0:25:07.34,中文,,0,0,0,,那就对了 没有什么可说的\N{\r外文}That's right. There's nothing to tell.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:08.59,0:25:13.05,中文,,0,0,0,,我要出去几个小时 拜访一些网球俱乐部的朋友\N{\r外文}I'm going out for a few hours to visit some old friends from the tennis club.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:13.14,0:25:16.39,中文,,0,0,0,,我回家后 我们一起吃晚饭\N{\r外文}When I get home, we'll all have dinner together.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:16.73,0:25:17.98,中文,,0,0,0,,好吗\N{\r外文}Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:18.94,0:25:22.44,中文,,0,0,0,,你什么也不会说 因为那样太傻\N{\r外文}But you won't say anything because it's just silly,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:22.56,0:25:23.90,中文,,0,0,0,,对吗\N{\r外文}isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:24.40,0:25:26.48,中文,,0,0,0,,我们怎么能控告政府\N{\r外文}How could we sue anybody?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:32.20,0:25:34.62,中文,,0,0,0,,你需要点钱吗 弗兰基\N{\r外文}Do you need some money, Frankie?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:35.04,0:25:38.12,中文,,0,0,0,,要几美元去买几张唱片\N{\r外文}A few dollars to buy some record albums?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:38.46,0:25:40.58,中文,,0,0,0,,给你 拿着5美元\N{\r外文}Here. Take $5.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:42.25,0:25:43.46,中文,,0,0,0,,或10美元\N{\r外文}Or 10.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:49.34,0:25:51.97,中文,,0,0,0,,你答应过要戒掉的\N{\r外文}You promised you were going to quit.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:10.99,0:26:12.49,中文,,0,0,0,,妈 我回来了\N{\r外文}Ma, I'm home.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:28.76,0:26:30.55,中文,,0,0,0,,你离我远点 听见了吗\N{\r外文}You stay away from me. You hear me?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:30.63,0:26:33.34,中文,,0,0,0,,我不知道你是谁 但如果你回来\N{\r外文}I don't know who you are, but if you come back here...
Dialogue: 0,0:26:33.43,0:26:36.43,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰克 冷静点 好吗 我叫迪克·科斯纳\N{\r外文}Frank, calm down, will you? I'm Dick Kesner.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:37.43,0:26:40.89,中文,,0,0,0,,我想让你把东西放这 跟我进另一间屋\N{\r外文}I want you to leave your things here, follow me into the next room.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:40.98,0:26:43.52,中文,,0,0,0,,他们都在等你\N{\r外文}Okay? They're all waiting for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:45.77,0:26:48.40,中文,,0,0,0,,你不必害怕 我就在这里 弗兰克\N{\r外文}You don't have to be scared. I'm right here, Frank.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:48.48,0:26:50.28,中文,,0,0,0,,我一直在这里\N{\r外文}I'll always be here.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:50.36,0:26:54.45,中文,,0,0,0,,但是有法律 这个国家的每一件事 都要合法\N{\r外文}But there are laws. Everything in this country has to be legal.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:54.53,0:26:57.28,中文,,0,0,0,,所以我们要做些决定\N{\r外文}So what we need to do is make some decisions.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:57.37,0:26:58.83,中文,,0,0,0,,科斯纳先生就是为这个来的\N{\r外文}That's what Mr Kesner is here for.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:58.91,0:27:01.62,中文,,0,0,0,,很多时候这些决定是由法庭来做的\N{\r外文}Many times these decisions are left up to the courts.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:01.70,0:27:04.75,中文,,0,0,0,,但可能会很贵 人们为了孩子而打架\N{\r外文}But that can be very expensive, people fighting over their children.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:04.83,0:27:06.08,中文,,0,0,0,,没人在打架\N{\r外文}Nobody is fighting.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:06.17,0:27:08.92,中文,,0,0,0,,看着我 弗兰克 没人在打架\N{\r外文}Look at me, Frank. Nobody is fighting.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:17.68,0:27:21.60,中文,,0,0,0,,还记得你的祖母吗 夏娃 她今天早晨到的\N{\r外文}Do you remember your grandma? Eve? She arrived this morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:22.35,0:27:23.56,中文,,0,0,0,,你好\N{\r外文}Hello.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:32.78,0:27:36.11,中文,,0,0,0,,你明白我们在跟你讲什么吗 弗兰克\N{\r外文}Do you understand what we're saying to you, Frank?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:37.41,0:27:40.66,中文,,0,0,0,,我和你父亲要离婚了\N{\r外文}Your father and I are getting a divorce.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:44.00,0:27:46.71,中文,,0,0,0,,什么都不会改变 我们还可以见面\N{\r外文}Nothing's going to change. We're still gonna see each other.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:46.79,0:27:50.38,中文,,0,0,0,,别说了 求你 不要打断 你不必全读这些\N{\r外文}Stop it, please. Don't interrupt. You don't have to read all of this.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:50.46,0:27:53.21,中文,,0,0,0,,多数都是关于你父母的 枯燥的成人事情\N{\r外文}Most of it is for your parents, boring adult business.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:53.30,0:27:55.93,中文,,0,0,0,,但这段很重要\N{\r外文}But this paragraph right here, this is important
Dialogue: 0,0:27:56.01,0:27:59.18,中文,,0,0,0,,因为它说的是离婚后你将跟谁\N{\r外文}because it states who you're gonna live with
Dialogue: 0,0:28:00.31,0:28:01.76,中文,,0,0,0,,在一起\N{\r外文}after the divorce.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:01.85,0:28:03.73,中文,,0,0,0,,你受谁的监护\N{\r外文}Whose custody you will be in.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:03.81,0:28:06.52,中文,,0,0,0,,这里有个空白处\N{\r外文}And there's a blank space right here.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:07.81,0:28:11.15,中文,,0,0,0,,我想让你到厨房去 坐在桌前\N{\r外文}I want you to go into the kitchen, sit at the table
Dialogue: 0,0:28:11.23,0:28:12.73,中文,,0,0,0,,写上一个人名\N{\r外文}and put a name down.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:12.82,0:28:13.99,中文,,0,0,0,,不要着急\N{\r外文}You can take as long as you want,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:14.07,0:28:15.61,中文,,0,0,0,,但是当你回到这个房间时\N{\r外文}but when you come back into this room,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:15.70,0:28:18.20,中文,,0,0,0,,我想看见那条线上写好了名字\N{\r外文}I want to see a name on that line.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:18.28,0:28:22.12,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰克 你只要写下个人名 所有这些就都结束了\N{\r外文}Frank, just write down a name and this will all be over.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:22.33,0:28:23.87,中文,,0,0,0,,不会有事的\N{\r外文}It's going to be okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:23.95,0:28:25.62,中文,,0,0,0,,爸 什么名字\N{\r外文}Dad, what name?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:25.71,0:28:27.00,中文,,0,0,0,,你母亲或你父亲\N{\r外文}Your mother or your father.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:27.08,0:28:29.96,中文,,0,0,0,,把名字写在那里 就那么简单\N{\r外文}Just put the name there. It's as simple as that.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:30.04,0:28:33.25,中文,,0,0,0,,不要害怕 这不是考试\N{\r外文}And don't look so scared. It's not a test.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:34.01,0:28:36.09,中文,,0,0,0,,没有错误的回答\N{\r外文}There's no wrong answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:50.77,0:28:52.65,中文,,0,0,0,,请给1张到大中心的票\N{\r外文}One ticket to Grand Central, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:52.73,0:28:54.78,中文,,0,0,0,,3.50美元 先生\N{\r外文}That will be $3.50, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:56.03,0:28:58.57,中文,,0,0,0,,我付支票可以吗\N{\r外文}Is it okay if I write you a cheque?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:03.79,0:29:06.20,中文,,0,0,0,,卡尔 我何时可以给我父亲打电话\N{\r外文}Carl, when do I get to call my father?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:06.58,0:29:09.25,中文,,0,0,0,,到纽约后你可以打电话给他\N{\r外文}You can call him when we get to New York.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:09.33,0:29:11.50,中文,,0,0,0,,我们7个小时后到飞机场\N{\r外文}We leave for the airport in seven hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:11.60,0:29:12.95,中文,,0,0,0,,1969年巴黎
Dialogue: 0,0:29:12.96,0:29:15.13,中文,,0,0,0,,别动,一直坐在那里\N{\r外文}Until then, just sit there.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:15.30,0:29:16.63,中文,,0,0,0,,安静点\N{\r外文}Be quiet.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:17.72,0:29:21.51,中文,,0,0,0,,旅馆的另外一侧有面对公园的房间\N{\r外文}On the other side of the hotel, they got suites that face the park.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:22.89,0:29:25.64,中文,,0,0,0,,这是联邦调查局能担负的最好的房间了\N{\r外文}It's the best room the F.B.I. can afford.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:28.48,0:29:30.90,中文,,0,0,0,,没关系 我原来待的地方更差\N{\r外文}It's okay, I've stayed in worse.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:31.60,0:29:33.31,中文,,0,0,0,,求你 你得听我说\N{\r外文}Please. You have to listen.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:33.40,0:29:36.73,中文,,0,0,0,,我不想听你解释 2张支票退回来了\N{\r外文}I don't want to hear your story. Two cheques bounced.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:36.82,0:29:38.61,中文,,0,0,0,,你知道我有多大的麻烦吗\N{\r外文}You know how much trouble I'm in?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:38.70,0:29:41.20,中文,,0,0,0,,银行搞错了\N{\r外文}No, but listen. I'm telling you. The bank, they made the mistake.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:41.28,0:29:42.91,中文,,0,0,0,,我马上再给你写张支票\N{\r外文}I'll write you another cheque right now!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:42.99,0:29:45.03,中文,,0,0,0,,我看上去像小孩子那么好骗吗\N{\r外文}What? Do I look like I was born yesterday?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:45.12,0:29:48.00,中文,,0,0,0,,你看 现在是半夜 我上哪里去\N{\r外文}Look, it's midnight. Where am I going to go?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:48.08,0:29:50.42,中文,,0,0,0,,你是个该死的孩子 回家去\N{\r外文}You're a goddamn kid. Go home.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:13.98,0:30:19.44,中文,,0,0,0,,阿巴戈内尔 弗兰克
Dialogue: 0,0:30:27.79,0:30:30.67,中文,,0,0,0,,乔治·泰勒 由乔治·泰勒授权
Dialogue: 0,0:30:32.04,0:30:35.55,中文,,0,0,0,,小弗兰克·泰勒
Dialogue: 0,0:30:38.63,0:30:42.18,中文,,0,0,0,,我希望你明白 我的老板派我到布鲁克林区 然后到皇后区\N{\r外文}I hope you understand. My boss sent me to Brooklyn, then Queens.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:42.26,0:30:43.72,中文,,0,0,0,,现在他想让我去长岛\N{\r外文}Now he wants me in Long Island
Dialogue: 0,0:30:43.80,0:30:46.60,中文,,0,0,0,,带些顾客来城里玩一晚上\N{\r外文}to take a few clients out for a night on the town.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:46.68,0:30:50.60,中文,,0,0,0,,对不起 我不能给其它银行的支票 兑付现金\N{\r外文}I'm sorry, but we're not allowed to cash cheques from other banks.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:50.68,0:30:53.60,中文,,0,0,0,,你怎么能知道它们是有效的呢 你说你叫什么名字来着\N{\r外文}How would we know if they were good? What did you say your name was?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:53.69,0:30:55.40,中文,,0,0,0,,阿什蕾\N{\r外文}Ashley. Ashley.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:55.48,0:30:58.73,中文,,0,0,0,,你知道我在外边人行道上发现什么了吗\N{\r外文}You know what I found on the sidewalk out there?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:03.65,0:31:06.41,中文,,0,0,0,,一定是从你脖子上滑落的\N{\r外文}Must have slipped right off your neck.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:10.54,0:31:13.58,中文,,0,0,0,,有什么需要我帮助吗 年轻人\N{\r外文}Is there something I can help you with, son?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:13.66,0:31:15.96,中文,,0,0,0,,下星期是我祖母的生日\N{\r外文}It's my grandmother's birthday next week
Dialogue: 0,0:31:16.04,0:31:18.67,中文,,0,0,0,,我想送给她件什么特别的东西\N{\r外文}and I want to get her something extra special.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:18.75,0:31:22.59,中文,,0,0,0,,求你了 我下星期期中考试 而书却丢了\N{\r外文}Please, it's my midterm next week and my books were stolen.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:24.34,0:31:27.01,中文,,0,0,0,,求你 只是5美元 没人会知道的\N{\r外文}Please, just $5. No one would have to know.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:27.10,0:31:30.47,中文,,0,0,0,,对不起 但我们不许收\N{\r外文}I'm sorry, but we are not allowed to take cheques
Dialogue: 0,0:31:30.56,0:31:32.68,中文,,0,0,0,,不认识的人的支票\N{\r外文}from people we don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:55.67,0:31:57.50,中文,,0,0,0,,欢迎来到纽约\N{\r外文}Welcome to New York.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:14.23,0:32:16.06,中文,,0,0,0,,很高兴你回来了 机长\N{\r外文}Pleasure to have you back, Captain.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:16.19,0:32:20.27,中文,,0,0,0,,怎么样 安吉洛 番茄今天下午熟了\N{\r外文}What do you think, Angelo? The tomatoes are ripe this afternoon.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:27.57,0:32:28.70,中文,,0,0,0,,这是什么\N{\r外文}What have we here?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:28.78,0:32:30.87,中文,,0,0,0,,能签个名吗 肯定行\N{\r外文}Can I have your autograph? You betcha.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:30.95,0:32:34.54,中文,,0,0,0,,也能给我签名吗 你将来当飞行员\N{\r外文}Can I have your autograph, too? You gonna be a pilot?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:35.04,0:32:36.79,中文,,0,0,0,,好了 好好学习\N{\r外文}There you go. Work hard in school.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:36.87,0:32:38.21,中文,,0,0,0,,亲爱的爸爸\N{\r外文}Dear Dad,
Dialogue: 0,0:32:38.29,0:32:40.79,中文,,0,0,0,,我已经决定去当飞行员\N{\r外文}I've decided to become an airline pilot.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:40.88,0:32:42.71,中文,,0,0,0,,我已经申请了所有的大航空公司\N{\r外文}I've applied to all the big airlines,
Dialogue: 0,0:32:42.80,0:32:45.88,中文,,0,0,0,,有希望的面试已经排满日程了\N{\r外文}and I have several promising interviews lined up.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:46.22,0:32:49.05,中文,,0,0,0,,妈妈怎样 你最近给她打电话了吗\N{\r外文}How is Mom? Have you called her lately?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:49.14,0:32:51.72,中文,,0,0,0,,爱你的 儿子 弗兰克\N{\r外文}Love, your son, Frank.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:52.01,0:32:55.02,中文,,0,0,0,,泛美航空公司
Dialogue: 0,0:32:55.39,0:32:56.60,中文,,0,0,0,,你好\N{\r外文}Hello.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:57.39,0:32:59.48,中文,,0,0,0,,我是穆偌中学的弗兰克·布莱克\N{\r外文}I'm Frank Black from Murrow High School,
Dialogue: 0,0:32:59.56,0:33:02.27,中文,,0,0,0,,我跟摩根先生有个约会\N{\r外文}and I have an appointment with Mr Morgan.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:02.40,0:33:05.15,中文,,0,0,0,,你给学校的报纸写文章\N{\r外文}You're the young man who's writing the article for the school paper.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:05.23,0:33:06.24,中文,,0,0,0,,对 是我\N{\r外文}Yes, ma'am. That's me.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:06.32,0:33:08.74,中文,,0,0,0,,我想知道关于成为飞行员的每一件事\N{\r外文}I want to know everything there is to know about being a pilot.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:09.57,0:33:13.08,中文,,0,0,0,,泛美公司都飞哪些飞机场 飞行员1年收入多少\N{\r外文}What airports does Pan Am fly to? What does a pilot make in a year?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:13.16,0:33:14.87,中文,,0,0,0,,谁告诉他们往哪儿飞\N{\r外文}Who tells them where they're gonna fly to?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:14.95,0:33:17.16,中文,,0,0,0,,慢一点 一个一个来 好的\N{\r外文}Slow down. Take them one at a time. All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:17.25,0:33:20.00,中文,,0,0,0,,飞行员这样说是什么意思\N{\r外文}What does it mean when one pilot says to another pilot,
Dialogue: 0,0:33:20.08,0:33:21.25,中文,,0,0,0,,"你装配了些什么"\N{\r外文}"What kind of equipment are you on?"
Dialogue: 0,0:33:21.33,0:33:23.25,中文,,0,0,0,,他们想知道你们使用什么样的飞机\N{\r外文}They want to know what aircraft you're flying.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:23.25,0:33:25.17,中文,,0,0,0,,DC-8 707 星座式\N{\r外文}DC-8, 707, Constellation...
Dialogue: 0,0:33:25.25,0:33:28.26,中文,,0,0,0,,还有那些我见过的飞行员戴的身份徽章怎样\N{\r外文}And what about those I.D. badges that I've seen pilots wear?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:28.34,0:33:30.68,中文,,0,0,0,,每个飞行员必须随时随身携带两样东西\N{\r外文}Every pilot must have two things with him at all times.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:30.76,0:33:34.26,中文,,0,0,0,,一个是航空公司的职员徽章 就像泛美航空公司的这个\N{\r外文}One is his airline personnel badge, looks just like this one from Pan Am.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:34.35,0:33:36.93,中文,,0,0,0,,另一个就是联邦航空局的执照\N{\r外文}The other one is their FAA licence.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:37.18,0:33:39.52,中文,,0,0,0,,就像这个一样\N{\r外文}And that looks just like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:42.44,0:33:45.07,中文,,0,0,0,,我能复印1份贴在我的文章里吗\N{\r外文}Do you think I could make a copy of this to put into my article?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:45.15,0:33:48.28,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰克 你可以把那个拿去 还有3年过期\N{\r外文}Frank, you can have that one, it's three years expired.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:48.36,0:33:50.45,中文,,0,0,0,,谢谢 还有你的身份徽章呢\N{\r外文}Thanks. And what about your I.D. badge?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:50.53,0:33:51.82,中文,,0,0,0,,你还有没有一个多余的借给我\N{\r外文}Do you have an extra one I could borrow?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:51.95,0:33:53.45,中文,,0,0,0,,那个我帮不了你\N{\r外文}No, I can't help you there.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:53.53,0:33:55.03,中文,,0,0,0,,要从宝丽来公司定制\N{\r外文}Those are special-ordered from Polaroid.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:55.12,0:33:57.95,中文,,0,0,0,,唯一弄到它的办法就是成为一名真的\N{\r外文}The only way to get one is to become a real live pilot
Dialogue: 0,0:33:58.04,0:33:59.50,中文,,0,0,0,,泛美公司的飞行员\N{\r外文}for Pan American Airways.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:59.79,0:34:02.04,中文,,0,0,0,,泛美航空公司
Dialogue: 0,0:34:04.50,0:34:06.21,中文,,0,0,0,,泛美公司 要我帮忙吗\N{\r外文}Pan Am, may I help you?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:06.30,0:34:08.63,中文,,0,0,0,,是的 我打电话是为了一套制服\N{\r外文}Yeah. Hello, I'm calling about a uniform.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:08.71,0:34:10.97,中文,,0,0,0,,等我转到采购部 谢谢\N{\r外文}Hold for Purchasing. Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:11.05,0:34:12.26,中文,,0,0,0,,采购部\N{\r外文}Purchasing.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:12.34,0:34:15.01,中文,,0,0,0,,我是旧金山基地的副驾驶员\N{\r外文}I'm a copilot based out of San Francisco.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:15.14,0:34:17.27,中文,,0,0,0,,我昨晚飞到纽约\N{\r外文}I flew a flight into New York last night,
Dialogue: 0,0:34:17.35,0:34:20.64,中文,,0,0,0,,但3小时后要飞巴黎\N{\r外文}but the problem is I'm headed out to Paris in three hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:20.73,0:34:22.40,中文,,0,0,0,,您需要什么帮助\N{\r外文}How can we help you?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:22.48,0:34:25.98,中文,,0,0,0,,我把制服送给旅馆清洗\N{\r外文}I sent my uniform to be cleaned through the hotel
Dialogue: 0,0:34:26.19,0:34:28.03,中文,,0,0,0,,但我想他们把它给弄丢了\N{\r外文}and I guess they must have lost it.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:28.15,0:34:30.44,中文,,0,0,0,,他们丢了制服 这事经常发生\N{\r外文}They lost a uniform. Happens all the time.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:30.53,0:34:33.49,中文,,0,0,0,,去好工制服公司\N{\r外文}Go down to the Well-Built Uniform Company at 9th and Broadway.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:33.57,0:34:34.66,中文,,0,0,0,,他们是我们的制服提供商\N{\r外文}They're our uniform supplier.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:34.74,0:34:36.74,中文,,0,0,0,,我告诉罗森先生你要来\N{\r外文}I'll tell Mr Rosen you're coming.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:36.83,0:34:38.79,中文,,0,0,0,,你看上去当飞行员太年轻了\N{\r外文}You look too young to be a pilot.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:38.87,0:34:40.50,中文,,0,0,0,,我是副驾驶员\N{\r外文}I'm a copilot.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:40.83,0:34:42.37,中文,,0,0,0,,为什么这么紧张\N{\r外文}Why so nervous?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:42.83,0:34:47.04,中文,,0,0,0,,你第一周刚上班就把制服丢了 会感觉怎样\N{\r外文}How would you feel if you lost your uniform first week on the job?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:47.17,0:34:50.17,中文,,0,0,0,,放松点 泛美公司有的是制服\N{\r外文}Relax. Pan Am has got lots of uniforms.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:50.84,0:34:52.51,中文,,0,0,0,,一共是164美元\N{\r外文}It's gonna be $164.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:53.38,0:34:55.51,中文,,0,0,0,,很好 我给你写张支票\N{\r外文}Great. I'll write you a cheque.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:55.60,0:34:57.72,中文,,0,0,0,,对不起 不收支票 不收现金\N{\r外文}Sorry, no checks, no cash.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:57.85,0:35:00.31,中文,,0,0,0,,你得写下你的职员身份号码\N{\r外文}You'll have to fill in your employee I.D. number.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:00.39,0:35:04.52,中文,,0,0,0,,我向泛美公司收帐 然后他们再从你下次薪水中扣除\N{\r外文}I'll bill Pan Am, and they'll take it out of your next paycheck.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:05.86,0:35:07.02,中文,,0,0,0,,那更好\N{\r外文}Even better.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:09.19,0:35:10.40,中文,,0,0,0,,亲爱的爸爸\N{\r外文}Dear Dad,
Dialogue: 0,0:35:10.53,0:35:13.57,中文,,0,0,0,,你总是告诉我一个诚实的人 没有什么可害怕的\N{\r外文}you always told me that an honest man has nothing to fear.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:13.70,0:35:16.53,中文,,0,0,0,,所以我尽量不去害怕\N{\r外文}So I'm trying my best not to be afraid.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:16.70,0:35:19.74,中文,,0,0,0,,对不起我离家出走了 但你不用担心\N{\r外文}I'm sorry I ran away, but you don't have to worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:19.87,0:35:24.21,中文,,0,0,0,,我现在要把这些都找回来 爸爸 我承诺 我要都找回来\N{\r外文}I'm gonna get it all back now, Daddy. I promise. I'm gonna get it all back.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:30.92,0:35:32.55,中文,,0,0,0,,你是真的飞行员吗\N{\r外文}Are you a real live pilot?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:32.63,0:35:34.88,中文,,0,0,0,,我肯定是 小姐 你叫什么名字\N{\r外文}I sure am, little lady. What's your name?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:34.97,0:35:37.64,中文,,0,0,0,,席琳 很高兴认识你\N{\r外文}Celine. Celine, it's a pleasure to meet you.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:37.72,0:35:40.14,中文,,0,0,0,,我也很高兴认识你\N{\r外文}It's a pleasure to meet you, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:43.93,0:35:48.31,中文,,0,0,0,,这是50 70 80 90美元\N{\r外文}That's 50, 70, 80, 90,
Dialogue: 0,0:35:48.40,0:35:50.15,中文,,0,0,0,,100美元\N{\r外文}$100.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:50.23,0:35:52.53,中文,,0,0,0,,祝你在巴黎过得愉快\N{\r外文}You have yourself a great time in Paris.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:52.61,0:35:54.07,中文,,0,0,0,,我总是过得愉快\N{\r外文}I always do.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:54.65,0:35:56.07,中文,,0,0,0,,对不起\N{\r外文}Excuse me.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:57.41,0:35:59.41,中文,,0,0,0,,我叫约翰·摩迪治 我管理这家分行\N{\r外文}I'm John Modiger. I manage this branch.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:59.49,0:36:01.70,中文,,0,0,0,,谢谢你使用我们的银行\N{\r外文}I want to thank you for coming in and using our institution.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:01.79,0:36:04.96,中文,,0,0,0,,幸会 我会再回来的 好\N{\r外文}It's a pleasure to meet you, John. I'll be back again. Good.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:05.16,0:36:07.58,中文,,0,0,0,,你以前和我们在一起了吗\N{\r外文}Have you stayed with us before?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:07.92,0:36:11.17,中文,,0,0,0,,不 我以前主要是在西海岸一带\N{\r外文}No, I've been primarily based on the West Coast.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:11.75,0:36:13.67,中文,,0,0,0,,我可以给你写张支票付房钱吗\N{\r外文}Is it all right if I write you a cheque for the room?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:13.76,0:36:15.80,中文,,0,0,0,,没问题 先生 很好\N{\r外文}No problem, sir. Great.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:25.18,0:36:28.44,中文,,0,0,0,,我刚才还在疑虑是否能给你写张 个人支票\N{\r外文}I was also wondering if I could write you a personal cheque?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:28.52,0:36:29.62,中文,,0,0,0,,对于航空公司的职员\N{\r外文}For airline personnel,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:29.62,0:36:31.73,中文,,0,0,0,,我们最多给个人支票兑现100美元现金\N{\r外文}we cash personal cheques up to $100.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:31.82,0:36:33.48,中文,,0,0,0,,薪水支票我们最多兑现300美元现金\N{\r外文}Payroll cheques we cash up to 300.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:35.11,0:36:37.78,中文,,0,0,0,,你是说工资支票给兑现300美元\N{\r外文}Did you say 300 for a payroll cheque?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:42.70,0:36:44.16,中文,,0,0,0,,亲爱的爸爸\N{\r外文}Dear Dad,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:44.37,0:36:47.75,中文,,0,0,0,,我已经决定要成为泛美航空公司的飞行员了\N{\r外文}I've decided to become a pilot for Pan American Airways,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:47.83,0:36:50.25,中文,,0,0,0,,泛美是天空中最值得信任的名字\N{\r外文}the most trusted name in the skies.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:50.33,0:36:54.55,中文,,0,0,0,,他们已经接受我参加他们的培训 并说如果我努力工作\N{\r外文}They've accepted me into their training programme and told me if I work hard,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:54.63,0:36:56.88,中文,,0,0,0,,不久我就真要插上翅膀了\N{\r外文}I should earn my wings real soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:56.97,0:37:00.09,中文,,0,0,0,,请跟10年级的乔安娜·卡尔顿联系\N{\r外文}Please get in touch with Joanna Carlton from the 10th grade.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:00.18,0:37:03.31,中文,,0,0,0,,告诉他 说我抱歉不能带她去3年级舞会\N{\r外文}Tell her I'm sorry that I could not take her to the junior prom.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:03.39,0:37:05.68,中文,,0,0,0,,爱你的 儿子 弗兰克\N{\r外文}Love, your son, Frank.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:44.26,0:37:46.43,中文,,0,0,0,,你好吗 很好 谢谢\N{\r外文}Hello, how are you? Fine, thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:46.52,0:37:48.64,中文,,0,0,0,,我有1张薪水支票想兑现金\N{\r外文}I have a payroll cheque I'd like to cash.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:48.73,0:37:50.19,中文,,0,0,0,,当然了\N{\r外文}Certainly.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:51.90,0:37:53.27,中文,,0,0,0,,对不起\N{\r外文}Excuse me.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:54.02,0:37:56.03,中文,,0,0,0,,我肯定你经常听人这么说\N{\r外文}I'm sure you hear this all the time,
Dialogue: 0,0:37:56.11,0:37:59.70,中文,,0,0,0,,但你的眼睛是我见过的最美丽的一双\N{\r外文}but you have the most beautiful eyes I have ever seen.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:00.45,0:38:02.95,中文,,0,0,0,,是 我经常听人这么说\N{\r外文}Yeah, I do get that all the time.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:03.87,0:38:05.37,中文,,0,0,0,,你喜欢它吗\N{\r外文}How would you like it?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:20.97,0:38:25.26,中文,,0,0,0,,对不起 先生 我们要等银行 1小时开门后才有现金\N{\r外文}I'm sorry, sir. We won't have any cash until the banks open in an hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:25.39,0:38:28.89,中文,,0,0,0,,但我肯定他们可以在飞机场 给你兑现支票\N{\r外文}But I'm sure they can cash your cheque at the airport.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:29.60,0:38:30.89,中文,,0,0,0,,飞机场\N{\r外文}The airport?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:31.02,0:38:33.27,中文,,0,0,0,,谁在飞机场兑现支票\N{\r外文}Who cashes cheques at the airport?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:33.40,0:38:36.90,中文,,0,0,0,,航空公司 他们总是给自己兑现\N{\r外文}The airlines. They've always taken care of their own.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:45.78,0:38:48.29,中文,,0,0,0,,你好 嗨 你要搭机吗\N{\r外文}Hello. Hi. Are you deadheading?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:48.91,0:38:49.95,中文,,0,0,0,,什么\N{\r外文}What?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:50.08,0:38:52.41,中文,,0,0,0,,你要搭机去迈阿密吗\N{\r外文}Are you my deadhead to Miami?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:54.75,0:38:56.09,中文,,0,0,0,,是的\N{\r外文}Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:56.92,0:38:59.59,中文,,0,0,0,,是 我要搭机 给你\N{\r外文}Yeah, I'm the deadhead. Here you go.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:00.21,0:39:03.43,中文,,0,0,0,,你有点晚了 但驾驶员座舱跳椅空着\N{\r外文}You're a little late, but the jump seat is open.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:05.89,0:39:10.47,中文,,0,0,0,,我干这一行已经有段时间了 但哪个是跳椅来着\N{\r外文}It's been a while since I've done this. Which one is the jump seat again?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:11.23,0:39:12.98,中文,,0,0,0,,旅途愉快\N{\r外文}Have a nice flight.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:13.14,0:39:15.06,中文,,0,0,0,,你搭我的飞机吗\N{\r外文}Are you my deadhead?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:17.40,0:39:20.65,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰克 奥利弗机长 约翰·拉金 副驾驶\N{\r外文}Frank, Captain Oliver. John Larkin, the copilot.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:20.78,0:39:22.53,中文,,0,0,0,,福瑞德·塔利 飞机工程师\N{\r外文}Fred Tulley, flight engineer.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:22.61,0:39:25.36,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰克·泰勒 泛美公司 谢谢让我搭乘 小伙子们\N{\r外文}Frank Taylor, Pan Am. Thanks for giving me a lift, boys.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:25.45,0:39:28.37,中文,,0,0,0,,去坐下吧 弗兰克 我们要起飞了\N{\r外文}Go ahead and take a seat, Frank. We're about to push.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:28.45,0:39:30.62,中文,,0,0,0,,你开什么飞机 DC-8\N{\r外文}What kind of equipment you on, DC-8?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:30.74,0:39:31.83,中文,,0,0,0,,707\N{\r外文}707.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:32.16,0:39:34.37,中文,,0,0,0,,你刚到就返回去\N{\r外文}You turning around on the redeye?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:34.46,0:39:36.79,中文,,0,0,0,,我下几个月要在洲际之间来回飞\N{\r外文}I'm jumping puddles for the next few months,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:36.92,0:39:40.13,中文,,0,0,0,,通过给那些又病又累的人替班 来多挣点钱\N{\r外文}trying to earn my keep running leap frogs for the weak and weary.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:40.25,0:39:42.80,中文,,0,0,0,,没什么不好的 我们都是这么过来的\N{\r外文}No shame in that. We all did it.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:49.97,0:39:52.02,中文,,0,0,0,,坐下吧 谢谢\N{\r外文}Have a seat. Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:53.14,0:39:55.31,中文,,0,0,0,,起飞后你想喝点什么吗\N{\r外文}Would you like a drink after takeoff?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:55.44,0:39:56.60,中文,,0,0,0,,牛奶\N{\r外文}Milk?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:57.02,0:39:58.98,中文,,0,0,0,,时速150公里 正确\N{\r外文}Eighty knots. Check.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:59.48,0:40:01.11,中文,,0,0,0,,已到V-1速度 起飞\N{\r外文}V-one. Rotate.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:04.11,0:40:05.99,中文,,0,0,0,,已到V-2速度 巡航\N{\r外文}V-two. Positive rate.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:06.11,0:40:07.36,中文,,0,0,0,,收起落架\N{\r外文}Gear up.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:08.16,0:40:10.83,中文,,0,0,0,,亲爱的爸爸 今天我毕业\N{\r外文}Dear Dad, today was graduation.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:11.37,0:40:16.00,中文,,0,0,0,,我现在是副驾驶 每月挣1400美元 外加福利\N{\r外文}I am now a copilot, earning $1,400 a month, plus benefits.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:16.29,0:40:20.25,中文,,0,0,0,,而最好的一点是 他们告诉我 说我的家里人可以免费飞\N{\r外文}And the best part is, they tell me my family can fly for free.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:20.34,0:40:23.21,中文,,0,0,0,,所以告诉妈妈去准备行李 买套新的泳衣\N{\r外文}So tell Mom to pack her bags and buy a new swimsuit
Dialogue: 0,0:40:23.34,0:40:26.72,中文,,0,0,0,,因为我要带你们去夏威夷过圣诞节\N{\r外文}because I'm taking us all to Hawaii for Christmas.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:26.84,0:40:30.22,中文,,0,0,0,,我爱你 爸爸 再见 弗兰克\N{\r外文}I love you, Dad. Aloha, Frank.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:31.18,0:40:32.60,中文,,0,0,0,,嗨 免费乘客 嗨\N{\r外文}Hello, deadhead. Hello.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:32.68,0:40:34.73,中文,,0,0,0,,旅途愉快吗\N{\r外文}Enjoying your free ride?
Dialogue: 0,0:40:40.73,0:40:42.02,中文,,0,0,0,,玛茜\N{\r外文}Marci,
Dialogue: 0,0:40:43.23,0:40:45.03,中文,,0,0,0,,你有没有掉了这个\N{\r外文}did you drop this?
Dialogue: 0,0:40:48.03,0:40:51.03,中文,,0,0,0,,一定是从你脖子上滑落下来的 不是\N{\r外文}Must have slipped right off your neck. No.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:52.70,0:40:53.83,中文,,0,0,0,,不是\N{\r外文}No!
Dialogue: 0,0:40:56.21,0:40:59.08,中文,,0,0,0,,对 对 对\N{\r外文}Yes, yes, yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:41:06.92,0:41:08.84,中文,,0,0,0,,你为什么停下来了\N{\r外文}Why are you stopping?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:10.26,0:41:12.89,中文,,0,0,0,,我想告诉你件事 玛茜\N{\r外文}I want to tell you something, Marci.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:14.52,0:41:16.23,中文,,0,0,0,,这是\N{\r外文}This is by far
Dialogue: 0,0:41:17.52,0:41:20.56,中文,,0,0,0,,我曾经有过的最好的约会\N{\r外文}the best date I have ever been on.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:33.34,0:41:33.91,中文,,0,0,0,,克罗宁小姐
Dialogue: 0,0:41:34.08,0:41:35.09,中文,,0,0,0,,阿达米小姐
Dialogue: 0,0:41:52.64,0:41:55.51,中文,,0,0,0,,欢迎来迈阿密互助银行 您有什么事情\N{\r外文}Welcome to Miami Mutual Bank. How may I help you?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:55.60,0:41:58.23,中文,,0,0,0,,我叫弗兰克·泰勒 我是泛美航空公司的副驾驶\N{\r外文}My name is Frank Taylor. I'm a copilot for Pan Am.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:58.31,0:42:01.44,中文,,0,0,0,,我想用这支票兑现金 然后\N{\r外文}I'd like to cash this cheque and then
Dialogue: 0,0:42:02.44,0:42:04.77,中文,,0,0,0,,我想带你去吃牛排晚餐\N{\r外文}I'd like to take you out for a steak dinner.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:15.28,0:42:17.70,中文,,0,0,0,,然后我们把这支票放进\N{\r外文}Then we feed the cheques into the MICR machine,
Dialogue: 0,0:42:17.79,0:42:19.25,中文,,0,0,0,,磁性墨迹识别机里\N{\r外文}which uses special ink to encode
Dialogue: 0,0:42:19.33,0:42:22.12,中文,,0,0,0,,它用一种特殊的墨水给支票加编码\N{\r外文}the account numbers on the bottom of the checks.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:22.83,0:42:25.13,中文,,0,0,0,,那些编码在哪里\N{\r外文}And where are these numbers?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:26.92,0:42:28.96,中文,,0,0,0,,就在这儿 在这儿\N{\r外文}They're right here. Right there?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:32.63,0:42:34.64,中文,,0,0,0,,它们叫做路由编码\N{\r外文}They're called routing numbers.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:34.76,0:42:37.47,中文,,0,0,0,,那么这些支票要路由到哪里去呢\N{\r外文}So where do the cheques get routed to?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:39.02,0:42:42.64,中文,,0,0,0,,我不太知道 从来没有人问过我\N{\r外文}I don't exactly know. Nobody ever asked me that before.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:43.65,0:42:45.36,中文,,0,0,0,,我们下一个竞标的物品还是来自\N{\r外文}Our next item up for bid is also from
Dialogue: 0,0:42:45.36,0:42:47.07,中文,,0,0,0,,新泽西中心银行的抵押没收品\N{\r外文}the Jersey Central Bank foreclosure.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:47.15,0:42:50.49,中文,,0,0,0,,这是台磁性墨迹识别机 这机器是用来给银行支票编码的\N{\r外文}This is a MICR encoder, a machine used to encode bank checks.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:50.61,0:42:51.99,中文,,0,0,0,,你有起标价吗\N{\r外文}Do I have an opening bid?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:52.11,0:42:55.45,中文,,0,0,0,,我们的罪犯是个伪造支票者 他从东海岸开始行骗\N{\r外文}Our unknown subject is a paperhanger who started working on the East Coast.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:55.53,0:42:57.24,中文,,0,0,0,,在过去的几个星期里 他发明了一种\N{\r外文}In the last few weeks, this unsub has developed
Dialogue: 0,0:42:57.33,0:43:00.25,中文,,0,0,0,,新型的支票欺诈手法 我称它"飘"\N{\r外文}a new form of cheque fraud I'm calling "The Float."
Dialogue: 0,0:43:00.33,0:43:03.21,中文,,0,0,0,,他在不同的银行开支票帐户\N{\r外文}What he's doing is he's opening checking accounts at various banks,
Dialogue: 0,0:43:03.33,0:43:06.79,中文,,0,0,0,,然后涂改那些支票底部的编码\N{\r外文}then changing the MICR ink routing numbers at the bottom of those checks.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:06.88,0:43:10.59,中文,,0,0,0,,请到下一张\N{\r外文}Next slide, please. Next slide, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:11.17,0:43:13.75,中文,,0,0,0,,遥控器坏了 你得手动\N{\r外文}The remote thing is broken. You'll have to do it by hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:13.76,0:43:16.34,中文,,0,0,0,,联邦调查局总部 华盛顿特区
Dialogue: 0,0:43:16.35,0:43:19.68,中文,,0,0,0,,应该是侧面的那个方按钮\N{\r外文}Agent Mullen, it should be the square button by the side.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:19.81,0:43:22.18,中文,,0,0,0,,转盘不好使 是个坏转盘\N{\r外文}This carousel doesn't work. It's a bad carousel.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:22.31,0:43:24.06,中文,,0,0,0,,谢谢 用手动\N{\r外文}Thank you. Move it manually.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:24.19,0:43:27.82,中文,,0,0,0,,这是美国联邦储备系统的12个银行的分布地图\N{\r外文}This is a map of the 12 banks of the U.S. Federal Reserve.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:27.90,0:43:29.15,中文,,0,0,0,,下一张\N{\r外文}Slide.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:30.19,0:43:32.53,中文,,0,0,0,,每个银行的识别机的扫描仪\N{\r外文}MICR scanners at every bank read these numbers
Dialogue: 0,0:43:32.61,0:43:34.57,中文,,0,0,0,,读取支票底部的这些数字 下一张\N{\r外文}at the bottom of the cheque. Slide.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:34.66,0:43:37.99,中文,,0,0,0,,然后把支票发送到相关的银行兑现\N{\r外文}And then ship that cheque off to its corresponding branch.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:38.08,0:43:41.58,中文,,0,0,0,,卡尔 对我们这些不熟悉银行诈骗的\N{\r外文}Carl, for those of us who are unfamiliar with bank fraud,
Dialogue: 0,0:43:41.83,0:43:44.96,中文,,0,0,0,,你能不能告诉我们你在讲的是什么\N{\r外文}you mind telling us what the hell you're talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:43:45.04,0:43:49.13,中文,,0,0,0,,东海岸分行的编号是从01到06\N{\r外文}The East Coast branches are numbered 01 to 06.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:49.21,0:43:51.80,中文,,0,0,0,,中部地区分行的编号是07到08 如此类推\N{\r外文}The central branch is 07, 08, so on and so forth.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:51.88,0:43:54.55,中文,,0,0,0,,底部的那些号码有什么实际意思吗\N{\r外文}You mean those numbers at the bottom of a cheque actually mean something?
Dialogue: 0,0:43:54.68,0:43:58.64,中文,,0,0,0,,所有这些都是我2天以前做的报告 如果你把\N{\r外文}All of this was in the report I filed two days ago. If you change
Dialogue: 0,0:43:58.72,0:44:03.06,中文,,0,0,0,,02改称12 这就意味着\N{\r外文}a 02 to a 12, that means that cheque,
Dialogue: 0,0:44:03.27,0:44:04.48,中文,,0,0,0,,在纽约提现金的支票\N{\r外文}which was cashed in New York,
Dialogue: 0,0:44:04.56,0:44:06.02,中文,,0,0,0,,被发送到旧金山的联邦分行\N{\r外文}does not go to the New York Federal Branch,
Dialogue: 0,0:44:06.10,0:44:10.44,中文,,0,0,0,,银行不知道支票会在2周后被退回\N{\r外文}but it is re-routed all the way to the San Francisco Federal Branch.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:10.52,0:44:13.03,中文,,0,0,0,,也就是说我们的目标可以待在一个地方\N{\r外文}The bank doesn't even know the cheque has bounced for two weeks.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:13.11,0:44:15.74,中文,,0,0,0,,趁他的支票在国内循环时\N{\r外文}Which means our unsub can stay in one place,
Dialogue: 0,0:44:15.86,0:44:19.58,中文,,0,0,0,,在同一个城市一遍一遍地写假支票\N{\r外文}paper the same city over and over again while his cheques circle the country.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:19.70,0:44:21.91,中文,,0,0,0,,你想和我的太太谈谈吧\N{\r外文}You want to talk to my wife.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:22.41,0:44:24.75,中文,,0,0,0,,我们家她管支票本\N{\r外文}She's the one who balances the chequebook at our house.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:30.21,0:44:31.59,中文,,0,0,0,,下一张\N{\r外文}Next slide.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:38.72,0:44:39.93,中文,,0,0,0,,爸爸\N{\r外文}Daddy.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:42.26,0:44:44.98,中文,,0,0,0,,我的孩子 飞行员 穿制服了\N{\r外文}My son, the birdman. That's some uniform, Frank.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:45.10,0:44:46.81,中文,,0,0,0,,你觉得怎样\N{\r外文}What do you think?
Dialogue: 0,0:44:47.48,0:44:48.65,中文,,0,0,0,,很好\N{\r外文}Nice.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:48.94,0:44:50.27,中文,,0,0,0,,坐下\N{\r外文}Sit down.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:53.40,0:44:56.03,中文,,0,0,0,,爸爸 你收到明信片了吗\N{\r外文}Dad, have you gotten the postcards?
Dialogue: 0,0:44:56.11,0:44:57.36,中文,,0,0,0,,当然\N{\r外文}Of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:57.45,0:44:58.95,中文,,0,0,0,,这叉子冰凉\N{\r外文}This fork is ice-cold.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:59.07,0:45:01.99,中文,,0,0,0,,不 爸爸 那是冰镇的吃沙拉用的叉子\N{\r外文}No, Dad, that's a chilled salad fork.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:03.79,0:45:06.29,中文,,0,0,0,,这是个高档餐厅 你知道\N{\r外文}It's a fancy restaurant, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:11.21,0:45:12.38,中文,,0,0,0,,这儿\N{\r外文}Here.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:13.96,0:45:16.47,中文,,0,0,0,,我给你件礼物 什么东西\N{\r外文}I got you something. What's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:16.59,0:45:17.88,中文,,0,0,0,,打开它\N{\r外文}Open it.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:23.39,0:45:25.77,中文,,0,0,0,,你知道那些是什么 对吧\N{\r外文}You know what those are, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:26.43,0:45:30.90,中文,,0,0,0,,是一辆1965年凯迪拉克敞篷跑车的钥匙\N{\r外文}Those are the keys to a 1965 Cadillac DeVille convertible.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:30.98,0:45:34.40,中文,,0,0,0,,全新的 爸爸 车身红色 车内白色\N{\r外文}Brand-new, Dad. Red with white interior,
Dialogue: 0,0:45:34.48,0:45:37.82,中文,,0,0,0,,分开的座位 空调 全套的配置\N{\r外文}split seats, air conditioning, the works.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:38.15,0:45:40.16,中文,,0,0,0,,你送给我一辆凯迪拉克\N{\r外文}Are you giving me a Cadillac?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:40.24,0:45:42.32,中文,,0,0,0,,我送给你一辆凯迪拉克\N{\r外文}I'm giving you a Cadillac.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:42.57,0:45:44.49,中文,,0,0,0,,爸爸 它就停在楼下\N{\r外文}Dad, she's parked downstairs.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:44.58,0:45:47.91,中文,,0,0,0,,我们吃完午饭后 就开到妈妈那里去\N{\r外文}When we're done eating lunch, why don't you drive on over to Mom's house,
Dialogue: 0,0:45:48.00,0:45:50.00,中文,,0,0,0,,带上她兜兜风\N{\r外文}pick her up, take a little joy ride?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:50.08,0:45:51.75,中文,,0,0,0,,你知道会发生什么\N{\r外文}Do you know what would happen
Dialogue: 0,0:45:51.83,0:45:55.63,中文,,0,0,0,,如果税务局发现我开辆新的单排座车 到处跑\N{\r外文}if the IRS found out I was driving around in a new coupe?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:57.34,0:46:01.01,中文,,0,0,0,,我坐火车来的 弗兰克 我要坐火车回家\N{\r外文}I took the train here, Frank. I'm taking the train home.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:03.10,0:46:04.47,中文,,0,0,0,,好吧\N{\r外文}All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:11.69,0:46:13.61,中文,,0,0,0,,我有的是钱\N{\r外文}I have plenty of money.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:13.69,0:46:16.02,中文,,0,0,0,,你知道 需要什么尽管讲\N{\r外文}You know, if you ever need anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:16.15,0:46:18.78,中文,,0,0,0,,你担心吗 担心我\N{\r外文}You worried? About me?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:19.86,0:46:21.78,中文,,0,0,0,,不 我不担心\N{\r外文}No, I'm not worried.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:21.86,0:46:23.95,中文,,0,0,0,,你想我自己买不起车\N{\r外文}You think I can't buy my own car?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:24.03,0:46:27.37,中文,,0,0,0,,2只老鼠掉进奶油桶里 弗兰克\N{\r外文}Two mice fell in a bucket of cream, Frank.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:28.37,0:46:29.96,中文,,0,0,0,,我是哪只\N{\r外文}Which one am I?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:30.87,0:46:32.96,中文,,0,0,0,,你是第2只老鼠\N{\r外文}You're that second mouse.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:34.84,0:46:36.96,中文,,0,0,0,,我今天路过商店\N{\r外文}I went by the store today.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:38.30,0:46:41.80,中文,,0,0,0,,我不得不把商店关几天 只是个时间问题\N{\r外文}I had to close the store for a while. It's all about timing, Frank.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:41.88,0:46:44.97,中文,,0,0,0,,狗屁政府清楚这点 他们落井下石\N{\r外文}Goddamn government knows that. They hit you when you're down.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:45.05,0:46:47.89,中文,,0,0,0,,我不想让他们把商店夺走 所以我就\N{\r外文}I wasn't going to let them take it from me, so I just
Dialogue: 0,0:46:48.02,0:46:50.48,中文,,0,0,0,,干脆自己关了店门 看他们能把我怎样\N{\r外文}shut the doors myself, called their bluff.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:55.56,0:46:58.15,中文,,0,0,0,,早晚他们是要忘了我的\N{\r外文}Sooner or later, they'll forget about me.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:58.23,0:46:59.74,中文,,0,0,0,,我明白\N{\r外文}I understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:01.57,0:47:03.24,中文,,0,0,0,,你告诉妈了吗\N{\r外文}Have you told Ma?
Dialogue: 0,0:47:05.74,0:47:08.83,中文,,0,0,0,,你母亲她很固执\N{\r外文}She's so stubborn, your mother.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:12.50,0:47:15.50,中文,,0,0,0,,不要担心 我不会不劝她就让她走的\N{\r外文}Don't worry, I'm not going to let her go without a fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:15.58,0:47:17.54,中文,,0,0,0,,我要劝她为我们留下\N{\r外文}I'm fighting for us...
Dialogue: 0,0:47:20.17,0:47:21.26,中文,,0,0,0,,爸爸\N{\r外文}Dad?
Dialogue: 0,0:47:23.76,0:47:26.18,中文,,0,0,0,,从我们相遇的那天起\N{\r外文}...since the day we met.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:26.76,0:47:29.43,中文,,0,0,0,,爸爸 在那些人当中\N{\r外文}Daddy, out of all those men,
Dialogue: 0,0:47:29.93,0:47:32.60,中文,,0,0,0,,是你把她带到家来的 记得吗\N{\r外文}you were the one that took her home, remember that?
Dialogue: 0,0:47:32.68,0:47:34.02,中文,,0,0,0,,200人\N{\r外文}Two hundred men
Dialogue: 0,0:47:34.10,0:47:37.61,中文,,0,0,0,,坐在那个小活动厅里 看她跳舞\N{\r外文}sitting in that tiny social hall, watching her dance.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:40.28,0:47:43.74,中文,,0,0,0,,那个小镇叫什么名字来着 曼沙 爸爸\N{\r外文}What was the name of that town? Montrichard, Dad.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:44.57,0:47:46.78,中文,,0,0,0,,我一句法语也不会说\N{\r外文}I didn't speak a word of French,
Dialogue: 0,0:47:46.87,0:47:50.45,中文,,0,0,0,,而6个星期之后她成了我的妻子\N{\r外文}and six weeks later, she was my wife.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:51.95,0:47:53.62,中文,,0,0,0,,她还是你的妻子\N{\r外文}She is your wife.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:56.08,0:48:00.46,中文,,0,0,0,,我儿子今天给我买了辆凯迪拉克 我想该为此干一杯\N{\r外文}My son bought me a Cadillac today. I think that calls for a toast.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:10.31,0:48:12.85,中文,,0,0,0,,为了他妈的最好的飞行员\N{\r外文}To the best damn pilot in the sky.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:13.93,0:48:17.06,中文,,0,0,0,,不像你想的那样 我只是名副驾驶\N{\r外文}It's not what you think. I'm just a copilot.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:18.81,0:48:21.44,中文,,0,0,0,,你看见这些人在注视你吗\N{\r外文}You see these people staring at you?
Dialogue: 0,0:48:24.99,0:48:28.20,中文,,0,0,0,,这些都是纽约市最有权势的人\N{\r外文}These are the most powerful people in New York City.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:28.28,0:48:33.08,中文,,0,0,0,,他们总是越过肩膀偷看 想知道今晚你去哪里\N{\r外文}They keep peeking over their shoulders, wondering where you're going tonight.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:33.16,0:48:35.04,中文,,0,0,0,,你要去哪里 弗兰克\N{\r外文}Where you going, Frank?
Dialogue: 0,0:48:35.12,0:48:37.37,中文,,0,0,0,,爸爸 没有人在盯着我\N{\r外文}Dad, nobody's staring at me.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:37.83,0:48:39.58,中文,,0,0,0,,什么奇异的地方吗\N{\r外文}Some place exotic?
Dialogue: 0,0:48:41.88,0:48:44.30,中文,,0,0,0,,告诉我你要去哪里\N{\r外文}Just tell me where you're going.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:46.59,0:48:48.76,中文,,0,0,0,,洛杉 好莱坞\N{\r外文}Los... Hollywood.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:49.01,0:48:50.39,中文,,0,0,0,,好莱坞\N{\r外文}Hollywood?
Dialogue: 0,0:48:53.22,0:48:54.56,中文,,0,0,0,,过来\N{\r外文}Come here.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:56.77,0:49:00.11,中文,,0,0,0,,我们其余的人真是笨蛋\N{\r外文}The rest of us really are suckers.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:06.36,0:49:09.16,中文,,0,0,0,,所以我穿了这红衣服和高跟鞋 对吗\N{\r外文}So I got on this red dress and these high heels, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:49:09.24,0:49:10.82,中文,,0,0,0,,我外边这儿戴了胸罩\N{\r外文}I got a bra out here.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:10.91,0:49:13.58,中文,,0,0,0,,我在公园里追2个波多黎各人\N{\r外文}I'm chasing two Puerto Rican guys through the park.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:11.58,0:49:15.08,中文,,0,0,0,,{\an8}加州 好莱坞
Dialogue: 0,0:49:13.66,0:49:16.12,中文,,0,0,0,,他们拎一个装满了从银行抢来的钱的箱子\N{\r外文}They got a suitcase filled with bank robbery loot.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:16.20,0:49:18.71,中文,,0,0,0,,我大喊 "联邦调查局 不许动"\N{\r外文}Okay, I'm screaming out, "F.B.I., freeze!"
Dialogue: 0,0:49:18.79,0:49:21.25,中文,,0,0,0,,我去拿枪却发现不在胸罩里\N{\r外文}I'm reaching for my gun, but I can't find it in the bra.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:21.33,0:49:25.30,中文,,0,0,0,,它太他妈大了 我想我他妈的都快要 射到我胸里去了\N{\r外文}It's so damn big, I thought I was going to shoot my tits off.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:27.47,0:49:30.97,中文,,0,0,0,,这是个有趣的故事 别人总是被逗笑\N{\r外文}That's a funny story. People always laugh at that story.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:31.05,0:49:32.68,中文,,0,0,0,,让我问你一个问题\N{\r外文}Let me ask you a question, Mr Amdursky.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:32.76,0:49:36.39,中文,,0,0,0,,如果你觉得当便衣很有意思 那你为什么转到银行诈骗科\N{\r外文}If you had so much fun undercover, why did you transfer to bank fraud?
Dialogue: 0,0:49:36.48,0:49:39.77,中文,,0,0,0,,不是我要求转的 我受责难被重分配的\N{\r外文}I didn't transfer. I was censured and reassigned.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:40.35,0:49:43.86,中文,,0,0,0,,就像是受罚了就受罚了 我出外勤时犯了个错误\N{\r外文}It's like being punished. I was punished. I screwed up in the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:43.94,0:49:46.99,中文,,0,0,0,,福克斯先生 你有没有在出外勤时 因为犯错而受罚过\N{\r外文}What about you, Mr Fox, were you punished for screwing up in the field?
Dialogue: 0,0:49:47.07,0:49:49.28,中文,,0,0,0,,没有 我以前从没穿便衣去调查过\N{\r外文}No, I've never worked in the field before.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:49.36,0:49:53.58,中文,,0,0,0,,我审计司法部的背景调查\N{\r外文}I audited background investigations of Department of Justice clerical applicants.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:53.66,0:49:54.61,中文,,0,0,0,,真是太好了\N{\r外文}That's just great.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:54.61,0:49:58.16,中文,,0,0,0,,我要一队便衣 结果他们给我派了2个不称职的人\N{\r外文}I ask for a team and they drag the bottom of the Pacific.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:58.71,0:50:01.00,中文,,0,0,0,,我能问你个问题吗\N{\r外文}Mind if I ask you a question, Agent Hanratty?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:01.12,0:50:02.67,中文,,0,0,0,,你为什么总是那么严肃\N{\r外文}How come you're so serious all the time?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:02.75,0:50:05.34,中文,,0,0,0,,这干扰你了吗 阿穆德斯基先生\N{\r外文}Does it bother you, Mr Amdursky?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:05.42,0:50:07.46,中文,,0,0,0,,对 是干扰我了\N{\r外文}Yeah, it does bother me.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:07.80,0:50:09.67,中文,,0,0,0,,干扰你了吗 福克斯先生\N{\r外文}Does it bother you, Mr Fox?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:09.76,0:50:11.51,中文,,0,0,0,,有点 我想\N{\r外文}A little, I guess.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:12.55,0:50:15.31,中文,,0,0,0,,你们想听我讲个笑话吗\N{\r外文}Would you like to hear me tell a joke?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:16.60,0:50:19.56,中文,,0,0,0,,想 我们很想听你讲个笑话\N{\r外文}Yeah, we'd love to hear a joke from you.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:21.35,0:50:22.73,中文,,0,0,0,,咚咚敲门\N{\r外文}Knock, knock.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:22.81,0:50:24.27,中文,,0,0,0,,是谁\N{\r外文}Who's there?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:26.94,0:50:28.74,中文,,0,0,0,,去你妈的\N{\r外文}Go fuck yourselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:42.12,0:50:44.79,中文,,0,0,0,,他今天兑现了3张支票 都取到钱了\N{\r外文}He cashed three checks. They all cleared.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:44.88,0:50:46.96,中文,,0,0,0,,我今天要存这张了的\N{\r外文}I was going to deposit this one today.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:48.88,0:50:50.97,中文,,0,0,0,,我不想有麻烦\N{\r外文}I don't want any trouble.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:51.59,0:50:53.01,中文,,0,0,0,,没有麻烦\N{\r外文}No trouble.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:53.80,0:50:55.10,中文,,0,0,0,,一点没有\N{\r外文}No trouble at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:55.18,0:50:58.31,中文,,0,0,0,,我们拿了这支票就走 谢谢\N{\r外文}We'll just take this cheque and be on our way. Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:58.39,0:51:00.43,中文,,0,0,0,,因为我不想让我的顾客受到骚扰\N{\r外文}Because I don't want my customers harassed.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:03.56,0:51:06.27,中文,,0,0,0,,你说什么 他还在这吗\N{\r外文}What are you saying? He's still here?
Dialogue: 0,0:51:07.02,0:51:08.15,中文,,0,0,0,,201房间\N{\r外文}201.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:10.36,0:51:11.40,中文,,0,0,0,,谢谢\N{\r外文}Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:12.49,0:51:14.61,中文,,0,0,0,,到角落了 谢谢 儿子\N{\r外文}Corner here. Thanks, son.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:16.49,0:51:18.29,中文,,0,0,0,,有楼梯 楼梯\N{\r外文}Some steps. Steps.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:22.04,0:51:24.00,中文,,0,0,0,,墨菲先生 你好吗\N{\r外文}Mr Murphy, how are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:51:24.08,0:51:25.67,中文,,0,0,0,,是弗兰克吗 是\N{\r外文}Is that Frank? Yeah, it's Frank.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:25.75,0:51:27.92,中文,,0,0,0,,你好 膝盖怎么样了\N{\r外文}Hey, Frank. How are you? How's the knee?
Dialogue: 0,0:51:28.00,0:51:30.17,中文,,0,0,0,,得了 我现在就跟你赛跑\N{\r外文}Come on, I'll race you right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:30.26,0:51:31.97,中文,,0,0,0,,小心点 好 弗兰克\N{\r外文}Take care. Okay, Frank.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:33.13,0:51:34.51,中文,,0,0,0,,看住后门\N{\r外文}Eyeball the back? Come on, Carl.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:34.59,0:51:36.47,中文,,0,0,0,,这家伙是个伪造字迹的人\N{\r外文}This guy's a pen-and-ink man, a goddamn paperhanger.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:36.55,0:51:38.39,中文,,0,0,0,,我们为什么不能跟着你\N{\r外文}Why can't we go with you, Carl?
Dialogue: 0,0:51:38.47,0:51:43.06,中文,,0,0,0,,睁大眼睛好好干 我给你们两个买冰激凌吃\N{\r外文}Keep your eyes open, do your job and I'll buy you both a Good Humour bar.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:52.82,0:51:54.99,中文,,0,0,0,,没事 夫人 联邦调查局\N{\r外文}It's all right, ma'am. F.B.I.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:57.53,0:51:59.66,中文,,0,0,0,,201\N{\r外文}201.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:11.88,0:52:13.09,中文,,0,0,0,,联邦调查局\N{\r外文}F.B.I.!
Dialogue: 0,0:52:22.22,0:52:23.43,中文,,0,0,0,,联邦调查局\N{\r外文}F.B.I.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:24.43,0:52:26.52,中文,,0,0,0,,从卫生间出来\N{\r外文}Come out of the bathroom!
Dialogue: 0,0:52:27.52,0:52:29.61,中文,,0,0,0,,走出卫生间\N{\r外文}Step out of the bathroom!
Dialogue: 0,0:52:33.53,0:52:36.24,中文,,0,0,0,,手放在头上 那是新的IBM电动打字机\N{\r外文}Hands on your head. That's the new IBM Selectric...
Dialogue: 0,0:52:36.32,0:52:38.49,中文,,0,0,0,,把手放到 5号字体打印的\N{\r外文}Put your hands on your head! ...print type in five seconds...
Dialogue: 0,0:52:38.57,0:52:39.82,中文,,0,0,0,,闭嘴\N{\r外文}Shut up!
Dialogue: 0,0:52:39.91,0:52:41.87,中文,,0,0,0,,把手放到头上\N{\r外文}Put your hands on your head!
Dialogue: 0,0:52:41.95,0:52:45.91,中文,,0,0,0,,他有200多张支票 1加仑的引渡墨水 草图\N{\r外文}He's got over 200 cheques, a gallon of India ink, drafting...
Dialogue: 0,0:52:46.00,0:52:48.33,中文,,0,0,0,,甚至薪水信封都写着他自己的地址\N{\r外文}Even has little payroll envelopes addressed to himself...
Dialogue: 0,0:52:48.42,0:52:50.71,中文,,0,0,0,,放下它 扔掉它 放松点\N{\r外文}Put it down! Drop it! Relax!
Dialogue: 0,0:52:51.25,0:52:53.00,中文,,0,0,0,,你来晚了 好吗\N{\r外文}You're late, all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:52:53.09,0:52:55.88,中文,,0,0,0,,我是巴里·艾伦 美国情报局的\N{\r外文}My name's Barry Allen, United States Secret Service.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:55.97,0:52:57.59,中文,,0,0,0,,你的嫌疑犯刚才想从窗户跳出去\N{\r外文}Your boy just tried to jump out the window.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:57.68,0:53:01.18,中文,,0,0,0,,我的同伴刚刚拘捕了他 我不明白你在说什么\N{\r外文}My partner has him in custody. I don't know what you're talking about.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:01.26,0:53:04.85,中文,,0,0,0,,你以为只有联邦调查局在追捕他吗 得了\N{\r外文}You think the F.B.I. are the only ones on this guy? Come on.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:04.93,0:53:07.02,中文,,0,0,0,,他篡改政府支票\N{\r外文}He's dabbling in government checks.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:07.10,0:53:10.86,中文,,0,0,0,,我们调查他的行踪已经几个月了\N{\r外文}We've been following a paper trail on this guy for months now.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:10.94,0:53:13.27,中文,,0,0,0,,你能不能别把枪对着我的脸\N{\r外文}You mind taking that gun out of my face?
Dialogue: 0,0:53:13.36,0:53:15.36,中文,,0,0,0,,真的 这让我感觉紧张\N{\r外文}Please. Really. It makes me nervous.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:15.49,0:53:17.15,中文,,0,0,0,,让我看看你的证件\N{\r外文}Let me see some credentials.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:17.74,0:53:19.16,中文,,0,0,0,,好 当然\N{\r外文}Yeah, sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:21.03,0:53:22.91,中文,,0,0,0,,把我的钱包都拿去吧\N{\r外文}Take my whole wallet.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:23.12,0:53:26.45,中文,,0,0,0,,你还想要我的枪 过来到这儿来拿枪\N{\r外文}You want my gun, too? Come over here, take my gun.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:28.04,0:53:31.33,中文,,0,0,0,,帮我个忙 往外看看 看看窗外\N{\r外文}Just do me a favour, take a look outside. Look out the window.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:31.42,0:53:34.55,中文,,0,0,0,,我的同伴正押着他走向那车 看\N{\r外文}My partner's walking him to the car as we speak. Look.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:37.47,0:53:40.34,中文,,0,0,0,,我进来时老家伙差点尿裤子\N{\r外文}Old guy almost pissed in his pants when I came through the door.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:40.55,0:53:43.93,中文,,0,0,0,,他直接从这窗户跳到我车的机器盖上\N{\r外文}He jumped right through the window onto the hood of my car.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:44.56,0:53:45.72,中文,,0,0,0,,墨菲\N{\r外文}Murph?
Dialogue: 0,0:53:45.81,0:53:49.77,中文,,0,0,0,,给洛杉矶警察局打电话 我不想让人走进我的犯罪现场\N{\r外文}Call the LAPD. I don't want people walking through my crime scene.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:51.90,0:53:54.69,中文,,0,0,0,,我没想到情报局卷了进来\N{\r外文}I didn't expect the Secret Service on this.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:54.82,0:53:57.65,中文,,0,0,0,,不要担心 你叫什么名字\N{\r外文}Don't worry about it. What's your name?
Dialogue: 0,0:53:58.19,0:54:00.61,中文,,0,0,0,,汉莱提 卡尔·汉莱提\N{\r外文}Hanratty, Carl Hanratty.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:06.20,0:54:08.79,中文,,0,0,0,,我能看一下你的证件吗\N{\r外文}Mind if I see some identification?
Dialogue: 0,0:54:09.62,0:54:12.54,中文,,0,0,0,,这些日子一定要小心\N{\r外文}You never can be too careful these days.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:13.59,0:54:15.38,中文,,0,0,0,,唉 运气不好 卡尔\N{\r外文}Well, tough luck, Carl.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:15.46,0:54:18.09,中文,,0,0,0,,你要是早来5分钟 就可以抓个正着\N{\r外文}Five minutes earlier, you would've landed yourself a pretty good collar.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:18.17,0:54:21.09,中文,,0,0,0,,要是晚来10秒钟 就被射死了\N{\r外文}Is that right? Ten seconds later, you'd have been shot.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:22.51,0:54:25.64,中文,,0,0,0,,你介意我跟你一起去吗 我得看看这家伙\N{\r外文}Mind if I come downstairs with you? I got to take a look at this guy.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:25.72,0:54:28.18,中文,,0,0,0,,当然不 帮个忙\N{\r外文}Sure thing. Just do me a favour and sit tight for a sec
Dialogue: 0,0:54:28.27,0:54:29.89,中文,,0,0,0,,等我下楼去取证据\N{\r外文}while I get this evidence downstairs.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:29.98,0:54:33.02,中文,,0,0,0,,我不想让服务员进来铺床\N{\r外文}I don't want some maid walking through here and making the bed.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:33.10,0:54:35.69,中文,,0,0,0,,洛杉矶警察局的人随时会到 等等\N{\r外文}LAPD should be here any sec. Wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:40.24,0:54:41.49,中文,,0,0,0,,你的钱包\N{\r外文}Your wallet.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:42.36,0:54:45.20,中文,,0,0,0,,替我保管一会儿 我相信你\N{\r外文}You hang onto it for a minute. I trust you.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:04.51,0:55:06.43,中文,,0,0,0,,情报局\N{\r外文}Secret Service.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:50.97,0:55:52.43,中文,,0,0,0,,见鬼\N{\r外文}God damn it!
Dialogue: 0,0:55:53.98,0:55:56.77,中文,,0,0,0,,很愚蠢 我犯了个愚蠢的错误\N{\r外文}It was stupid. I made a stupid mistake.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:57.61,0:55:58.90,中文,,0,0,0,,别想它了\N{\r外文}Forget about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:58.98,0:56:01.53,中文,,0,0,0,,还有好多嫌疑犯要抓呢\N{\r外文}There are hundreds of unknown subjects out there.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:01.61,0:56:02.73,中文,,0,0,0,,我能抓住这家伙\N{\r外文}I can get this guy.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:03.73,0:56:05.86,中文,,0,0,0,,造假的人所做的最糟糕的事情 就是被人看见脸了\N{\r外文}The worst thing a paperhanger can do is show his face.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:05.95,0:56:07.28,中文,,0,0,0,,我读了报告\N{\r外文}I read the report.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:07.37,0:56:11.04,中文,,0,0,0,,1米80高 棕色头发 27到30岁之间 70公斤\N{\r外文}Six feet tall, brown hair, 27 to 30 years of age, 160 pounds.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:11.12,0:56:12.70,中文,,0,0,0,,这差不多说谁都是\N{\r外文}This could be almost anybody.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:12.79,0:56:14.87,中文,,0,0,0,,我听见了他的声音 我看见了他的脸\N{\r外文}I heard his voice. I saw his face.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:14.96,0:56:16.92,中文,,0,0,0,,他没有什么可掩藏的了\N{\r外文}There's nothing for him to hide behind any more.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:18.38,0:56:19.67,中文,,0,0,0,,小心些\N{\r外文}Just be careful.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:19.88,0:56:21.80,中文,,0,0,0,,你干了12年了\N{\r外文}You got 12 years in.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:21.88,0:56:23.59,中文,,0,0,0,,没有人干扰你的工作\N{\r外文}Nobody bothers you down on the first floor.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:23.67,0:56:25.43,中文,,0,0,0,,你写了那本银行诈骗案的书\N{\r外文}You practically wrote the book on bank fraud.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:25.51,0:56:28.60,中文,,0,0,0,,那会让你有一天成为部门主管的\N{\r外文}That's the kind of thing that can make you section chief someday.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:28.68,0:56:31.97,中文,,0,0,0,,不要把自己放到那种位置上\N{\r外文}Just don't put yourself in this type of position.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:32.18,0:56:33.43,中文,,0,0,0,,哪种位置\N{\r外文}What type of position?
Dialogue: 0,0:56:35.35,0:56:37.65,中文,,0,0,0,,受辱的位置\N{\r外文}The position of being humiliated.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:45.90,0:56:48.70,中文,,0,0,0,,你想听我讲个笑话吗\N{\r外文}Sean, would you like to hear me tell a joke?
Dialogue: 0,0:56:50.03,0:56:51.37,中文,,0,0,0,,当然\N{\r外文}Yeah. Sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:52.54,0:56:54.08,中文,,0,0,0,,咚咚敲门\N{\r外文}Knock, knock.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:56.87,0:57:01.38,中文,,0,0,0,,我的下个问题是 飞行员退休后\N{\r外文}My next question is, when a pilot retires,
Dialogue: 0,0:57:02.21,0:57:04.80,中文,,0,0,0,,泛美每个月都给他们发张支票吗\N{\r外文}Pan Am sends them a cheque every single month?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:04.88,0:57:07.63,中文,,0,0,0,,对 按养老金计划给他们发支票和福利\N{\r外文}Yeah, pension programme sends a cheque and benefits.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:07.72,0:57:09.18,中文,,0,0,0,,支票上有多少钱\N{\r外文}How much is that cheque for?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:09.59,0:57:11.26,中文,,0,0,0,,我现在没有心情谈这个\N{\r外文}Kid, I'm really not in the mood for this right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:11.35,0:57:13.31,中文,,0,0,0,,那个空中强盗都快把我搞疯了\N{\r外文}This Skywayman's driving me crazy.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:13.39,0:57:14.60,中文,,0,0,0,,哪个强盗\N{\r外文}Who's the Skywayman?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:14.68,0:57:17.77,中文,,0,0,0,,一个疯子假扮成泛美飞行员 在这个国家到处飞\N{\r外文}Some nut flying around the country, posing as a Pan Am pilot.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:17.85,0:57:20.69,中文,,0,0,0,,今天报纸有他的一个栏目\N{\r外文}There's a column about him in the paper today.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:27.11,0:57:30.95,中文,,0,0,0,,我不断告诉他们说这不是我的问题 这家伙甚至不飞泛美\N{\r外文}I keep telling them it's not my problem. This guy doesn't even fly Pan Am.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:31.03,0:57:34.08,中文,,0,0,0,,他飞别的公司 他飞联合 环球\N{\r外文}Flies everybody else. Flies United, TWA,
Dialogue: 0,0:57:34.20,0:57:35.87,中文,,0,0,0,,大陆 东部\N{\r外文}Continental, Eastern.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:36.20,0:57:37.91,中文,,0,0,0,,空中强盗\N{\r外文}The Skywayman.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:38.41,0:57:40.58,中文,,0,0,0,,报界喜欢这小丑\N{\r外文}Newspaper loves this clown.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:41.42,0:57:43.54,中文,,0,0,0,,他们称他为空中的詹姆斯·邦德\N{\r外文}They call him the James Bond of the sky.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:46.55,0:57:47.55,中文,,0,0,0,,你说\N{\r外文}Did you say...
Dialogue: 0,0:57:47.63,0:57:49.26,中文,,0,0,0,,邦德 詹姆斯·邦德\N{\r外文}Bond, James Bond.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:58.94,0:58:01.44,中文,,0,0,0,,告诉我 琼 他为什么那样做\N{\r外文}Tell me, Joan, why does he do it?
Dialogue: 0,0:58:01.56,0:58:03.06,中文,,0,0,0,,他喜欢赢\N{\r外文}He likes to win.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:03.48,0:58:05.44,中文,,0,0,0,,我们20分钟后着陆\N{\r外文}We'll be landing in 20 minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:05.57,0:58:08.36,中文,,0,0,0,,你想服从还是让我杀了你\N{\r外文}Do you want to play it easy, or the hard way?
Dialogue: 0,0:58:08.44,0:58:10.15,中文,,0,0,0,,这家伙可不老实\N{\r外文}And this isn't a tranquiliser.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:10.24,0:58:13.28,中文,,0,0,0,,普茜 你了解飞机比枪多得多\N{\r外文}Pussy, you know a lot more about planes than guns.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:13.99,0:58:15.49,中文,,0,0,0,,你好 普茜\N{\r外文}Hello, Pussy.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:16.41,0:58:18.37,中文,,0,0,0,,你肯定是这样的衣服\N{\r外文}You're sure this is the suit, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:58:18.45,0:58:19.62,中文,,0,0,0,,肯定\N{\r外文}Positive.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:19.79,0:58:21.83,中文,,0,0,0,,跟他在电影里穿的完全一样\N{\r外文}It's the exact suit he wore in the movie.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:21.92,0:58:24.17,中文,,0,0,0,,好 我买3套\N{\r外文}Okay. I'll take three.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:24.25,0:58:25.96,中文,,0,0,0,,当然 弗莱明先生\N{\r外文}Certainly, Mr Fleming.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:26.09,0:58:30.30,中文,,0,0,0,,现在你缺的就是一辆他开的那种 小的外国跑车\N{\r外文}Now all you need is one of those little foreign sports cars that he drives.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:57.91,0:58:59.45,中文,,0,0,0,,你好 嗨\N{\r外文}Hello. Hi.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:03.33,0:59:05.25,中文,,0,0,0,,我以前见过你吗\N{\r外文}Haven't I seen you before?
Dialogue: 0,0:59:07.80,0:59:09.09,中文,,0,0,0,,也许\N{\r外文}Maybe.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:09.63,0:59:12.80,中文,,0,0,0,,几年以前我上过《17岁》的封面\N{\r外文}A couple of years ago, I was on the cover of Seventeen.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:15.09,0:59:17.60,中文,,0,0,0,,你是模特 对吗 谢丽尔\N{\r外文}You're that model, right? Cheryl.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:18.60,0:59:21.48,中文,,0,0,0,,我同学总喜欢把你的照片贴在存衣柜里\N{\r外文}Guys used to put your picture on their lockers.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:23.27,0:59:26.15,中文,,0,0,0,,我看见的停在外面的那辆银色轿车 是你的吗\N{\r外文}Isn't that your silver car I saw parked out front?
Dialogue: 0,0:59:26.44,0:59:28.65,中文,,0,0,0,,对 是我所有车中的一部\N{\r外文}Yeah. One of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:32.99,0:59:35.62,中文,,0,0,0,,所以 能给我签个名吗\N{\r外文}So, think I could get an autograph?
Dialogue: 0,0:59:39.99,0:59:42.00,中文,,0,0,0,,你房间里有笔吗\N{\r外文}Do you have a pen in your room?
Dialogue: 0,0:59:43.43,0:59:46.25,中文,,0,0,0,,15美分大号 干衣 10美分5分钟 开业
Dialogue: 0,1:00:20.70,1:00:23.54,中文,,0,0,0,,像你这样的人可以买任何想要的东西\N{\r外文}A man like you can buy anything he wants.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:35.22,1:00:38.39,中文,,0,0,0,,你在旅馆的礼品店里买了一副纸牌\N{\r外文}He buys a deck of cards at the hotel gift shop.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:41.72,1:00:43.56,中文,,0,0,0,,你想看纸牌戏法吗\N{\r外文}You want to see a card trick?
Dialogue: 0,1:00:45.18,1:00:47.19,中文,,0,0,0,,这些牌花多少钱买的\N{\r外文}How much did these cards cost?
Dialogue: 0,1:00:49.02,1:00:51.40,中文,,0,0,0,,我不知道 55美分 我想\N{\r外文}I don't know, 55 cents, I think.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:54.74,1:00:58.74,中文,,0,0,0,,如果他们在楼下礼品店卖我\N{\r外文}And if they sold me downstairs at the hotel gift shop,
Dialogue: 0,1:01:00.74,1:01:02.74,中文,,0,0,0,,你愿付多少钱\N{\r外文}how much would you pay?
Dialogue: 0,1:01:05.58,1:01:08.54,中文,,0,0,0,,对不起 我愿付什么\N{\r外文}I'm sorry, how much would I pay for what?
Dialogue: 0,1:01:11.46,1:01:13.09,中文,,0,0,0,,整个晚上\N{\r外文}The entire night.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:15.42,1:01:18.59,中文,,0,0,0,,你一晚愿付我多少钱\N{\r外文}How much would you pay me for the entire night?
Dialogue: 0,1:01:23.22,1:01:25.93,中文,,0,0,0,,谢丽尔 我真不知道\N{\r外文}Cheryl, I really don't know.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:28.10,1:01:29.77,中文,,0,0,0,,不要害怕\N{\r外文}Don't be scared.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:34.28,1:01:35.99,中文,,0,0,0,,给我出个价\N{\r外文}Make me an offer.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:43.74,1:01:45.12,中文,,0,0,0,,300美元\N{\r外文}300?
Dialogue: 0,1:01:46.45,1:01:47.96,中文,,0,0,0,,抓牌\N{\r外文}Go fish.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:51.83,1:01:53.46,中文,,0,0,0,,500美元\N{\r外文}$500?
Dialogue: 0,1:01:54.17,1:01:55.46,中文,,0,0,0,,抓牌\N{\r外文}Go fish.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:56.80,1:01:58.30,中文,,0,0,0,,600美元\N{\r外文}600.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:00.13,1:02:01.43,中文,,0,0,0,,抓牌\N{\r外文}Go fish!
Dialogue: 0,1:02:04.76,1:02:06.10,中文,,0,0,0,,1000美元\N{\r外文}$1,000.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:08.68,1:02:09.81,中文,,0,0,0,,好\N{\r外文}Okay.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:11.81,1:02:13.65,中文,,0,0,0,,1000美元\N{\r外文}$1,000.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:15.32,1:02:16.65,中文,,0,0,0,,好\N{\r外文}Okay.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:17.49,1:02:19.03,中文,,0,0,0,,我马上就回来\N{\r外文}I'll be right back.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:19.82,1:02:21.45,中文,,0,0,0,,等等 你去哪儿\N{\r外文}Wait a second, where are you going?
Dialogue: 0,1:02:21.53,1:02:23.99,中文,,0,0,0,,我下楼去兑现支票\N{\r外文}I'm going downstairs to cash a cheque.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:25.08,1:02:28.83,中文,,0,0,0,,你想旅馆能在早晨3点能给你 兑现1000美元支票\N{\r外文}You think this hotel is going to cash a $1,000 cheque at 3:00 a.m.?
Dialogue: 0,1:02:32.17,1:02:35.67,中文,,0,0,0,,是张纽约储蓄和贷款支票 像金子一样 他们会给兑现的\N{\r外文}It's a New York Savings and Loan cheque. It's like gold. They'll cash it.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:36.09,1:02:39.55,中文,,0,0,0,,你不觉得他们可能会产生点怀疑吗 让我看看\N{\r外文}Don't you think they might get a little suspicious? Let me see that.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:41.80,1:02:44.76,中文,,0,0,0,,是银行开出的支票 给我背书\N{\r外文}It's a cashier's cheque. Endorse it over to me.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:44.85,1:02:46.35,中文,,0,0,0,,我不能那么做\N{\r外文}I couldn't do that.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:46.43,1:02:49.85,中文,,0,0,0,,这张支票是1400美元的 我们谈好的价是1000美元\N{\r外文}This cheque is for 1,400. We agreed upon 1,000.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:51.31,1:02:54.02,中文,,0,0,0,,为什么我不能给你400美元\N{\r外文}Why don't I give you back 400
Dialogue: 0,1:02:54.81,1:02:56.98,中文,,0,0,0,,然后你给我那支票呢\N{\r外文}and you give me that cheque?
Dialogue: 0,1:02:58.32,1:02:59.69,中文,,0,0,0,,那更好\N{\r外文}Even better.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:31.73,1:03:33.69,中文,,0,0,0,,这是谁的吗\N{\r外文}Does this belong to anybody?
Dialogue: 0,1:03:50.37,1:03:52.25,中文,,0,0,0,,我是汉莱提 圣诞快乐\N{\r外文}This is Hanratty. Merry Christmas.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:52.37,1:03:53.75,中文,,0,0,0,,你好 卡尔\N{\r外文}Hello, Carl.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:54.54,1:03:55.67,中文,,0,0,0,,你好\N{\r外文}Hello.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:57.92,1:04:00.25,中文,,0,0,0,,巴里·艾伦 情报局的\N{\r外文}Barry Allen, Secret Service.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:01.17,1:04:05.01,中文,,0,0,0,,这几个小时我一直在找你\N{\r外文}I've been trying to track you down now for the last couple of hours.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:05.13,1:04:06.26,中文,,0,0,0,,你想要什么\N{\r外文}What do you want?
Dialogue: 0,1:04:07.09,1:04:10.77,中文,,0,0,0,,我想为在洛杉矶发生的事向你道歉\N{\r外文}I wanted to apologise for what happened out in Los Angeles.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:12.10,1:04:14.27,中文,,0,0,0,,不 不要向我道歉\N{\r外文}No, you don't apologise to me.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:14.85,1:04:17.23,中文,,0,0,0,,你平安夜也总是在工作吗\N{\r外文}Do you always work on Christmas Eve, Carl?
Dialogue: 0,1:04:17.61,1:04:19.52,中文,,0,0,0,,我自愿\N{\r外文}I volunteered
Dialogue: 0,1:04:19.77,1:04:21.73,中文,,0,0,0,,所以有家的人可以早点回家了\N{\r外文}so the men with families could go home early.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:22.61,1:04:24.82,中文,,0,0,0,,好像你戴着个结婚戒指来的\N{\r外文}Looked like you were wearing a wedding ring out in Los Angeles.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:24.90,1:04:26.70,中文,,0,0,0,,我以为你有家呢\N{\r外文}I thought maybe you had a family.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:27.03,1:04:28.53,中文,,0,0,0,,没有家\N{\r外文}No. No family.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:30.37,1:04:34.00,中文,,0,0,0,,你想跟我谈谈吗 我们见面谈吧\N{\r外文}You want to talk to me? Let's talk face to face.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:34.29,1:04:35.58,中文,,0,0,0,,好吧\N{\r外文}All right.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:35.66,1:04:39.34,中文,,0,0,0,,我在斯戴弗桑阿姆斯的办公室 3113房间\N{\r外文}I'm at my suite at the Stuyvesant Arms, room 3113.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:39.79,1:04:42.92,中文,,0,0,0,,上午我要出发去拉斯韦加斯度周末\N{\r外文}In the morning, I leave for Las Vegas for the weekend.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:45.22,1:04:47.64,中文,,0,0,0,,你想再耍我一次吗\N{\r外文}You think you're going to get me again?
Dialogue: 0,1:04:48.26,1:04:51.89,中文,,0,0,0,,你不去韦加斯 你也不在斯戴弗桑阿姆斯\N{\r外文}You're not going to Vegas, you're not in the Stuyvesant Arms.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:52.81,1:04:57.94,中文,,0,0,0,,你想让我派20名特工 在平安夜 冲进你的旅馆\N{\r外文}You'd love for me to send out 20 agents, Christmas Eve, barge into your hotel,
Dialogue: 0,1:04:58.23,1:05:00.61,中文,,0,0,0,,撞开你的门 所以你可以耍我们大家\N{\r外文}knock down the door so you can make fools out of us all.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:01.32,1:05:04.65,中文,,0,0,0,,如果我耍弄了你我真的很抱歉 真的\N{\r外文}I'm really sorry if I made a fool out of you. I really am.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:06.11,1:05:09.12,中文,,0,0,0,,不 你不要对我有歉意\N{\r外文}No. You do not feel sorry for me.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:09.49,1:05:13.83,中文,,0,0,0,,事实上 我知道是你 我没有给你戴上手铐 但我知道\N{\r外文}The truth is, I knew it was you. I didn't get the cuffs on you, but I knew.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:14.91,1:05:17.83,中文,,0,0,0,,人们只知道你告诉他们的 卡尔\N{\r外文}People only know what you tell them, Carl.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:18.92,1:05:21.96,中文,,0,0,0,,那么你告诉我 巴里·艾伦 情报局的\N{\r外文}Then tell me this, Barry Allen, Secret Service.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:22.50,1:05:25.26,中文,,0,0,0,,你怎么知道我不会看你的钱包\N{\r外文}How did you know I wouldn't look in your wallet?
Dialogue: 0,1:05:25.34,1:05:28.34,中文,,0,0,0,,与杨基队为什么总赢一样的道理\N{\r外文}The same reason the Yankees always win.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:28.47,1:05:31.60,中文,,0,0,0,,没有人能把眼睛从条纹衣服上移开\N{\r外文}Nobody can keep their eyes off the pinstripes.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:31.85,1:05:34.52,中文,,0,0,0,,杨基对能赢是因为有了米基·曼托\N{\r外文}The Yankees win because they have Mickey Mantle.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:34.60,1:05:36.85,中文,,0,0,0,,从来没有人对他们的服装下赌注\N{\r外文}No one ever bets on the uniform.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:37.60,1:05:39.65,中文,,0,0,0,,你肯定这点吗 卡尔\N{\r外文}You sure about that, Carl?
Dialogue: 0,1:05:39.81,1:05:42.02,中文,,0,0,0,,我告诉你我能肯定什么\N{\r外文}I'll tell you what I am sure of.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:42.15,1:05:44.02,中文,,0,0,0,,你肯定是要被抓住的\N{\r外文}You're going to get caught.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:44.69,1:05:48.32,中文,,0,0,0,,这样或是那样 只是个数学问题 就像韦加斯\N{\r外文}One way or another, it's a mathematical fact. It's like Vegas.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:48.45,1:05:50.20,中文,,0,0,0,,总是庄家赢\N{\r外文}The house always wins.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:55.66,1:05:59.17,中文,,0,0,0,,卡尔 对不起 我得结束谈话了\N{\r外文}Well, Carl, I'm sorry, but I have to go.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:00.62,1:06:03.29,中文,,0,0,0,,你打电话不只是为了道歉 对吗\N{\r外文}You didn't call just to apologise, did you?
Dialogue: 0,1:06:04.55,1:06:05.80,中文,,0,0,0,,你什么意思\N{\r外文}What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,1:06:07.55,1:06:09.59,中文,,0,0,0,,你没别人可打电话\N{\r外文}You have no one else to call.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:47.09,1:06:48.63,中文,,0,0,0,,还要咖啡吗 先生\N{\r外文}More coffee, sir?
Dialogue: 0,1:06:50.88,1:06:53.14,中文,,0,0,0,,巴里·艾伦
Dialogue: 0,1:06:54.97,1:06:57.77,中文,,0,0,0,,你收集吗 收集什么\N{\r外文}Are you a collector? Of what?
Dialogue: 0,1:06:57.85,1:06:59.18,中文,,0,0,0,,《宇宙之光的俘虏》\N{\r外文}Captives of the Cosmic Ray,
Dialogue: 0,1:06:59.27,1:07:01.23,中文,,0,0,0,,《金色巨人之地》\N{\r外文}The Big Freeze, Land of the Golden Giants.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:01.31,1:07:03.94,中文,,0,0,0,,我都收集全了 你在说什么\N{\r外文}I've got them all. What are you talking about?
Dialogue: 0,1:07:04.69,1:07:05.94,中文,,0,0,0,,巴里·艾伦\N{\r外文}Barry Allen.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:09.11,1:07:10.15,中文,,0,0,0,,"闪电"\N{\r外文}The Flash.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:12.45,1:07:13.78,中文,,0,0,0,,等等 孩子\N{\r外文}Wait, kid.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:16.37,1:07:17.99,中文,,0,0,0,,你指 就像这本喜剧书\N{\r外文}You mean, like the comic book?
Dialogue: 0,1:07:18.08,1:07:21.12,中文,,0,0,0,,对 当他不是"闪电" 那就是他的名字 巴里·艾伦\N{\r外文}Yeah, the comic book. When he's not The Flash, that's his name, Barry Allen.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:22.96,1:07:24.33,中文,,0,0,0,,谢谢\N{\r外文}Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:28.25,1:07:31.09,中文,,0,0,0,,听清楚了 他读喜剧书\N{\r外文}Now get this, he reads comic books!
Dialogue: 0,1:07:31.51,1:07:33.88,中文,,0,0,0,,喜剧书 巴里·艾伦是"闪电"\N{\r外文}Comic books! Barry Allen is The Flash!
Dialogue: 0,1:07:33.97,1:07:36.05,中文,,0,0,0,,慢点儿 你在说什么呢\N{\r外文}Carl, slow down. I don't know what the hell you're talking about.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:36.14,1:07:38.22,中文,,0,0,0,,我们的目标是个孩子\N{\r外文}He's a kid. Our unsub is a kid.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:38.31,1:07:41.23,中文,,0,0,0,,怪不得我们对不上他的指纹 他没有犯罪记录\N{\r外文}That's why we couldn't match his prints, that's why he doesn't have a record.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:41.31,1:07:43.39,中文,,0,0,0,,联系纽约警察局\N{\r外文}I want you to contact NYPD for every
Dialogue: 0,1:07:43.48,1:07:46.27,中文,,0,0,0,,查一下所有离家出走的年轻人的情况\N{\r外文}all-points juvenile runaways in New York City.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:46.36,1:07:49.78,中文,,0,0,0,,别忘了飞机场 他到处洒支票\N{\r外文}Don't forget the airports. He's been kiting cheques all over the country.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:49.86,1:07:51.94,中文,,0,0,0,,为什么是纽约 杨基队\N{\r外文}Why New York? The Yankees!
Dialogue: 0,1:07:52.03,1:07:54.49,中文,,0,0,0,,他说过杨基队的事情\N{\r外文}He said something about the Yankees!
Dialogue: 0,1:07:57.03,1:07:58.49,中文,,0,0,0,,我们到名单哪儿了\N{\r外文}Where are we on the list?
Dialogue: 0,1:07:58.58,1:08:01.12,中文,,0,0,0,,53号 阿巴戈内尔\N{\r外文}Number 53, Abagnale.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:04.37,1:08:06.96,中文,,0,0,0,,早晨好 我们是打电话的联邦调查局特工\N{\r外文}Good morning, ma'am, we're the F.B.I. agents who called.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:07.04,1:08:08.17,中文,,0,0,0,,对 我在等你们\N{\r外文}Yes, I've been waiting.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:08.84,1:08:11.84,中文,,0,0,0,,我想你们都饿了 我正在解冻沙拉丽蛋糕\N{\r外文}I hope you're all hungry. I put out the Sara Lee.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:15.26,1:08:17.26,中文,,0,0,0,,我的丈夫杰克是名律师\N{\r外文}My husband, Jack, is a lawyer.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:17.34,1:08:19.97,中文,,0,0,0,,你的第一任丈夫怎样了 阿巴戈内里太太\N{\r外文}What about your first husband, Mrs Abagnale?
Dialogue: 0,1:08:20.06,1:08:23.68,中文,,0,0,0,,阿巴戈内尔 但我喜欢被称为巴恩斯\N{\r外文}Abagnale. But I prefer to be called Barnes.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:25.69,1:08:28.77,中文,,0,0,0,,"弗兰克·威廉·阿巴戈内尔" 据说他服过役\N{\r外文}"Frank William Abagnale." It says he was in the service.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:28.86,1:08:30.94,中文,,0,0,0,,你们是在大战时认识的\N{\r外文}Did you two meet during the war?
Dialogue: 0,1:08:31.78,1:08:35.74,中文,,0,0,0,,对 我住在法国的一个很小的村庄里 叫曼沙\N{\r外文}Yeah, I lived in a very small village in France, Montrichard.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:36.16,1:08:39.66,中文,,0,0,0,,那种地方的人从来都没听说过沙拉丽 这样的蛋糕\N{\r外文}The kind of place where they never heard of Sara Lee.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:40.08,1:08:41.62,中文,,0,0,0,,请便\N{\r外文}Help yourselves.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:41.70,1:08:43.54,中文,,0,0,0,,没人喜欢沙拉丽\N{\r外文}Nobody doesn't like Sara Lee.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:43.62,1:08:45.12,中文,,0,0,0,,你填写过一份离家出走少年的失踪报告\N{\r外文}You filled out a missing person's report
Dialogue: 0,1:08:45.21,1:08:48.67,中文,,0,0,0,,小弗兰克·阿巴戈内尔\N{\r外文}for a runaway juvenile by the name of Frank Abagnale, Jr.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:49.21,1:08:50.46,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰基没事吧\N{\r外文}Is Frankie okay?
Dialogue: 0,1:08:51.42,1:08:52.96,中文,,0,0,0,,你知道他在美国大通银行的死账户上\N{\r外文}You're aware of the fact that he wrote some cheques
Dialogue: 0,1:08:53.05,1:08:55.26,中文,,0,0,0,,开支票吗\N{\r外文}on a closed account at Chase Manhattan Bank?
Dialogue: 0,1:08:55.34,1:08:58.80,中文,,0,0,0,,知道 警察认为他犯了某种罪\N{\r外文}Yes. The police think he's some type of criminal.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:58.89,1:09:01.35,中文,,0,0,0,,他犯的是重罪 巴恩斯太太\N{\r外文}What he did was a felony, Mrs Barnes.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:01.89,1:09:03.52,中文,,0,0,0,,一共才1000美元\N{\r外文}It was $1,000.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:04.27,1:09:08.10,中文,,0,0,0,,像他这么大的孩子有一半在吸毒 向警察扔石子\N{\r外文}Half the kids his age are on dope, throwing rocks at police.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:08.85,1:09:13.07,中文,,0,0,0,,就因为我的儿子犯了个小错误 他们都吓死我了\N{\r外文}And they scared me to death because my son made a little mistake.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:14.11,1:09:17.11,中文,,0,0,0,,一个17岁的孩子需要吃饭\N{\r外文}A 17-year-old boy has to eat,
Dialogue: 0,1:09:17.57,1:09:19.24,中文,,0,0,0,,需要找个地方睡觉\N{\r外文}has to have a place to sleep.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:19.49,1:09:21.37,中文,,0,0,0,,我们理解 夫人\N{\r外文}We understand, ma'am.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:22.03,1:09:23.58,中文,,0,0,0,,有你儿子的照片吗\N{\r外文}Would you happen to have a picture of your son?
Dialogue: 0,1:09:23.87,1:09:25.58,中文,,0,0,0,,有 我有他的旧年册\N{\r外文}Yes, I have his old yearbook.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:30.46,1:09:32.17,中文,,0,0,0,,小弗兰克
Dialogue: 0,1:09:35.30,1:09:36.34,中文,,0,0,0,,好\N{\r外文}Okay.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:38.68,1:09:41.35,中文,,0,0,0,,我们要给所有部门发电传\N{\r外文}We need to send out an all-office teletype.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:41.43,1:09:44.93,中文,,0,0,0,,我们的嫌疑犯叫小弗兰克·阿巴戈内尔 17岁\N{\r外文}Our unsub's name is Frank Abagnale, Jr., age 17!
Dialogue: 0,1:09:45.02,1:09:47.27,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰基没事吧 他有麻烦了吗\N{\r外文}Is Frankie okay? Is he in trouble?
Dialogue: 0,1:09:47.35,1:09:50.23,中文,,0,0,0,,抱歉我得告诉你 你的儿子在伪造支票\N{\r外文}Ma'am, I'm sorry to have to tell you, your son is forging checks.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:50.31,1:09:53.32,中文,,0,0,0,,伪造支票 等等 我们肯定能赔偿\N{\r外文}Forging checks? Wait! I'm sure we can take care of that.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:53.40,1:09:55.40,中文,,0,0,0,,我在教堂做半日工\N{\r外文}I'm working part-time at the church now.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:55.48,1:09:57.99,中文,,0,0,0,,告诉我他欠多少 我还给你们\N{\r外文}Just tell me how much he owes and I'll pay you back.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:58.07,1:10:00.41,中文,,0,0,0,,到目前为止 约130万美元\N{\r外文}So far, it's about $1.3 million.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:12.05,1:10:16.01,中文,,0,0,0,,河湾公寓 亚特兰大市 佐治亚州
Dialogue: 0,1:10:17.97,1:10:19.55,中文,,0,0,0,,嗨 梅勒妮\N{\r外文}Hi, Melanie, how are you?
Dialogue: 0,1:10:19.63,1:10:22.14,中文,,0,0,0,,在室内时用烟灰缸\N{\r外文}When you're in the house, please use an ashtray.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:22.22,1:10:23.97,中文,,0,0,0,,这奶油真好\N{\r外文}Frank, this fondue is so good!
Dialogue: 0,1:10:24.05,1:10:26.93,中文,,0,0,0,,很好 拿着 好 我喜欢摩埃特\N{\r外文}Great. Take this. Good, I love Moët!
Dialogue: 0,1:10:35.32,1:10:39.49,中文,,0,0,0,,詹姆斯 求你了 离那音响远点\N{\r外文}James, please! Stay away from the hi-fi system, all right?
Dialogue: 0,1:10:39.57,1:10:42.49,中文,,0,0,0,,这是卷轴到卷轴的 你不能那样进带\N{\r外文}It's a reel-to-reel, you can't wind it like that.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:45.49,1:10:48.58,中文,,0,0,0,,天哪 特里 这可是意大利的编织\N{\r外文}Christ, Terry! This is Italian knit!
Dialogue: 0,1:10:48.66,1:10:51.29,中文,,0,0,0,,看你往哪儿去 只不过是件衬衫 伙计\N{\r外文}Watch where you're going! It's just a shirt, man!
Dialogue: 0,1:10:51.37,1:10:53.38,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰克 快过来\N{\r外文}Frank! Come quick!
Dialogue: 0,1:10:54.08,1:10:57.30,中文,,0,0,0,,郎斯调到聊天室里了\N{\r外文}Lance just fell into the conversation pit!
Dialogue: 0,1:11:02.84,1:11:05.43,中文,,0,0,0,,对不起 你知道兰斯·埃坡巴姆在哪儿吗\N{\r外文}Excuse me, you know where Lance Applebaum is?
Dialogue: 0,1:11:05.51,1:11:06.64,中文,,0,0,0,,谢谢\N{\r外文}Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:07.64,1:11:09.85,中文,,0,0,0,,这些瓶子一定要贴上标签\N{\r外文}These bottles need to be labelled when you pick them up!
Dialogue: 0,1:11:09.93,1:11:12.23,中文,,0,0,0,,你知道这有多危险吗\N{\r外文}Do you understand how dangerous this is? Do you?
Dialogue: 0,1:11:12.31,1:11:15.56,中文,,0,0,0,,不要只是哭 要点头 跟我说你不再这样了\N{\r外文}Don't stand there crying. Nod your head. Tell me you won't do it again.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:15.65,1:11:17.78,中文,,0,0,0,,现在擦干眼泪去工作吧\N{\r外文}Now dry up and get back to work.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:24.32,1:11:25.37,中文,,0,0,0,,没事吧\N{\r外文}You okay?
Dialogue: 0,1:11:26.33,1:11:28.83,中文,,0,0,0,,他叫我去采血 我就做了\N{\r外文}He told me to pick up the blood, so I did.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:28.91,1:11:31.08,中文,,0,0,0,,但他从没告诉过我要贴标签\N{\r外文}But he never told me to label it.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:32.46,1:11:34.46,中文,,0,0,0,,没关系 不要哭了\N{\r外文}It's okay, stop crying.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:34.88,1:11:36.29,中文,,0,0,0,,你叫什么名字\N{\r外文}What's your name?
Dialogue: 0,1:11:37.25,1:11:38.55,中文,,0,0,0,,布伦达\N{\r外文}Brenda.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:41.17,1:11:43.34,中文,,0,0,0,,布伦达 我不会介意它的\N{\r外文}Brenda, I wouldn't worry about it.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:43.43,1:11:45.84,中文,,0,0,0,,这些大夫并不是什么都知道\N{\r外文}These doctors don't know everything.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:46.60,1:11:48.39,中文,,0,0,0,,这是我第一周上班\N{\r外文}It's my first week.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:48.68,1:11:50.52,中文,,0,0,0,,我想他们要解雇我了\N{\r外文}I think they're going to fire me.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:50.60,1:11:53.52,中文,,0,0,0,,不会的 没有人会解雇你的\N{\r外文}No, nobody's going to fire you, Brenda.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:53.89,1:11:55.90,中文,,0,0,0,,我想你会干得很好\N{\r外文}I bet you're good at your job.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:57.02,1:11:58.52,中文,,0,0,0,,不 我不会\N{\r外文}No, I'm not.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:59.57,1:12:01.99,中文,,0,0,0,,我想如果我求你帮我查一下\N{\r外文}I bet if I asked you to check on the status
Dialogue: 0,1:12:02.07,1:12:03.78,中文,,0,0,0,,我朋友兰斯·埃坡巴姆的状况\N{\r外文}of my friend Lance Applebaum,
Dialogue: 0,1:12:04.61,1:12:07.32,中文,,0,0,0,,你会很快帮我做到的\N{\r外文}you could do that for me in a second.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:14.87,1:12:17.75,中文,,0,0,0,,埃坡巴姆先生踝骨骨折\N{\r外文}Mr Applebaum fractured his ankle.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:17.84,1:12:21.55,中文,,0,0,0,,阿什兰德大夫在7号检查室给他治疗\N{\r外文}Dr Ashland is treating him in exam room seven.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:21.63,1:12:24.09,中文,,0,0,0,,你看 没问题吧\N{\r外文}You see that? No problem.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:26.26,1:12:28.55,中文,,0,0,0,,这是急诊图表\N{\r外文}This is the emergency chart.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:29.14,1:12:33.02,中文,,0,0,0,,看见那个蓝色的星了吗 那表示病人已经被诊断\N{\r外文}See that blue star? That means the patient has been diagnosed.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:33.10,1:12:37.56,中文,,0,0,0,,给他治疗后 再在这里画个红圈 明白吗\N{\r外文}And then after he's been treated, we put a red circle here. See?
Dialogue: 0,1:12:38.90,1:12:41.19,中文,,0,0,0,,你觉得那些牙套怎么样\N{\r外文}How do you like those braces?
Dialogue: 0,1:12:42.65,1:12:44.24,中文,,0,0,0,,我看它们挺好\N{\r外文}I guess they're all right.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:44.95,1:12:47.07,中文,,0,0,0,,我去年把我的摘下来了\N{\r外文}I got mine off last year.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:47.99,1:12:50.62,中文,,0,0,0,,天啊 我讨厌它们 只是里边的牙\N{\r外文}Boy, I hated them. They were bottoms.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:50.83,1:12:53.04,中文,,0,0,0,,我还得戴我的护牙\N{\r外文}I still got to wear my mouth guard.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:53.91,1:12:55.75,中文,,0,0,0,,你的牙确实很好\N{\r外文}You have really nice teeth.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:57.54,1:12:59.25,中文,,0,0,0,,谢谢\N{\r外文}Well, thank you.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:59.63,1:13:01.88,中文,,0,0,0,,你笑得很美\N{\r外文}And you have a pretty smile.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:05.38,1:13:09.34,中文,,0,0,0,,不 我是认真的 我真觉得你戴牙套看上去挺好\N{\r外文}No, I mean it. I really think those braces look good on you.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:09.55,1:13:10.97,中文,,0,0,0,,谢谢\N{\r外文}Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:11.14,1:13:12.47,中文,,0,0,0,,不客气\N{\r外文}You're welcome.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:16.18,1:13:17.19,中文,,0,0,0,,布伦达\N{\r外文}Brenda.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:17.48,1:13:18.69,中文,,0,0,0,,什么\N{\r外文}Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:18.85,1:13:21.65,中文,,0,0,0,,这医院在招人吗\N{\r外文}Do you know if they're hiring here at the hospital?
Dialogue: 0,1:13:23.15,1:13:25.86,中文,,0,0,0,,我不能确定 你想干什么\N{\r外文}I'm not sure. What do you want to do?
Dialogue: 0,1:13:27.91,1:13:29.36,中文,,0,0,0,,我是大夫\N{\r外文}I'm a doctor.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:33.16,1:13:34.83,中文,,0,0,0,,亲爱的爸爸\N{\r外文}Dear Dad,
Dialogue: 0,1:13:34.91,1:13:37.62,中文,,0,0,0,,我决定把原来的工作放下一段时间\N{\r外文}I decided to get off the road for a while.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:37.71,1:13:41.63,中文,,0,0,0,,我找了个医院的夜班工作 遇到了一些很好的人\N{\r外文}I've taken a night job at a hospital and met some really nice people.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:41.71,1:13:45.67,中文,,0,0,0,,感觉真好 每天晚上能踏踏实实地睡在同一张床上\N{\r外文}Feels good to have my feet on the ground, to wake up in the same bed every night.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:45.98,1:13:46.70,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰克·考纳斯
Dialogue: 0,1:13:47.05,1:13:50.84,中文,,0,0,0,,天知道 可能我还要找个人结婚\N{\r外文}Who knows, maybe I'll even find someone to settle down with.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:53.68,1:13:56.77,中文,,0,0,0,,"哈佛医学院" 全班成绩前茅\N{\r外文}"Harvard Medical School." Top of your class.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:57.85,1:14:00.60,中文,,0,0,0,,"南加州儿童医院"\N{\r外文}"Southern California Children's Hospital."
Dialogue: 0,1:14:01.10,1:14:04.44,中文,,0,0,0,,真是很吸引人的简历 考纳斯大夫\N{\r外文}That is a pretty impressive résumé, Dr Conners.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:04.73,1:14:06.40,中文,,0,0,0,,不幸的是\N{\r外文}Unfortunately,
Dialogue: 0,1:14:07.03,1:14:09.11,中文,,0,0,0,,我需要的只是\N{\r外文}the only thing I need is
Dialogue: 0,1:14:09.36,1:14:13.49,中文,,0,0,0,,半夜到早晨8点的夜班急诊室主管\N{\r外文}an emergency room supervisor for my midnight to 8:00 a.m. shift.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:14.74,1:14:17.87,中文,,0,0,0,,一个照看6名实习生和20名护士的人\N{\r外文}Someone to babysit six interns and 20 nurses.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:18.87,1:14:20.37,中文,,0,0,0,,但是\N{\r外文}But...
Dialogue: 0,1:14:22.04,1:14:25.38,中文,,0,0,0,,说到底 我想你会感兴趣的\N{\r外文}Hell, I doubt that you'd be interested in that.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:28.22,1:14:31.39,中文,,0,0,0,,过去他们总是挑选我自己的护士\N{\r外文}In the past, they've always let me choose my own nurses.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:32.93,1:14:34.22,中文,,0,0,0,,考纳利大夫\N{\r外文}Dr Connelly.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:35.72,1:14:37.31,中文,,0,0,0,,哈里斯大夫 在\N{\r外文}Dr Harris. Present.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:38.39,1:14:39.56,中文,,0,0,0,,阿什兰大夫\N{\r外文}Dr Ashland.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:39.64,1:14:41.06,中文,,0,0,0,,考纳斯大夫\N{\r外文}Dr Conners?
Dialogue: 0,1:14:41.77,1:14:43.73,中文,,0,0,0,,你每天晚上都要检查出勤吗\N{\r外文}You gonna take roll every night?
Dialogue: 0,1:14:43.81,1:14:45.77,中文,,0,0,0,,是的 我要 阿什兰大夫\N{\r外文}Yes, I will, Dr Ashland.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:45.90,1:14:49.19,中文,,0,0,0,,如果你要迟到了 我建议你带假条来\N{\r外文}And if you're going to be late, I suggest you bring a note.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:52.74,1:14:54.24,中文,,0,0,0,,巴斯曼小姐\N{\r外文}Miss Basmann.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:54.74,1:14:56.16,中文,,0,0,0,,梅斯小姐\N{\r外文}Miss Mace.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:56.83,1:14:58.33,中文,,0,0,0,,斯特朗小姐\N{\r外文}Miss Strong.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:58.58,1:14:59.66,中文,,0,0,0,,到\N{\r外文}Here.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:59.75,1:15:01.08,中文,,0,0,0,,布朗护士\N{\r外文}Nurse Brown.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:02.25,1:15:03.58,中文,,0,0,0,,桑福德护士\N{\r外文}Nurse Sanford.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:04.00,1:15:06.55,中文,,0,0,0,,每4小时30毫克可待因\N{\r外文}Thirty milligrams of codeine every four hours.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:06.63,1:15:10.47,中文,,0,0,0,,每分钟60滴血浆 直到我们算出需要量\N{\r外文}Run the plasma at 60 drops a minute till we calculate the fluid requirements.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:10.59,1:15:14.14,中文,,0,0,0,,你估计这烫伤的程度和面积有多少 基达尔\N{\r外文}What do you estimate the degree and extent of the burns, Kildare?
Dialogue: 0,1:15:14.26,1:15:17.43,中文,,0,0,0,,2度和3度烫伤 面积超过皮肤总面积的20%\N{\r外文}Second and third-degree burns over about 20% of the body surface.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:17.51,1:15:18.89,中文,,0,0,0,,你同意吗 我同意\N{\r外文}Do you concur? I concur.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:18.97,1:15:20.43,中文,,0,0,0,,把他送到小儿科去吧\N{\r外文}Let's get him up to Paediatrics.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:22.02,1:15:23.19,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰克·考纳斯
Dialogue: 0,1:15:27.69,1:15:28.78,中文,,0,0,0,,嗨 布伦达\N{\r外文}Hello, Brenda.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:28.86,1:15:30.28,中文,,0,0,0,,嗨 考纳斯大夫\N{\r外文}Hi, Dr Conners.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:30.94,1:15:33.53,中文,,0,0,0,,你需要在这里签字 谢谢\N{\r外文}You need to sign these. Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:40.70,1:15:42.66,中文,,0,0,0,,看我有什么变化吗\N{\r外文}Do you notice anything different about me?
Dialogue: 0,1:15:42.75,1:15:44.92,中文,,0,0,0,,你摘掉牙套了\N{\r外文}You got your braces off! Come here.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:45.00,1:15:47.50,中文,,0,0,0,,我整晚都一直在想让你看看\N{\r外文}I've been trying to show you all night!
Dialogue: 0,1:15:50.21,1:15:51.55,中文,,0,0,0,,做得好\N{\r外文}Good job.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:51.63,1:15:54.47,中文,,0,0,0,,摘牙套时痛吗 我当时感觉很特别\N{\r外文}Did it hurt when they took them off? Mine felt so weird after.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:54.55,1:15:57.47,中文,,0,0,0,,我总是用舌头舔牙 我控制不住\N{\r外文}I keep rubbing my tongue over them. I can't stop!
Dialogue: 0,1:15:57.68,1:15:59.06,中文,,0,0,0,,它们可真滑\N{\r外文}They're so slippery.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:59.14,1:16:02.31,中文,,0,0,0,,感觉很好 是吗 是的 感觉好极了\N{\r外文}It feels good, doesn't it? Yeah, it feels incredible.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:12.57,1:16:13.90,中文,,0,0,0,,噢 天\N{\r外文}Oh, my!
Dialogue: 0,1:16:15.24,1:16:16.66,中文,,0,0,0,,对不起\N{\r外文}I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:28.50,1:16:31.80,中文,,0,0,0,,考纳斯大夫到急诊室\N{\r外文}Dr Conners to the E.R. Dr Conners to the E.R.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:31.88,1:16:33.01,中文,,0,0,0,,你不去吗\N{\r外文}Shouldn't you go?
Dialogue: 0,1:16:33.09,1:16:37.72,中文,,0,0,0,,不去 急诊病房有位大夫 我们不会被打扰\N{\r外文}No. They have a staff doctor in the emergency ward, we'll be fine.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:44.02,1:16:45.94,中文,,0,0,0,,他要是正在手术怎么办\N{\r外文}What if he's in surgery?
Dialogue: 0,1:16:47.85,1:16:49.44,中文,,0,0,0,,你真的认为我得去吗\N{\r外文}Do you really think I have to go?
Dialogue: 0,1:16:50.02,1:16:51.78,中文,,0,0,0,,在这里边 考纳斯大夫\N{\r外文}In here, Dr Conners.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:08.92,1:17:12.38,中文,,0,0,0,,先生们 是什么问题\N{\r外文}Gentlemen, what seems to be the problem?
Dialogue: 0,1:17:13.09,1:17:17.63,中文,,0,0,0,,脚踏车意外 膝盖骨下大约13厘米处胫骨骨折\N{\r外文}Bicycle accident. A fractured tibia about five inches below the patella.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:22.76,1:17:24.22,中文,,0,0,0,,哈里斯大夫\N{\r外文}Dr Harris.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:24.81,1:17:26.39,中文,,0,0,0,,你同意吗\N{\r外文}Do you concur?
Dialogue: 0,1:17:27.06,1:17:28.98,中文,,0,0,0,,同意什么 先生\N{\r外文}Concur with what, sir?
Dialogue: 0,1:17:29.65,1:17:32.82,中文,,0,0,0,,同意阿什兰大夫刚才说的 你同意吗\N{\r外文}With what Dr Ashland just said. Do you concur?
Dialogue: 0,1:17:34.99,1:17:37.90,中文,,0,0,0,,嗯 是个脚踏车意外 这孩子说的\N{\r外文}Well, it was a bicycle accident. The boy told us.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:38.99,1:17:40.28,中文,,0,0,0,,所以你同意\N{\r外文}So you concur?
Dialogue: 0,1:17:41.95,1:17:45.62,中文,,0,0,0,,我们应该给他照X光 缝合伤口 再给他打上石膏\N{\r外文}We should take an X-ray, stitch him up and put him in a walking cast.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:49.42,1:17:51.38,中文,,0,0,0,,很好 阿什兰大夫\N{\r外文}Very good, Dr Ashland. Very good.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:51.46,1:17:54.42,中文,,0,0,0,,我看 你们好像不太需要我\N{\r外文}Well, you don't seem to have much need for me.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:54.67,1:17:55.76,中文,,0,0,0,,继续\N{\r外文}Carry on.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:58.18,1:17:59.97,中文,,0,0,0,,我搞错了 是不是\N{\r外文}I blew it, didn't I?
Dialogue: 0,1:18:01.01,1:18:02.60,中文,,0,0,0,,我为什么没说同意呢\N{\r外文}Why didn't I concur?
Dialogue: 0,1:18:10.86,1:18:12.69,中文,,0,0,0,,看门人柜橱
Dialogue: 0,1:18:24.70,1:18:26.33,中文,,0,0,0,,请随便\N{\r外文}Make yourself at home!
Dialogue: 0,1:18:27.66,1:18:29.16,中文,,0,0,0,,老弗兰克·阿巴戈内尔\N{\r外文}Frank Abagnale, Sr.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:29.33,1:18:31.04,中文,,0,0,0,,你不是警察\N{\r外文}You're not a cop.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:32.50,1:18:34.79,中文,,0,0,0,,特工汉莱提 联邦调查局的\N{\r外文}Special Agent Hanratty, F.B.I.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:35.34,1:18:38.51,中文,,0,0,0,,你不是警察 我的房东说你不是警察\N{\r外文}You're not a cop. My landlord said you were not a cop.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:38.97,1:18:42.59,中文,,0,0,0,,如果你要拘捕我 我想换件衣服\N{\r外文}If you're going to arrest me, I'd like to put on a different suit.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:42.68,1:18:44.97,中文,,0,0,0,,如果可以的话 我不是来拘捕你的\N{\r外文}If that's okay... I'm not here to arrest you.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:45.06,1:18:47.35,中文,,0,0,0,,我是在抓你儿子 他有麻烦了\N{\r外文}I'm looking for your son. He's in trouble.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:47.47,1:18:49.14,中文,,0,0,0,,你知道他在哪里吗\N{\r外文}Do you know where he is?
Dialogue: 0,1:18:51.48,1:18:54.94,中文,,0,0,0,,如果我告诉你他在哪里 你能保证不告诉她妈吗\N{\r外文}If I tell you where he is, will you promise not to tell his mother?
Dialogue: 0,1:18:55.02,1:18:56.11,中文,,0,0,0,,当然\N{\r外文}Sure.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:57.32,1:19:01.40,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰克做了个假身份证参加海军了\N{\r外文}Frank made up a fake I.D. and enlisted in the Marine Corps.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:01.49,1:19:03.57,中文,,0,0,0,,他现在在越南\N{\r外文}He's over in Vietnam right now.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:03.66,1:19:05.74,中文,,0,0,0,,那孩子现在在地球那头\N{\r外文}That kid is halfway around the world,
Dialogue: 0,1:19:05.83,1:19:09.87,中文,,0,0,0,,在他妈的丛林里爬行 跟共产党打仗 所以\N{\r外文}crawling through the damn jungle, fighting the communists, so...
Dialogue: 0,1:19:11.33,1:19:15.34,中文,,0,0,0,,求你 不要到我家来 还把我儿子叫成罪犯\N{\r外文}Please, don't come to my home and call my boy a criminal...
Dialogue: 0,1:19:15.59,1:19:19.34,中文,,0,0,0,,我从来没说他是罪犯 我说他有麻烦了\N{\r外文}I never said he was a criminal, Mr Abagnale. I said he was in trouble.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:20.80,1:19:24.14,中文,,0,0,0,,如果你想给我打电话谈谈 这是号码\N{\r外文}If you'd like to give me a call and talk, here's my number.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:28.60,1:19:30.35,中文,,0,0,0,,亲爱的爸爸
Dialogue: 0,1:19:32.27,1:19:34.28,中文,,0,0,0,,河湾公寓 亚特兰大市 佐治亚州 30398
Dialogue: 0,1:19:36.56,1:19:38.53,中文,,0,0,0,,你不是位父亲 对吗\N{\r外文}You're not a father, are you?
Dialogue: 0,1:19:40.61,1:19:41.74,中文,,0,0,0,,什么\N{\r外文}Pardon me?
Dialogue: 0,1:19:41.86,1:19:44.16,中文,,0,0,0,,如果你是位父亲 你应该知道\N{\r外文}If you were a father, you'd know.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:44.24,1:19:49.70,中文,,0,0,0,,我永远也不会放弃我儿子的\N{\r外文}I would never give up my son. I would never give up my son.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:51.71,1:19:53.75,中文,,0,0,0,,是的 先生 我理解\N{\r外文}Yes, sir. I understand.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:54.71,1:19:56.54,中文,,0,0,0,,肖恩 记下这个\N{\r外文}Sean, now get this.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:57.04,1:20:03.84,中文,,0,0,0,,河湾公寓 兰德欧沃街415号 亚特兰大市 佐治亚州\N{\r外文}"Riverbend Apartments, 415 Landover, Atlanta, Georgia." Atlanta, Georgia.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:03.93,1:20:08.64,中文,,0,0,0,,我在去机场的路上 4小时后和小组会合 再见\N{\r外文}I'm on my way to the airport. I'll meet the team in four hours. Bye-bye!
Dialogue: 0,1:20:10.89,1:20:13.14,中文,,0,0,0,,好了 没关系的\N{\r外文}Come on, it's okay.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:14.14,1:20:15.73,中文,,0,0,0,,你不必哭\N{\r外文}You don't have to cry.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:16.06,1:20:20.48,中文,,0,0,0,,对不起 真对不起 弗兰克 我不能做\N{\r外文}I'm sorry! I'm so sorry, Frank! I can't do this.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:20.57,1:20:22.24,中文,,0,0,0,,布伦达 听我说\N{\r外文}Brenda, listen to me.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:23.24,1:20:25.36,中文,,0,0,0,,我不在乎你是处女\N{\r外文}I don't care if you're a virgin, all right?
Dialogue: 0,1:20:25.45,1:20:26.70,中文,,0,0,0,,我能等\N{\r外文}Really, I can wait.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:27.91,1:20:29.62,中文,,0,0,0,,我不是处女\N{\r外文}I'm not a virgin.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:34.08,1:20:36.50,中文,,0,0,0,,我2年前做了堕胎手术\N{\r外文}I had an abortion two years ago.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:40.09,1:20:42.59,中文,,0,0,0,,我父母找朋友做的\N{\r外文}My parents had a friend do it.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:43.09,1:20:46.30,中文,,0,0,0,,一个和我父亲一起玩高尔夫的人\N{\r外文}A man that my father plays golf with.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:47.80,1:20:51.01,中文,,0,0,0,,当我刚恢复好 他们就把我踢出了家门\N{\r外文}And when I got better, they kicked me out of the house.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:51.93,1:20:55.48,中文,,0,0,0,,我堕过胎 不再是他们的女儿了\N{\r外文}I had an abortion and I wasn't their daughter any more!
Dialogue: 0,1:20:56.31,1:20:59.27,中文,,0,0,0,,我很抱歉 请不要生我的气\N{\r外文}I'm so sorry. Please don't be mad at me.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:00.94,1:21:02.11,中文,,0,0,0,,不 不\N{\r外文}No, no.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:02.28,1:21:04.44,中文,,0,0,0,,请不要生我的气\N{\r外文}Please don't be mad at me.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:06.45,1:21:08.95,中文,,0,0,0,,我和你父母谈谈怎样\N{\r外文}What if I spoke to your parents?
Dialogue: 0,1:21:09.12,1:21:11.28,中文,,0,0,0,,也许能理顺关系\N{\r外文}Maybe I can straighten things out.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:11.37,1:21:14.95,中文,,0,0,0,,我一直在求他们 但他们还是不让我回家\N{\r外文}I ask them all the time, but they said I still can't come home.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:15.83,1:21:18.96,中文,,0,0,0,,我爸爸是律师\N{\r外文}And my daddy's a lawyer.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:27.34,1:21:28.51,中文,,0,0,0,,布伦达\N{\r外文}Brenda?
Dialogue: 0,1:21:31.14,1:21:33.85,中文,,0,0,0,,如果你和医生订婚会怎样\N{\r外文}What if you were engaged to a doctor?
Dialogue: 0,1:21:34.52,1:21:36.39,中文,,0,0,0,,那样会不会改变什么\N{\r外文}Would that change anything?
Dialogue: 0,1:21:36.48,1:21:37.73,中文,,0,0,0,,什么\N{\r外文}What?
Dialogue: 0,1:21:41.52,1:21:44.03,中文,,0,0,0,,我去你父母那里\N{\r外文}What if I went to your parents,
Dialogue: 0,1:21:45.49,1:21:47.82,中文,,0,0,0,,同你父亲谈谈\N{\r外文}and I spoke to your father
Dialogue: 0,1:21:51.07,1:21:53.70,中文,,0,0,0,,求他同意把你嫁给我 那会怎样\N{\r外文}and I asked permission to marry you?
Dialogue: 0,1:22:07.42,1:22:09.84,中文,,0,0,0,,是空的 没有人\N{\r外文}It's empty. Nobody here.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:23.44,1:22:26.53,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰克·考纳斯
Dialogue: 0,1:22:29.24,1:22:32.24,中文,,0,0,0,,新奥尔良
Dialogue: 0,1:22:33.87,1:22:36.20,中文,,0,0,0,,考纳斯大夫 你是路德教徒吗\N{\r外文}Dr Conners, are you Lutheran?
Dialogue: 0,1:22:37.70,1:22:39.46,中文,,0,0,0,,是 我是路德教徒\N{\r外文}Yes, I am a Lutheran.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:39.54,1:22:41.71,中文,,0,0,0,,但是请叫我弗兰克\N{\r外文}But please, call me Frank.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:43.04,1:22:45.71,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰克 你来祈祷好吗\N{\r外文}Frank, would you like to say grace?
Dialogue: 0,1:22:51.22,1:22:53.55,中文,,0,0,0,,除非你觉得不自在\N{\r外文}Unless you're not comfortable.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:53.89,1:22:55.31,中文,,0,0,0,,绝对可以\N{\r外文}Absolutely.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:05.82,1:23:08.90,中文,,0,0,0,,2只老鼠掉进奶油桶里\N{\r外文}Two little mice fell into a bucket of cream.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:10.74,1:23:12.82,中文,,0,0,0,,第1只老鼠很快放弃 被淹死了\N{\r外文}The first mouse quickly gave up and drowned,
Dialogue: 0,1:23:12.91,1:23:14.74,中文,,0,0,0,,但是第2只老鼠拼命努力\N{\r外文}but the second mouse struggled so hard
Dialogue: 0,1:23:14.82,1:23:17.45,中文,,0,0,0,,把奶油搅拌成黄油\N{\r外文}that he eventually churned that cream into butter,
Dialogue: 0,1:23:18.24,1:23:19.70,中文,,0,0,0,,它走了出来\N{\r外文}and he walked out.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:21.25,1:23:22.25,中文,,0,0,0,,阿门\N{\r外文}Amen.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:25.08,1:23:26.92,中文,,0,0,0,,很美\N{\r外文}That was beautiful.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:27.25,1:23:29.59,中文,,0,0,0,,老鼠把奶油搅拌成了黄油\N{\r外文}The mouse churned that cream into butter.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:32.76,1:23:33.97,中文,,0,0,0,,对\N{\r外文}That's right.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:35.30,1:23:36.72,中文,,0,0,0,,谢谢\N{\r外文}Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:36.80,1:23:39.93,中文,,0,0,0,,你有没有决定 想在新奥尔良的哪一家医院工作\N{\r外文}Frank, have you decided which hospital you want to work at in New Orleans?
Dialogue: 0,1:23:41.94,1:23:45.56,中文,,0,0,0,,说实在的 我在考虑回到法律这行\N{\r外文}To be quite honest, I'm thinking about getting back into law.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:46.36,1:23:49.11,中文,,0,0,0,,噢 天啊 你是医生还是律师\N{\r外文}Oh, my! Are you a doctor or a lawyer?
Dialogue: 0,1:23:49.94,1:23:53.36,中文,,0,0,0,,我去医学院之前 在加州通过了律师考试\N{\r外文}Before I went to medical school, I passed the bar in California.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:53.45,1:23:56.20,中文,,0,0,0,,我干了1年法律 后来我决定\N{\r外文}I practised law for one year, then I decided,
Dialogue: 0,1:23:56.45,1:23:58.99,中文,,0,0,0,,为什么不试试当个儿科医生呢\N{\r外文}why not try my hand at paediatrics?
Dialogue: 0,1:24:00.12,1:24:02.33,中文,,0,0,0,,你真让人惊奇\N{\r外文}You're just full of surprises.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:03.29,1:24:04.50,中文,,0,0,0,,是啊\N{\r外文}Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:05.54,1:24:08.88,中文,,0,0,0,,医生和律师 布伦达中大奖了\N{\r外文}A doctor and a lawyer. Brenda hit the jackpot.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:09.38,1:24:11.34,中文,,0,0,0,,你在哪儿上的法律学校\N{\r外文}Where did you go to law school?
Dialogue: 0,1:24:11.80,1:24:13.22,中文,,0,0,0,,伯克利\N{\r外文}Berkeley.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:15.72,1:24:17.68,中文,,0,0,0,,那不是你上学的地方吗 爸\N{\r外文}Oh, my gosh. Isn't that where you went, Daddy?
Dialogue: 0,1:24:17.80,1:24:19.43,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰克可以帮你工作\N{\r外文}Maybe Frank could come work for you, Roger.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:19.51,1:24:22.77,中文,,0,0,0,,你总是说找助理起诉员有多难\N{\r外文}You're always saying how hard it is to find assistant prosecutors.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:22.85,1:24:25.90,中文,,0,0,0,,他行吗 爸爸 他行吗 求你了\N{\r外文}Could he, Daddy? Could he, please? Could he come work with you, please?
Dialogue: 0,1:24:25.98,1:24:30.23,中文,,0,0,0,,那个狡猾的霍灵斯沃还在那儿教学吗\N{\r外文}Was that snake Hollingsworth still teaching there when you went through Berkeley?
Dialogue: 0,1:24:32.07,1:24:33.07,中文,,0,0,0,,霍灵斯沃\N{\r外文}Hollingsworth.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:33.15,1:24:35.49,中文,,0,0,0,,是的 坏脾气的老霍灵斯沃 对吗\N{\r外文}Yes. Grumpy old Hollingsworth, right?
Dialogue: 0,1:24:35.57,1:24:37.32,中文,,0,0,0,,脾气更坏了\N{\r外文}Meaner than ever.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:37.82,1:24:39.70,中文,,0,0,0,,还有他的狗呢\N{\r外文}And that dog of his?
Dialogue: 0,1:24:42.54,1:24:46.04,中文,,0,0,0,,告诉我 弗兰克 他的狗叫什么名字\N{\r外文}Tell me, Frank, what was the name of his little dog?
Dialogue: 0,1:24:55.68,1:24:57.09,中文,,0,0,0,,对不起\N{\r外文}I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:58.93,1:25:00.47,中文,,0,0,0,,狗死了\N{\r外文}The dog was dead.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:03.73,1:25:05.35,中文,,0,0,0,,真是不幸\N{\r外文}How unfortunate.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:06.77,1:25:07.85,中文,,0,0,0,,是\N{\r外文}Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:38.22,1:25:40.72,中文,,0,0,0,,医生 律师 路德教徒\N{\r外文}A doctor, a lawyer, a Lutheran.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:43.56,1:25:45.64,中文,,0,0,0,,那么 你是什么 弗兰克\N{\r外文}So, what are you, Frank?
Dialogue: 0,1:25:46.56,1:25:49.94,中文,,0,0,0,,因为你要跟我女儿结婚\N{\r外文}'Cause I think you're about to ask for my daughter's hand in marriage,
Dialogue: 0,1:25:50.06,1:25:51.52,中文,,0,0,0,,我有权利知道\N{\r外文}and I have a right to know.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:52.11,1:25:53.73,中文,,0,0,0,,知道什么 先生\N{\r外文}Know what, sir?
Dialogue: 0,1:25:54.32,1:25:55.74,中文,,0,0,0,,事实\N{\r外文}The truth.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:57.90,1:25:59.95,中文,,0,0,0,,告诉我事实 弗兰克\N{\r外文}Tell me the truth, Frank.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:01.32,1:26:03.41,中文,,0,0,0,,你在这儿做什么\N{\r外文}What are you doing here?
Dialogue: 0,1:26:05.16,1:26:08.08,中文,,0,0,0,,像你这样的人在和布伦达做什么\N{\r外文}What is a man like you doing with Brenda?
Dialogue: 0,1:26:09.67,1:26:13.13,中文,,0,0,0,,如果你想要我的祝福 如果你想要我的女儿\N{\r外文}If you want my blessing, if you want my daughter,
Dialogue: 0,1:26:13.50,1:26:15.67,中文,,0,0,0,,我想现在就听你说说\N{\r外文}I'd like to hear it from you now.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:18.42,1:26:20.18,中文,,0,0,0,,事实是 先生\N{\r外文}The truth is, sir...
Dialogue: 0,1:26:24.10,1:26:26.27,中文,,0,0,0,,事实就是\N{\r外文}The truth is that...
Dialogue: 0,1:26:28.77,1:26:31.31,中文,,0,0,0,,我不是医生 我不是律师\N{\r外文}I'm not a doctor, I'm not a lawyer.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:33.94,1:26:35.98,中文,,0,0,0,,我也不是飞行员\N{\r外文}I'm not an airline pilot.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:37.94,1:26:39.78,中文,,0,0,0,,我什么都不是 先生\N{\r外文}I'm nothing, really.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:46.99,1:26:50.12,中文,,0,0,0,,我只是个爱你女儿的孩子\N{\r外文}I'm just a kid who's in love with your daughter.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:52.38,1:26:53.50,中文,,0,0,0,,不对\N{\r外文}No.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:03.01,1:27:04.97,中文,,0,0,0,,你知道你是什么吗\N{\r外文}You know what you are?
Dialogue: 0,1:27:05.30,1:27:07.06,中文,,0,0,0,,你是个浪漫的人\N{\r外文}You're a romantic.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:07.18,1:27:10.18,中文,,0,0,0,,没有我们爱的女人 像我们这样的男人什么都不是\N{\r外文}Men like us are nothing without the women we love.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:10.31,1:27:13.90,中文,,0,0,0,,我必须承认 我也为有这样愚蠢的怪念头内疚\N{\r外文}I must confess, I'm guilty of the same foolish whimsy.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:13.98,1:27:16.11,中文,,0,0,0,,5次约会后\N{\r外文}I proposed to Carol after five dates
Dialogue: 0,1:27:16.19,1:27:18.99,中文,,0,0,0,,我向卡罗尔求婚 口袋空空\N{\r外文}with two nickels in my pockets and holes in my shoes
Dialogue: 0,1:27:19.07,1:27:20.99,中文,,0,0,0,,因为我知道她就是那个我要找的\N{\r外文}because I knew she was the one.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:21.99,1:27:23.74,中文,,0,0,0,,所以继续向前 弗兰克\N{\r外文}So go ahead, Frank.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:27.66,1:27:29.33,中文,,0,0,0,,不要害怕\N{\r外文}Don't be afraid.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:29.54,1:27:32.50,中文,,0,0,0,,提出你想跟我提的吧\N{\r外文}Ask the question you came here to ask me.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:37.67,1:27:41.17,中文,,0,0,0,,要想在新奥尔良当律师 我得做什么\N{\r外文}What would I have to do to take the bar here in New Orleans?
Dialogue: 0,1:27:46.10,1:27:48.10,中文,,0,0,0,,不 别的问题\N{\r外文}No, the other question.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:53.35,1:27:55.35,中文,,0,0,0,,穿过那门就是\N{\r外文}Right through that door.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:57.19,1:27:59.11,中文,,0,0,0,,祝你好运 考纳斯先生\N{\r外文}Good luck, Mr Conners.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:59.90,1:28:01.11,中文,,0,0,0,,谢谢\N{\r外文}Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:02.82,1:28:07.33,中文,,0,0,0,,1969年12月26日
Dialogue: 0,1:28:09.20,1:28:10.62,中文,,0,0,0,,嗨 弗兰克\N{\r外文}Hey, Frank.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:11.08,1:28:13.41,中文,,0,0,0,,你知道我一直没明白的是什么吗\N{\r外文}You know what I could never figure out?
Dialogue: 0,1:28:13.54,1:28:16.33,中文,,0,0,0,,你是怎么骗过律师考试的\N{\r外文}How did you cheat on the bar exam in Louisiana?
Dialogue: 0,1:28:16.42,1:28:18.04,中文,,0,0,0,,有什么区别\N{\r外文}What's the difference?
Dialogue: 0,1:28:18.13,1:28:22.13,中文,,0,0,0,,有人替你考试的 我要被长时间地关在监狱里\N{\r外文}Someone took the test for you? I'm going to prison for a long time.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:22.59,1:28:25.09,中文,,0,0,0,,说真的 有什么区别\N{\r外文}Seriously, what's the difference?
Dialogue: 0,1:28:25.47,1:28:27.47,中文,,0,0,0,,就是个简单的问题\N{\r外文}It's a simple question.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:28.55,1:28:31.06,中文,,0,0,0,,你吃那小饼吗\N{\r外文}Are you going to eat that éclair?
Dialogue: 0,1:28:32.73,1:28:35.39,中文,,0,0,0,,是啊 我留着以后吃\N{\r外文}Yeah. I'm saving it for later.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:36.44,1:28:38.44,中文,,0,0,0,,或者你想分点给我\N{\r外文}Or you want to split it with me?
Dialogue: 0,1:28:38.56,1:28:39.61,中文,,0,0,0,,不\N{\r外文}No.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:43.11,1:28:45.74,中文,,0,0,0,,把小饼给我一半我就告诉你\N{\r外文}Give me half that éclair and I'll tell you.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:56.58,1:28:59.17,中文,,0,0,0,,我早晚会想出来的\N{\r外文}I'm gonna figure it out sooner or later.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:05.80,1:29:09.35,中文,,0,0,0,,你在菲利浦·利戈比手下工作 负责企业法\N{\r外文}You'll be working under Phillip Rigby in corporate law.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:09.68,1:29:12.77,中文,,0,0,0,,你为什么不搬进来 布置一下办公桌\N{\r外文}Why don't you settle in, organise your desk?
Dialogue: 0,1:29:15.43,1:29:17.44,中文,,0,0,0,,我们12点30分\N{\r外文}We're having lunch at 12:30
Dialogue: 0,1:29:17.52,1:29:21.90,中文,,0,0,0,,与首席检察官和麦克森州长共进午餐 正是他本人\N{\r外文}with the Attorney General and Governor McKeithen himself.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:22.44,1:29:23.61,中文,,0,0,0,,州长\N{\r外文}A governor!
Dialogue: 0,1:29:23.69,1:29:25.32,中文,,0,0,0,,我们拼写得正确吗\N{\r外文}Did we spell it right?
Dialogue: 0,1:29:25.44,1:29:26.70,中文,,0,0,0,,非常对\N{\r外文}You sure did.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:27.03,1:29:28.53,中文,,0,0,0,,恭喜你\N{\r外文}Congratulations.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:28.61,1:29:30.49,中文,,0,0,0,,谢谢 先生 欢迎你\N{\r外文}Thank you, sir. Welcome aboard.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:38.21,1:29:40.96,中文,,0,0,0,,看这张照片 斯图尔特先生\N{\r外文}Look at this photograph, Mr Stewart.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:41.29,1:29:45.30,中文,,0,0,0,,这是张普林提斯约克的照片 就是在那他们发现他死了\N{\r外文}It's a photograph of Prentice York, where they found him, dead.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:45.72,1:29:48.63,中文,,0,0,0,,这是照片的局部放大\N{\r外文}Here is an enlargement of part of that photograph.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:49.01,1:29:52.64,中文,,0,0,0,,这是张被告在作废支票上签名的照片\N{\r外文}This is a photograph of the defendant's signature on a cancelled cheque.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:52.72,1:29:56.64,中文,,0,0,0,,这是同一个签名的局部放大 与\N{\r外文}Here is an enlargement of that same signature, which matches
Dialogue: 0,1:29:56.89,1:29:59.90,中文,,0,0,0,,他写给西蒙太太的信上的签名相吻合\N{\r外文}the signature on the letters that he wrote to Mrs Simon,
Dialogue: 0,1:29:59.98,1:30:04.19,中文,,0,0,0,,这就说明了他在路易斯安娜州行骗\N{\r外文}which discuss the possibility of defrauding the great state of Louisiana.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:04.32,1:30:07.15,中文,,0,0,0,,法官大人 陪审团的女士们 先生们\N{\r外文}Your Honour, ladies and gentlemen of the jury,
Dialogue: 0,1:30:07.24,1:30:11.53,中文,,0,0,0,,这就是不可辩驳的证据 说明被告确实在说谎\N{\r外文}this is irrefutable evidence that the defendant is, in fact, lying.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:17.50,1:30:21.46,中文,,0,0,0,,考纳斯先生 这是预审\N{\r外文}Mr Conners, this is a preliminary hearing.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:22.25,1:30:24.84,中文,,0,0,0,,没有被告\N{\r外文}There is no defendant.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:26.84,1:30:29.72,中文,,0,0,0,,没有陪审团\N{\r外文}There is no jury.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:31.51,1:30:32.76,中文,,0,0,0,,只有我\N{\r外文}It's just me.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:34.06,1:30:35.26,中文,,0,0,0,,孩子\N{\r外文}Son,
Dialogue: 0,1:30:35.51,1:30:38.10,中文,,0,0,0,,你到底怎么了\N{\r外文}what in the hell is wrong with you?
Dialogue: 0,1:30:39.56,1:30:41.85,中文,,0,0,0,,是米驰吗 罗杰\N{\r外文}Is that Mitch? Roger!
Dialogue: 0,1:30:42.69,1:30:43.94,中文,,0,0,0,,是米驰\N{\r外文}It's Mitch!
Dialogue: 0,1:30:44.11,1:30:45.94,中文,,0,0,0,,我忘了时间了\N{\r外文}I lost all track of time.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:46.03,1:30:48.36,中文,,0,0,0,,作为今晚"跟着唱"现场嘉宾\N{\r外文}As studio guests for the sing-along tonight,
Dialogue: 0,1:30:48.44,1:30:51.95,中文,,0,0,0,,我们邀请了 纽约城圣莫尼卡教堂的儿童合唱组\N{\r外文}we have the children's choir of Saint Monica's Church in New York City.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:52.03,1:30:56.12,中文,,0,0,0,,你能加入他们为爱尔兰唱几首歌吗 大家一起\N{\r外文}Won't you join them and the gang in a few songs for the Irish? Everybody!
Dialogue: 0,1:32:26.96,1:32:28.09,中文,,0,0,0,,爸\N{\r外文}Dad?
Dialogue: 0,1:32:32.47,1:32:34.22,中文,,0,0,0,,你来干什么\N{\r外文}What are you doing here?
Dialogue: 0,1:32:36.22,1:32:37.97,中文,,0,0,0,,我来看你\N{\r外文}I came to see you.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:42.14,1:32:44.06,中文,,0,0,0,,你穿成这样干什么\N{\r外文}What are you doing dressed like this?
Dialogue: 0,1:32:44.14,1:32:46.10,中文,,0,0,0,,我找了份政府工作\N{\r外文}I took a government job.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:46.23,1:32:49.61,中文,,0,0,0,,你知道我在做什么吗 你有没有个好律师\N{\r外文}You see what I'm doing? Do you have a good lawyer?
Dialogue: 0,1:32:50.86,1:32:52.36,中文,,0,0,0,,我现在算是个律师\N{\r外文}I sort of am a lawyer now.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:52.44,1:32:54.99,中文,,0,0,0,,看这封信 税务局想要更多\N{\r外文}Look at this letter. The IRS wants more.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:55.95,1:32:58.49,中文,,0,0,0,,我跟他们达成个协议 我交2项罚金\N{\r外文}I had a deal with them. Two penalties.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:58.57,1:33:01.24,中文,,0,0,0,,他们吃了蛋糕 现在还想要掉下的渣子\N{\r外文}They ate the cake, now they want the crumbs.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:01.95,1:33:03.58,中文,,0,0,0,,我想起诉他们\N{\r外文}I want to sue them.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:04.75,1:33:06.83,中文,,0,0,0,,现在他们想要渣子\N{\r外文}Now they want the crumbs.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:08.58,1:33:09.84,中文,,0,0,0,,坐下\N{\r外文}Sit down.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:09.92,1:33:13.17,中文,,0,0,0,,他们试图吓唬我 你知道吗\N{\r外文}They're trying to scare me, intimidate me. You know what?
Dialogue: 0,1:33:14.84,1:33:16.22,中文,,0,0,0,,知道什么\N{\r外文}You know what?
Dialogue: 0,1:33:16.30,1:33:18.34,中文,,0,0,0,,我要让他们追逐我\N{\r外文}I'll make them chase me
Dialogue: 0,1:33:18.93,1:33:21.18,中文,,0,0,0,,用他们的余生\N{\r外文}for the rest of their lives!
Dialogue: 0,1:33:28.15,1:33:30.23,中文,,0,0,0,,很高兴看见你 爸爸\N{\r外文}It's great to see you, Daddy.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:32.07,1:33:34.49,中文,,0,0,0,,坐下 我想给你看样东西\N{\r外文}Sit down, I want to show you something.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:36.90,1:33:39.20,中文,,0,0,0,,我来是要给你这个\N{\r外文}I came here to give you this.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:39.28,1:33:42.24,中文,,0,0,0,,这是我的订婚舞会邀请函\N{\r外文}It's an invitation to an engagement party.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:45.00,1:33:47.21,中文,,0,0,0,,爸爸 我要结婚了\N{\r外文}Daddy, I'm getting married.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:48.00,1:33:50.21,中文,,0,0,0,,你能相信我要订婚了吗\N{\r外文}Can you believe that I'm getting married?
Dialogue: 0,1:33:50.29,1:33:53.59,中文,,0,0,0,,你现在什么都不用担心了\N{\r外文}You don't need to worry about anything now, Dad. Listen.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:53.67,1:33:57.30,中文,,0,0,0,,我要有辆崭新的凯迪拉克 我要有栋6万美元的房子\N{\r外文}I'm getting a brand-new Cadillac, I'm getting a $60,000 house,
Dialogue: 0,1:33:57.38,1:33:59.09,中文,,0,0,0,,我全得回来了\N{\r外文}I'm getting it all back.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:59.22,1:34:03.97,中文,,0,0,0,,所有的珠宝 毛皮 他们拿走的每一样东西我都要得回来\N{\r外文}All the jewellery, the furs, everything they took from us, I'll get it back.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:07.35,1:34:09.31,中文,,0,0,0,,妈看见你穿成这样了吗\N{\r外文}Has Ma seen you dressed like this?
Dialogue: 0,1:34:10.90,1:34:13.11,中文,,0,0,0,,对 她回来取过几个箱子\N{\r外文}Yeah, she came to pick up some boxes.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:13.52,1:34:15.32,中文,,0,0,0,,那就好 你知道为什么\N{\r外文}That's okay. You know why?
Dialogue: 0,1:34:15.40,1:34:17.74,中文,,0,0,0,,因为她要跟我们一起去参加婚礼\N{\r外文}Because she's going to the wedding with us.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:17.86,1:34:20.20,中文,,0,0,0,,我要给你穿套全新的衣服\N{\r外文}I'm gonna get you a brand-new suit, Dad.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:20.66,1:34:23.16,中文,,0,0,0,,一套曼哈顿之鹰 带3颗黑色珍珠纽扣\N{\r外文}One of those Manhattan Eagle, three-button black pearl suits.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:23.24,1:34:24.33,中文,,0,0,0,,你会帅极了\N{\r外文}You'll look great.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:24.41,1:34:26.91,中文,,0,0,0,,那些是不错 但她不会见我的\N{\r外文}Those are nice. She won't see me.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:29.46,1:34:31.67,中文,,0,0,0,,你有没有试着给她打电话\N{\r外文}Have you tried to call her?
Dialogue: 0,1:34:33.46,1:34:35.96,中文,,0,0,0,,为什么你现在不给她打电话呢\N{\r外文}Why don't you call her right now?
Dialogue: 0,1:34:36.34,1:34:38.26,中文,,0,0,0,,为什么你现在不给她打电话呢\N{\r外文}Why don't you call her right now?
Dialogue: 0,1:34:38.55,1:34:40.05,中文,,0,0,0,,爸 给她打电话\N{\r外文}Dad, just call her.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:40.13,1:34:41.68,中文,,0,0,0,,为了我打\N{\r外文}Call her for me.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:41.93,1:34:45.64,中文,,0,0,0,,告诉她我有2张头等仓机票 去看她儿子的婚礼\N{\r外文}Tell her I have two first-class tickets to go see her son's wedding...
Dialogue: 0,1:34:45.72,1:34:47.60,中文,,0,0,0,,你母亲现在和杰克·巴恩斯结婚了\N{\r外文}You mother's married now to my friend, Jack Barnes.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:47.68,1:34:50.44,中文,,0,0,0,,他们在长岛有套房子\N{\r外文}They have a house in Long Island.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:51.60,1:34:54.27,中文,,0,0,0,,联邦调查局来找过我\N{\r外文}I had an F.B.I. agent come see me.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:55.52,1:34:58.82,中文,,0,0,0,,你能躲过他们 儿子 那家伙好像害怕了\N{\r外文}You got their number, son. The guy looked scared.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:59.36,1:35:03.16,中文,,0,0,0,,美国政府 亲爱的 吓得不敢照面\N{\r外文}The United States Government, champ, running for the hills.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:04.20,1:35:05.58,中文,,0,0,0,,一步登天\N{\r外文}To the moon!
Dialogue: 0,1:35:19.22,1:35:20.63,中文,,0,0,0,,都结束了\N{\r外文}It's over.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:21.80,1:35:23.18,中文,,0,0,0,,我要洗手不干了\N{\r外文}I'm going to stop now.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:26.35,1:35:28.14,中文,,0,0,0,,他们永远也抓不住你\N{\r外文}They're never gonna catch you, Frank.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:28.22,1:35:31.69,中文,,0,0,0,,她不该那样做 她为什么对你那样做呢\N{\r外文}She wouldn't do that! Why would she do that to you?
Dialogue: 0,1:35:31.85,1:35:34.77,中文,,0,0,0,,坐我旁边 喝一杯 我是你父亲\N{\r外文}Come on. Sit with me. Have a drink. I'm your father.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:36.23,1:35:40.44,中文,,0,0,0,,那么叫我住手吧\N{\r外文}Then ask me to stop. Then ask me to stop.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:43.78,1:35:45.37,中文,,0,0,0,,你不会住手的\N{\r外文}You can't stop.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:47.95,1:35:49.95,中文,,0,0,0,,你要去哪儿\N{\r外文}Where are you going?
Dialogue: 0,1:35:50.04,1:35:52.37,中文,,0,0,0,,好了 你要去哪儿\N{\r外文}Come on, Frank, where are you going?
Dialogue: 0,1:35:52.50,1:35:55.08,中文,,0,0,0,,你今晚要去哪儿\N{\r外文}Where are you going? Where are you going tonight?
Dialogue: 0,1:35:55.42,1:35:56.79,中文,,0,0,0,,什么奇异的地方\N{\r外文}Someplace exotic?
Dialogue: 0,1:35:56.88,1:35:59.51,中文,,0,0,0,,你今晚要去哪儿 塔西提岛 夏威夷\N{\r外文}Where are you going tonight? Tahiti? Hawaii?
Dialogue: 0,1:36:16.90,1:36:18.61,中文,,0,0,0,,这是汉莱提\N{\r外文}This is Hanratty.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:19.90,1:36:21.40,中文,,0,0,0,,你好 卡尔\N{\r外文}Hello, Carl.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:21.99,1:36:23.49,中文,,0,0,0,,圣诞快乐\N{\r外文}Merry Christmas.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:23.99,1:36:25.86,中文,,0,0,0,,你好吗 考纳斯大夫\N{\r外文}How are you, Dr Conners?
Dialogue: 0,1:36:26.37,1:36:29.49,中文,,0,0,0,,我已经有几个月不当考纳斯大夫了\N{\r外文}Carl, I haven't been Dr Conners for months now.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:32.91,1:36:34.12,中文,,0,0,0,,噢\N{\r外文}Well,
Dialogue: 0,1:36:34.42,1:36:37.17,中文,,0,0,0,,在平安夜我坐在办公室\N{\r外文}I'm sitting here in my office on Christmas Eve.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:38.00,1:36:39.63,中文,,0,0,0,,你想要什么\N{\r外文}What do you want?
Dialogue: 0,1:36:45.13,1:36:46.34,中文,,0,0,0,,好吧\N{\r外文}Okay.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:50.89,1:36:52.77,中文,,0,0,0,,我想结束这一切\N{\r外文}I want it to be over.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:57.40,1:37:00.23,中文,,0,0,0,,我想结束这一切 我要结婚了\N{\r外文}I want it to be over. I'm getting married.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:00.77,1:37:02.40,中文,,0,0,0,,我正在安顿\N{\r外文}I'm settling down.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:02.48,1:37:04.74,中文,,0,0,0,,你偷了差不多4百万美元\N{\r外文}You've stolen almost $4 million.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:04.99,1:37:07.28,中文,,0,0,0,,你想我们能把这作为结婚礼物给你\N{\r外文}You think we could call it a wedding present?
Dialogue: 0,1:37:07.36,1:37:09.66,中文,,0,0,0,,这不是件你能躲开的事\N{\r外文}This isn't something you get to walk away from, Frank.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:09.74,1:37:12.12,中文,,0,0,0,,我想休战 没有休战\N{\r外文}I want to call a truce. No truce.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:12.20,1:37:15.83,中文,,0,0,0,,你会被抓住并送入监狱 你以为后果会是怎样的\N{\r外文}You will be caught, you will go to prison. Where did you think this was going?
Dialogue: 0,1:37:16.37,1:37:18.71,中文,,0,0,0,,请放我一马 卡尔\N{\r外文}Please leave me alone, Carl.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:19.34,1:37:20.59,中文,,0,0,0,,求你\N{\r外文}Please?
Dialogue: 0,1:37:21.17,1:37:23.26,中文,,0,0,0,,我就快抓住你了 不是吗\N{\r外文}I'm getting close, aren't I?
Dialogue: 0,1:37:23.34,1:37:25.97,中文,,0,0,0,,我接近了所以你害怕了 我知道\N{\r外文}You're scared because I'm getting close. I know
Dialogue: 0,1:37:26.05,1:37:30.26,中文,,0,0,0,,你在什里夫伯特租了辆车 住在查尔斯湖的一家旅馆\N{\r外文}you rented a car in Shreveport, stayed in a hotel on Lake Charles.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:31.26,1:37:33.14,中文,,0,0,0,,你想跑 尽管去吧\N{\r外文}You want to run, be my guest.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:33.22,1:37:35.85,中文,,0,0,0,,你的支票可不像你那么会说谎\N{\r外文}Your cheques don't lie as well as you do.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:35.93,1:37:37.60,中文,,0,0,0,,不要追我了\N{\r外文}Stop chasing me.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:40.77,1:37:42.27,中文,,0,0,0,,我不能停\N{\r外文}I can't stop.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:43.61,1:37:44.99,中文,,0,0,0,,这是我的工作\N{\r外文}It's my job.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:46.24,1:37:47.95,中文,,0,0,0,,没关系 卡尔\N{\r外文}It's okay, Carl.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:50.12,1:37:52.16,中文,,0,0,0,,我只是想我该问一下\N{\r外文}I just thought I'd ask.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:56.75,1:37:58.25,中文,,0,0,0,,圣诞快乐\N{\r外文}Merry Christmas.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:01.79,1:38:03.38,中文,,0,0,0,,我喜欢我的工作\N{\r外文}I love my job.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:04.80,1:38:06.17,中文,,0,0,0,,好吧\N{\r外文}All right.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:06.38,1:38:09.80,中文,,0,0,0,,我们找来 最近2个月的路易斯安娜州的所有报纸\N{\r外文}Let's get every newspaper in Louisiana for the last two months.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:09.89,1:38:11.35,中文,,0,0,0,,我们要找什么\N{\r外文}What're we looking for?
Dialogue: 0,1:38:11.43,1:38:13.97,中文,,0,0,0,,订婚声明 以考纳斯的名字\N{\r外文}Engagement announcements. Name of Conners.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:14.56,1:38:17.56,中文,,0,0,0,,得了 这孩子现在应该已经改名了\N{\r外文}Come on, the kid would have changed his name by now.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:18.69,1:38:20.48,中文,,0,0,0,,他不能改\N{\r外文}He can't change it.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:20.69,1:38:22.36,中文,,0,0,0,,她认为他是考纳斯\N{\r外文}She thinks he's Conners.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:22.44,1:38:24.94,中文,,0,0,0,,如果他丢了名字 就丢了她\N{\r外文}If he loses the name, he loses the girl.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:35.16,1:38:37.79,中文,,0,0,0,,恭喜 玩得好吗\N{\r外文}Congratulations! Having a good time?
Dialogue: 0,1:38:42.17,1:38:43.67,中文,,0,0,0,,继续跳舞\N{\r外文}Keep dancing.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:46.51,1:38:48.17,中文,,0,0,0,,看谁来了\N{\r外文}Look who's here.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:49.68,1:38:51.97,中文,,0,0,0,,我去卫生间\N{\r外文}I'm going to the little boys' room.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:52.55,1:38:53.97,中文,,0,0,0,,快点回来\N{\r外文}Hurry back.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:09.36,1:39:12.36,中文,,0,0,0,,我是联邦调查局的汉莱提特工\N{\r外文}Good evening. I'm Agent Hanratty with the F.B.I.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:12.45,1:39:14.78,中文,,0,0,0,,我们想和主人谈话\N{\r外文}We'd like to have a few kind words with your host, if possible.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:14.87,1:39:16.16,中文,,0,0,0,,我去找他\N{\r外文}I'll get him.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:18.62,1:39:20.54,中文,,0,0,0,,就在那儿 先生\N{\r外文}Right over there, sir.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:22.79,1:39:24.71,中文,,0,0,0,,晚上好 我是罗杰·斯特朗\N{\r外文}Good evening, gentlemen. I'm Roger Strong.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:24.79,1:39:26.54,中文,,0,0,0,,卡尔·汉莱提 联邦调查局的\N{\r外文}Carl Hanratty, F.B.I.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:26.54,1:39:28.30,中文,,0,0,0,,这是阿姆德斯基和福克斯特工\N{\r外文}These are Agents Amdursky and Fox.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:29.34,1:39:32.89,中文,,0,0,0,,抱歉闯到你的舞会 没关系 我能为你做什么\N{\r外文}Sorry to crash your party, sir. Not at all. What can I do for you?
Dialogue: 0,1:39:32.97,1:39:36.35,中文,,0,0,0,,如果不太麻烦 我想见新郎\N{\r外文}If it's not too much trouble, I'd like to meet the groom.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:36.43,1:39:38.22,中文,,0,0,0,,有什么问题吗\N{\r外文}Is there a problem?
Dialogue: 0,1:39:40.81,1:39:43.40,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰克 你能拿一下这些支票吗\N{\r外文}Frank! Can you hold all these?
Dialogue: 0,1:39:43.48,1:39:45.44,中文,,0,0,0,,这些是我父亲的朋友送的\N{\r外文}They're checks. They're from my dad's friends.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:45.52,1:39:47.82,中文,,0,0,0,,是送给我们用来开始新生活\N{\r外文}They're for us so we can start our new life...
Dialogue: 0,1:39:47.90,1:39:50.49,中文,,0,0,0,,你要干什么 怎么了\N{\r外文}What are you doing? What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,1:39:50.61,1:39:52.36,中文,,0,0,0,,我们得离开\N{\r外文}We have to leave.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:55.20,1:39:56.70,中文,,0,0,0,,你爱我 是吗\N{\r外文}You love me, right?
Dialogue: 0,1:39:56.91,1:39:59.24,中文,,0,0,0,,我是说 无论怎样你都会爱我\N{\r外文}I mean, you'd love me no matter what.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:59.41,1:40:01.43,中文,,0,0,0,,无论我生病还是贫穷\N{\r外文}You'd love me whether I was sick or poor,
Dialogue: 0,1:40:01.43,1:40:03.25,中文,,0,0,0,,或者如果我有另外一个名字 你都会爱我\N{\r外文}or if I had a different name.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:03.33,1:40:04.79,中文,,0,0,0,,你从哪儿弄来的那些钱\N{\r外文}Frank, where did you get all that money?
Dialogue: 0,1:40:04.92,1:40:08.13,中文,,0,0,0,,名字并不重要\N{\r外文}Brenda, listen. A name doesn't matter.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:08.21,1:40:09.55,中文,,0,0,0,,我叫弗兰克·考纳斯\N{\r外文}My name is Frank Conners.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:09.63,1:40:12.26,中文,,0,0,0,,那是跟你一起时用的名字 但我们都有秘密\N{\r外文}That's who I am with you. But we all have secrets.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:12.34,1:40:14.55,中文,,0,0,0,,有时旅行时 我用弗兰克·泰勒这名字\N{\r外文}Sometimes when I travel, I use the name Frank Taylor.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:14.64,1:40:16.30,中文,,0,0,0,,这是我的秘密\N{\r外文}That's my secret.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:16.39,1:40:20.27,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰克·泰勒 你知道 弗兰克·布莱克 这没关系\N{\r外文}Frank Taylor, you know. Frank Black. It doesn't matter.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:20.89,1:40:22.48,中文,,0,0,0,,你为什么说这些\N{\r外文}Why are you saying all this?
Dialogue: 0,1:40:24.06,1:40:26.56,中文,,0,0,0,,我不想再跟你说谎\N{\r外文}Brenda, I don't want to lie to you any more.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:26.65,1:40:28.98,中文,,0,0,0,,我不是医生 从来没上过医学院\N{\r外文}I'm not a doctor, I never went to medical school.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:29.07,1:40:32.36,中文,,0,0,0,,我不是律师 不是哈佛毕业生 也不是路德教徒\N{\r外文}I'm not a lawyer, or a Harvard graduate or a Lutheran.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:32.44,1:40:36.20,中文,,0,0,0,,我1年半前16岁时从家里跑出来\N{\r外文}I ran away from home a year and a half ago when I was 16.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:41.70,1:40:43.62,中文,,0,0,0,,你不是路德教徒\N{\r外文}You're not a Lutheran?
Dialogue: 0,1:40:44.79,1:40:47.63,中文,,0,0,0,,看见这些钱了吗 我还有更多\N{\r外文}You see all this money? I have more.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:48.17,1:40:50.00,中文,,0,0,0,,我有的是\N{\r外文}I have plenty more.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:50.80,1:40:54.47,中文,,0,0,0,,足够我们两个下半辈子用了\N{\r外文}I have enough money to last us for the rest of our lives. Look.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:55.38,1:40:57.30,中文,,0,0,0,,别逗我\N{\r外文}Frank, stop teasing me!
Dialogue: 0,1:40:57.68,1:41:01.10,中文,,0,0,0,,你是弗兰克·考纳斯 28岁\N{\r外文}You're Frank Conners and you're 28 years old...
Dialogue: 0,1:41:03.31,1:41:05.14,中文,,0,0,0,,你为什么对我说谎\N{\r外文}Why would you lie to me?
Dialogue: 0,1:41:06.60,1:41:09.40,中文,,0,0,0,,我想知道你的名字 告诉我你的名字\N{\r外文}I want to know your name. Tell me your name.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:09.48,1:41:12.86,中文,,0,0,0,,我们可以住在任何想住的地方 但是你得信任我\N{\r外文}We can live anywhere we want. But you have to trust me.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:12.94,1:41:15.78,中文,,0,0,0,,你信任我吗 你爱我吗 布伦达\N{\r外文}Do you trust me? Do you love me, Brenda?
Dialogue: 0,1:41:15.86,1:41:17.32,中文,,0,0,0,,是的 我爱你\N{\r外文}Yes. I love you.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:18.03,1:41:19.62,中文,,0,0,0,,对不起 孩子妈妈\N{\r外文}Excuse me, Mother.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:20.24,1:41:22.95,中文,,0,0,0,,这是汉莱提先生 我太太 卡罗尔\N{\r外文}This is Mr Hanratty. My wife, Carol.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:23.04,1:41:25.00,中文,,0,0,0,,汉 汉莱提 夫人\N{\r外文}Mister... Hanratty, ma'am.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:25.29,1:41:27.12,中文,,0,0,0,,你看见弗兰克或布伦达了吗\N{\r外文}Have you seen Frank or Brenda?
Dialogue: 0,1:41:27.21,1:41:29.17,中文,,0,0,0,,我想他们上楼了\N{\r外文}I think they went upstairs.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:38.89,1:41:40.05,中文,,0,0,0,,过来\N{\r外文}Come here.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:40.72,1:41:44.35,中文,,0,0,0,,2天后 在迈阿密国际机场见我\N{\r外文}In two days, meet me at Miami International Airport.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:44.43,1:41:48.10,中文,,0,0,0,,你父母睡觉后离开家 搭出租车\N{\r外文}Leave the house after your parents go to sleep. Take a taxicab.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:48.19,1:41:51.82,中文,,0,0,0,,把这钱给出租司机 告诉他整夜开\N{\r外文}Give the taxi driver this money. Tell him to drive all through the night.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:51.90,1:41:53.78,中文,,0,0,0,,你将在上午10点离开\N{\r外文}You're gonna leave at 10:00 a.m.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:53.86,1:41:55.32,中文,,0,0,0,,上午10点 好吗\N{\r外文}10:00 a.m. All right?
Dialogue: 0,1:42:15.01,1:42:17.22,中文,,0,0,0,,哪个房间 角落那个\N{\r外文}Which room, sir? In the corner.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:17.72,1:42:21.89,中文,,0,0,0,,听我说 迈阿密国际机场到站口 重复一遍\N{\r外文}You have to listen. The International Terminal in Miami. Say it.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:22.01,1:42:26.14,中文,,0,0,0,,不管怎样 搭出租车 上午10点到那儿\N{\r外文}No matter what, take a taxicab, be there at 10:00 a.m.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:26.22,1:42:28.02,中文,,0,0,0,,我会到那儿的 不管怎样\N{\r外文}I'll be there at 10:00 a.m. no matter what.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:28.10,1:42:30.65,中文,,0,0,0,,2天后 2天 布伦达 2天\N{\r外文}In two days. Two days, Brenda. Two days.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:30.73,1:42:33.61,中文,,0,0,0,,2天后我会到那儿 不管怎样 上午10点到\N{\r外文}In two days I'll be there, no matter what, at 10:00 a.m.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:40.66,1:42:43.49,中文,,0,0,0,,我们不会告诉任何人 答应我\N{\r外文}We're not gonna tell anyone, Brenda. You have to promise me now.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:43.58,1:42:48.71,中文,,0,0,0,,求你 你走之前请告诉我你的名字\N{\r外文}Please! Before you go, please tell me your name. Tell me.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:50.17,1:42:53.79,中文,,0,0,0,,小弗兰克·威廉·阿巴戈内尔\N{\r外文}Frank William Abagnale, Jr.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:43.43,1:43:45.70,中文,,0,0,0,,迈阿密国际机场
Dialogue: 0,1:45:06.59,1:45:07.84,中文,,0,0,0,,布伦达\N{\r外文}Brenda.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:20.86,1:45:22.90,中文,,0,0,0,,这家伙没来 可能走漏了风声\N{\r外文}This guy is a no-show. Maybe he was tipped.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:23.19,1:45:24.74,中文,,0,0,0,,今天没来 他明天会来的\N{\r外文}He's not here today, it'll be tomorrow.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:24.82,1:45:26.49,中文,,0,0,0,,在他出境之前我们会抓住他的\N{\r外文}We'll get him before he leaves the country.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:26.57,1:45:28.37,中文,,0,0,0,,他没有护照\N{\r外文}He doesn't have a passport.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:28.45,1:45:30.49,中文,,0,0,0,,他上过哈佛和伯克利\N{\r外文}For the last six months, he's gone to Harvard and Berkeley.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:30.58,1:45:32.62,中文,,0,0,0,,我肯定他能搞到本护照\N{\r外文}I'm betting he can get a passport.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:32.70,1:45:35.04,中文,,0,0,0,,我们的人在这儿等着他\N{\r外文}Our men are waiting for him here in Miami International.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:35.12,1:45:36.75,中文,,0,0,0,,他以前用过这儿 他了解这里的布局\N{\r外文}He's used it before, he knows the layout.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:36.83,1:45:40.29,中文,,0,0,0,,迈阿密警察局给我们提供了 2班倒的各25人的便衣警察\N{\r外文}The Miami police offered us 50 uniformed cops in two shifts of 25.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:40.38,1:45:42.75,中文,,0,0,0,,再加上我们的人 这儿差不多有100人\N{\r外文}With our guys, that's almost 100 men in one airport.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:42.84,1:45:44.30,中文,,0,0,0,,我们应该到处布置人吗\N{\r外文}Don't you think we should spread it around?
Dialogue: 0,1:45:44.38,1:45:45.88,中文,,0,0,0,,不 这是出境点\N{\r外文}No, this is the exit point.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:45.97,1:45:49.97,中文,,0,0,0,,你怎么知道他没有租辆车开到纽约 或亚特兰大\N{\r外文}How do you know he hasn't rented a car and driven to airports in New York, Atlanta?
Dialogue: 0,1:45:50.05,1:45:53.10,中文,,0,0,0,,因为我没在纽约 没在亚特兰大\N{\r外文}Because I'm not in New York. I'm not in Atlanta.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:53.39,1:45:55.68,中文,,0,0,0,,我是弗兰克·罗伯茨\N{\r外文}Yes. This is Frank Roberts.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:55.77,1:45:58.27,中文,,0,0,0,,我正在通知这一地区的所有大学\N{\r外文}I'm letting all the universities in the area know
Dialogue: 0,1:45:58.35,1:46:02.11,中文,,0,0,0,,泛美航空公司将在今年开始一项 新的招募计划\N{\r外文}that Pan Am will be initiating a new recruiting programme this year.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:02.19,1:46:05.11,中文,,0,0,0,,我明天到你们学校\N{\r外文}I'll be stopping by your campus tomorrow morning.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:05.94,1:46:08.15,中文,,0,0,0,,非常感谢各位光临\N{\r外文}Thank you all very much for coming.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:08.66,1:46:12.08,中文,,0,0,0,,在今天结束时 我要挑选8位年轻女士\N{\r外文}At the end of the day, I'll be choosing eight young ladies
Dialogue: 0,1:46:12.16,1:46:13.58,中文,,0,0,0,,作为\N{\r外文}to be a part of
Dialogue: 0,1:46:14.33,1:46:18.16,中文,,0,0,0,,泛美未来机组乘务员培训计划的一部分\N{\r外文}Pan Am's future stewardess flight crew programme.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:18.25,1:46:20.38,中文,,0,0,0,,这些女士将伴我\N{\r外文}These eight young ladies will accompany me on
Dialogue: 0,1:46:20.46,1:46:23.34,中文,,0,0,0,,做为期2个月的公共关系全欧洲之旅\N{\r外文}a two-month public relations tour through Europe
Dialogue: 0,1:46:24.42,1:46:27.13,中文,,0,0,0,,在那里她们将第一手发现需要什么\N{\r外文}where they will discover firsthand what it takes
Dialogue: 0,1:46:27.22,1:46:29.26,中文,,0,0,0,,才能成为一名泛美空中小姐\N{\r外文}to be a Pan American stewardess.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:32.35,1:46:36.39,中文,,0,0,0,,给我至少2个人 不 每2个国家航线柜台1个人\N{\r外文}Give me at least two men, no, one man per every two counters.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:38.64,1:46:39.69,中文,,0,0,0,,阿姆德斯基\N{\r外文}Amdursky?
Dialogue: 0,1:46:41.31,1:46:45.40,中文,,0,0,0,,保证你的人守着人行道和出入口\N{\r外文}Make sure your uniforms are covering the sidewalks, entrances and exits.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:47.57,1:46:50.41,中文,,0,0,0,,我们来经常巡查男洗手间\N{\r外文}Let's have periodic sweeps of the men's lav.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:52.12,1:46:55.12,中文,,0,0,0,,什么条件使我能成为未来的空中小姐\N{\r外文}What qualifies me to be a future stewardess?
Dialogue: 0,1:46:55.37,1:47:00.12,中文,,0,0,0,,我认为我真的很友善 真能帮助人\N{\r外文}Well, I think that I'm really friendly and I can really help out
Dialogue: 0,1:47:00.21,1:47:03.21,中文,,0,0,0,,使人感到在飞机上受到欢迎 并且\N{\r外文}and make people feel welcome on the plane and...
Dialogue: 0,1:47:03.29,1:47:05.50,中文,,0,0,0,,我们将以9600公里时速\N{\r外文}We'll be travelling at 6,000 miles per hour,
Dialogue: 0,1:47:05.59,1:47:07.55,中文,,0,0,0,,在90米的高度上飞行\N{\r外文}at an altitude of 300 feet.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:07.67,1:47:09.97,中文,,0,0,0,,我行装已打好\N{\r外文}All my bags are packed.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:10.80,1:47:12.39,中文,,0,0,0,,我准备好要走\N{\r外文}I'm ready to go.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:14.76,1:47:16.35,中文,,0,0,0,,依琳娜·安德森\N{\r外文}Ilene Anderson.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:24.56,1:47:26.02,中文,,0,0,0,,米姬·埃克\N{\r外文}Miggy Acker.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:30.82,1:47:32.57,中文,,0,0,0,,黛布拉·乔·麦克米伦\N{\r外文}Debra Jo McMillan.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:39.62,1:47:41.04,中文,,0,0,0,,坎迪·赫斯顿\N{\r外文}Candy Heston.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:54.39,1:47:56.34,中文,,0,0,0,,迈阿密国际机场
Dialogue: 0,1:48:40.56,1:48:43.64,中文,,0,0,0,,看见走在前面的金发妞了吗 我本该成为一名飞行员的\N{\r外文}Did you see that blonde out front? I should have been a pilot.
Dialogue: 0,1:48:43.73,1:48:44.73,中文,,0,0,0,,很对\N{\r外文}Exactly.
Dialogue: 0,1:48:44.81,1:48:47.69,中文,,0,0,0,,汉莱提先生 请接听免费电话\N{\r外文}Mr Hanratty, pick up the courtesy telephone.
Dialogue: 0,1:48:47.77,1:48:50.19,中文,,0,0,0,,汉莱提 你的对讲机刚才不好使\N{\r外文}Hanratty. Your walkie-talkie wasn't working.
Dialogue: 0,1:48:50.28,1:48:51.94,中文,,0,0,0,,有一个坐大都市单排座车\N{\r外文}There's a guy in a Pan Am uniform
Dialogue: 0,1:48:52.03,1:48:54.86,中文,,0,0,0,,穿泛美制服的人在到站J口\N{\r外文}sitting in a white Coupe DeVille in front of Terminal J.
Dialogue: 0,1:48:54.95,1:48:58.16,中文,,0,0,0,,那是包机口 你看见他的脸了吗\N{\r外文}That's the charter terminal. Did you get a look at his face?
Dialogue: 0,1:48:58.24,1:49:01.37,中文,,0,0,0,,他带着飞行员的帽子 我想是他\N{\r外文}He's got his pilot's cap on. Carl, I think it's him.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:13.55,1:49:15.18,中文,,0,0,0,,从车里出来 弗兰克\N{\r外文}Out of the car, Frank.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:15.80,1:49:17.01,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰克\N{\r外文}Frank?
Dialogue: 0,1:49:17.22,1:49:19.05,中文,,0,0,0,,走出汽车\N{\r外文}Step out of the car.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:19.30,1:49:21.26,中文,,0,0,0,,把手放在我能看见的地方别动\N{\r外文}Keep your hands where I can see them.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:21.35,1:49:23.22,中文,,0,0,0,,不要开枪 我只是位司机\N{\r外文}Don't shoot me. I'm just a driver.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:23.31,1:49:25.14,中文,,0,0,0,,一个人给我100美元让我穿这制服\N{\r外文}A man paid me $100 to wear this uniform
Dialogue: 0,1:49:25.23,1:49:28.44,中文,,0,0,0,,到飞机场接人 你接谁\N{\r外文}to pick someone up at the airport. Who're you picking up?
Dialogue: 0,1:49:28.52,1:49:29.65,中文,,0,0,0,,嘿\N{\r外文}Hey!
Dialogue: 0,1:49:32.87,1:49:34.27,中文,,0,0,0,,汉德拉提
Dialogue: 0,1:49:50.59,1:49:53.43,中文,,0,0,0,,7个月后
Dialogue: 0,1:49:54.30,1:49:57.30,中文,,0,0,0,,南美洲 澳大利亚 新加坡 埃及\N{\r外文}South America, Australia, Singapore, Egypt.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:57.38,1:49:59.51,中文,,0,0,0,,这家伙完全失去控制了\N{\r外文}The kid's gone completely out of control.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:59.59,1:50:01.93,中文,,0,0,0,,为什么没通知我 谁也没通知\N{\r外文}Why wasn't I called? Nobody was called, sir.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:02.01,1:50:03.81,中文,,0,0,0,,直到银行上周才知道\N{\r外文}The banks didn't know what was happening until last week.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:03.89,1:50:04.93,中文,,0,0,0,,不可能\N{\r外文}That's impossible.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:05.02,1:50:07.27,中文,,0,0,0,,他们没通知是因为这不是伪造\N{\r外文}They didn't call because it's not counterfeiting. It's something else.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:07.35,1:50:09.98,中文,,0,0,0,,他做什么 他做的是真支票\N{\r外文}What is he doing? He's making real checks, sir.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:10.06,1:50:11.94,中文,,0,0,0,,那么完美 航空公司辨别不出来\N{\r外文}These are so perfect, the airline didn't know the difference.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:12.02,1:50:13.90,中文,,0,0,0,,上张支票是在一周前在马德里兑现的\N{\r外文}Last cheque was cashed in Madrid a week ago.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:13.98,1:50:16.78,中文,,0,0,0,,我猜他还在那儿 我们现在得出发了\N{\r外文}My guess is he's still there. We've to leave now, sir. Today.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:16.86,1:50:19.53,中文,,0,0,0,,去哪 西班牙 去西班牙\N{\r外文}For where? Spain? You want to go to Spain?
Dialogue: 0,1:50:19.61,1:50:21.91,中文,,0,0,0,,他会回到印支票的地方的\N{\r外文}Eventually, he's gotta go back to where the cheques were printed.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:21.99,1:50:23.37,中文,,0,0,0,,这就是他为什么在欧洲活动\N{\r外文}I think that's why he's moving back through Europe.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:23.45,1:50:24.87,中文,,0,0,0,,他在做一个圈子\N{\r外文}Look at the map, sir. He's making a circle.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:24.95,1:50:26.66,中文,,0,0,0,,他要用完支票了\N{\r外文}He's running out of checks.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:26.75,1:50:30.28,中文,,0,0,0,,我可能说得不准 但如果我们从马德里开始追踪他\N{\r外文}It's a long shot, but if we could track him from Madrid,
Dialogue: 0,1:50:30.28,1:50:31.21,中文,,0,0,0,,还是能抓住他的\N{\r外文}we could still catch him.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:31.29,1:50:34.30,中文,,0,0,0,,你在这儿抓不住他 在那儿也抓不住\N{\r外文}I'm sorry, Carl. If you couldn't catch him here, you're not gonna catch him there.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:34.38,1:50:36.21,中文,,0,0,0,,我们会让他跑掉的\N{\r外文}We're going to let him get away.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:37.38,1:50:39.76,中文,,0,0,0,,不 卡尔 你让他跑掉的\N{\r外文}No, Carl, you let him get away.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:21.63,1:51:24.26,中文,,0,0,0,,完美的边界尺寸\N{\r外文}A perfect one-sixteenth
Dialogue: 0,1:51:24.64,1:51:26.43,中文,,0,0,0,,整个一圈\N{\r外文}all the way around.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:28.73,1:51:31.02,中文,,0,0,0,,上色毫无瑕疵\N{\r外文}Colour separation is flawless.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:33.77,1:51:35.32,中文,,0,0,0,,墨迹没有流淌\N{\r外文}There's no bleeding.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:35.44,1:51:38.15,中文,,0,0,0,,在美国没有人能干得这么好\N{\r外文}Nobody does work like this in the States.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:38.23,1:51:39.69,中文,,0,0,0,,除了我们\N{\r外文}Nobody but us.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:39.78,1:51:41.49,中文,,0,0,0,,是在哪儿印制的\N{\r外文}Where was it printed?
Dialogue: 0,1:51:41.57,1:51:44.37,中文,,0,0,0,,是在一个老印刷机上 老印刷机\N{\r外文}It was printed on a monster. A monster.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:44.45,1:51:46.83,中文,,0,0,0,,海德尔堡 伊斯的利亚半岛 海德尔堡\N{\r外文}A Heidelberg, an Istra. Heidelberg.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:46.91,1:51:50.25,中文,,0,0,0,,过时的 4色的 能感觉出印刷机的重量\N{\r外文}A dinosaur, four colours, you can smell the weight.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:50.50,1:51:52.67,中文,,0,0,0,,2吨 不算墨水\N{\r外文}Two tons, without the ink.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:53.21,1:51:55.63,中文,,0,0,0,,他们在哪儿做这样的印刷\N{\r外文}Where do they do printing like this?
Dialogue: 0,1:51:55.71,1:51:57.34,中文,,0,0,0,,德国 英国\N{\r外文}Germany, Great Britain.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:57.42,1:51:58.67,中文,,0,0,0,,法国\N{\r外文}France.
Dialogue: 0,1:52:01.09,1:52:03.51,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰克的母亲提过法国一个村子的名字\N{\r外文}France. Frank's mother said the name of a village in France,
Dialogue: 0,1:52:03.59,1:52:04.89,中文,,0,0,0,,那儿没有沙拉利\N{\r外文}where they didn't have Sara Lee.
Dialogue: 0,1:52:04.97,1:52:06.68,中文,,0,0,0,,她遇见弗兰克父亲的村子\N{\r外文}The village where she met Frank's father.
Dialogue: 0,1:52:06.76,1:52:07.89,中文,,0,0,0,,我记不得\N{\r外文}I don't remember.
Dialogue: 0,1:52:07.97,1:52:11.81,中文,,0,0,0,,以"M"开头 是"曼"什么的 福克斯先生\N{\r外文}It started with an "M." It was "Mont" something. Mr Fox?
Dialogue: 0,1:52:11.89,1:52:14.35,中文,,0,0,0,,提问 "你是在大战时遇见你丈夫的"\N{\r外文}Yes. Question, "You met your husband during the war?"
Dialogue: 0,1:52:14.44,1:52:16.44,中文,,0,0,0,,回答 "我住在法国一个村庄\N{\r外文}Answer, "I lived in a very small village in France,
Dialogue: 0,1:52:16.52,1:52:18.07,中文,,0,0,0,,在那儿人们从没听说过沙拉利"\N{\r外文}"the kind of place where they never heard of Sara Lee."
Dialogue: 0,1:52:18.15,1:52:21.11,中文,,0,0,0,,告诉我你记下了那个村子的名字\N{\r外文}Tell me you wrote down the name of the village, Mr Fox.
Dialogue: 0,1:52:22.61,1:52:24.03,中文,,0,0,0,,曼沙\N{\r外文}Montrichard.
Dialogue: 0,1:52:26.87,1:52:31.71,中文,,0,0,0,,曼沙 法国 平安夜 1967年
Dialogue: 0,1:53:20.88,1:53:22.05,中文,,0,0,0,,卡尔\N{\r外文}Carl?
Dialogue: 0,1:53:24.72,1:53:26.38,中文,,0,0,0,,圣诞快乐\N{\r外文}Merry Christmas!
Dialogue: 0,1:53:26.51,1:53:29.47,中文,,0,0,0,,我们总是在圣诞节交谈 感觉怎么样\N{\r外文}How is it that we're always talking on Christmas?
Dialogue: 0,1:53:29.55,1:53:31.76,中文,,0,0,0,,每个圣诞节 我跟你谈话\N{\r外文}Every Christmas, I'm talking to you!
Dialogue: 0,1:53:31.85,1:53:34.43,中文,,0,0,0,,穿上衣服 你被捕了\N{\r外文}Put your shirt on, Frank. You're under arrest.
Dialogue: 0,1:53:34.52,1:53:36.64,中文,,0,0,0,,你饿了吗 想要些豆子吗\N{\r外文}Are you hungry? Do you want some beans?
Dialogue: 0,1:53:36.73,1:53:38.65,中文,,0,0,0,,他们这儿有法国最好的豆子\N{\r外文}Carl, they got the best French beans here.
Dialogue: 0,1:53:38.73,1:53:42.48,中文,,0,0,0,,外面有20多名法国警察\N{\r外文}There's two dozen French police officers outside.
Dialogue: 0,1:53:42.57,1:53:43.99,中文,,0,0,0,,他们想抓你\N{\r外文}They wanted to bring you in,
Dialogue: 0,1:53:44.07,1:53:46.40,中文,,0,0,0,,但他们需要美国人的帮助\N{\r外文}but they needed the help of an American.
Dialogue: 0,1:53:46.49,1:53:47.99,中文,,0,0,0,,但我说了我不把他们带到你这里来\N{\r外文}But I told them I wouldn't bring them to you,
Dialogue: 0,1:53:48.07,1:53:50.07,中文,,0,0,0,,除非我能亲自给你戴上手铐\N{\r外文}unless I could put the cuffs on you myself.
Dialogue: 0,1:53:50.20,1:53:52.83,中文,,0,0,0,,你有枪吗 没有\N{\r外文}You have a gun? Do you have a gun? No gun?
Dialogue: 0,1:53:52.91,1:53:53.91,中文,,0,0,0,,没有\N{\r外文}No. No gun.
Dialogue: 0,1:53:55.87,1:53:58.04,中文,,0,0,0,,那你在跟我说什么\N{\r外文}And you're telling me what?
Dialogue: 0,1:53:59.25,1:54:02.80,中文,,0,0,0,,在平安夜外面有20多名法国警察\N{\r外文}There's two dozen French police officers out there right now on Christmas Eve?
Dialogue: 0,1:54:02.88,1:54:05.09,中文,,0,0,0,,你是那么说的吗 对\N{\r外文}That's what you're telling me? Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:05.17,1:54:07.76,中文,,0,0,0,,好吧 这里没有窗户\N{\r外文}All right. There's no windows here.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:08.34,1:54:09.84,中文,,0,0,0,,我到前门看看\N{\r外文}I'm going to take a look out the front door.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:09.93,1:54:10.93,中文,,0,0,0,,不\N{\r外文}No!
Dialogue: 0,1:54:11.01,1:54:15.02,中文,,0,0,0,,我告诉他们我先走出去给他们一个信号 你自己戴上\N{\r外文}I told them I'd walk out first and give a signal. Put these on yourself.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:15.10,1:54:17.77,中文,,0,0,0,,不 我不能那样 你知道为什么\N{\r外文}No, I can't do that! You know why?
Dialogue: 0,1:54:19.27,1:54:20.86,中文,,0,0,0,,因为你总是放屁\N{\r外文}Because I think you're full of shit.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:20.94,1:54:23.52,中文,,0,0,0,,我看外面一个人也没有\N{\r外文}I don't think there's anyone else out there.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:23.61,1:54:26.44,中文,,0,0,0,,我看只有你和我 对\N{\r外文}I think it's just me and you. That's right.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:26.53,1:54:28.32,中文,,0,0,0,,只有你和我 你知道吗\N{\r外文}It's just me and you, and you know what?
Dialogue: 0,1:54:28.99,1:54:30.95,中文,,0,0,0,,你得自己抓住我\N{\r外文}You're gonna have to catch me yourself.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:31.03,1:54:33.99,中文,,0,0,0,,我们没时间争论了 很好\N{\r外文}We don't have time for this. That's good.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:34.91,1:54:37.33,中文,,0,0,0,,告诉我你想让我看见什么\N{\r外文}Tell me what you want me to see.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:37.87,1:54:41.54,中文,,0,0,0,,我不会对你撒谎的 你戴着结婚戒指\N{\r外文}I wouldn't lie to you. You're wearing a wedding ring.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:41.63,1:54:44.25,中文,,0,0,0,,那件事你骗我了 是不是撒谎了\N{\r外文}You lied to me about that! Did you lie about that?
Dialogue: 0,1:54:44.34,1:54:48.17,中文,,0,0,0,,你问我是不是有个家 我是有 但不再有了\N{\r外文}You asked me if I had a family. I did. But I don't any more.
Dialogue: 0,1:54:56.85,1:55:00.77,中文,,0,0,0,,喂 不 没有问题 我们马上出来\N{\r外文}Yes. No, there is no problem. We're coming out right now.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:03.19,1:55:04.73,中文,,0,0,0,,干得不错\N{\r外文}That was good.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:05.27,1:55:07.40,中文,,0,0,0,,你是不是给旅馆前台服务员钱\N{\r外文}Did you pay some hotel desk clerk to make that call for you?
Dialogue: 0,1:55:07.49,1:55:08.53,中文,,0,0,0,,让他给你打那个电话\N{\r外文}Is that what you did?
Dialogue: 0,1:55:08.61,1:55:11.78,中文,,0,0,0,,是卢克警官 我还有1分钟带你出去\N{\r外文}It was Captain Luc. I've got one minute to bring you out.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:11.86,1:55:14.28,中文,,0,0,0,,卢克警官 噢 卢克警官 好\N{\r外文}Captain Luc? Oh, Captain Luc! Well,
Dialogue: 0,1:55:14.37,1:55:18.25,中文,,0,0,0,,听起来很像那么回事 但是 像我说的\N{\r外文}that sounds pretty official to me, but, like I said,
Dialogue: 0,1:55:18.33,1:55:22.29,中文,,0,0,0,,我看只有我和你 所以你得来抓我\N{\r外文}I think it's just me and you here. So you'll have to catch me.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:22.38,1:55:24.88,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰克 这件事你得相信我\N{\r外文}Frank, you have to trust me on this.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:24.96,1:55:28.09,中文,,0,0,0,,这些人感到难堪 他们生气了\N{\r外文}These people have been embarrassed. They're angry.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:28.17,1:55:30.63,中文,,0,0,0,,你抢了他们的银行 偷了他们的钱 生活在他们的国家\N{\r外文}You rob their banks, you steal their money, you live in their country.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:30.72,1:55:32.97,中文,,0,0,0,,我告诉过你会这样的\N{\r外文}I told you this was what was going to happen.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:33.05,1:55:34.76,中文,,0,0,0,,没有其它了结方式\N{\r外文}That there was no other way for it to end.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:36.06,1:55:37.93,中文,,0,0,0,,不要搞错\N{\r外文}Don't make a mistake.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:38.14,1:55:40.39,中文,,0,0,0,,很好 卡尔 你知道吗\N{\r外文}That's good, Carl, you know?
Dialogue: 0,1:55:41.02,1:55:43.77,中文,,0,0,0,,接着编\N{\r外文}Keep pushing that lie. Keep pushing it.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:43.86,1:55:47.48,中文,,0,0,0,,接着编直到编成真的 他们会杀了你\N{\r外文}Keep pushing till you make it true. They'll kill you.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:47.82,1:55:50.03,中文,,0,0,0,,如果你走出那门 他们会杀了你\N{\r外文}You walk out that door, they're gonna kill you.
Dialogue: 0,1:55:55.28,1:55:57.03,中文,,0,0,0,,是真的吗\N{\r外文}Is that the truth?
Dialogue: 0,1:56:01.08,1:56:02.25,中文,,0,0,0,,是\N{\r外文}Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,1:56:08.00,1:56:09.55,中文,,0,0,0,,你有孩子吗\N{\r外文}Do you have any children, Carl?
Dialogue: 0,1:56:10.97,1:56:13.38,中文,,0,0,0,,有个4岁的女儿\N{\r外文}I have a 4-year-old daughter.
Dialogue: 0,1:56:14.22,1:56:16.55,中文,,0,0,0,,你凭你的女儿发誓\N{\r外文}Do you swear on your daughter?
Dialogue: 0,1:56:18.72,1:56:20.10,中文,,0,0,0,,你发誓\N{\r外文}You swear?
Dialogue: 0,1:56:25.48,1:56:26.81,中文,,0,0,0,,发誓\N{\r外文}You swear?
Dialogue: 0,1:56:58.80,1:57:00.97,中文,,0,0,0,,好极了 卡尔\N{\r外文}That was really good, Carl.
Dialogue: 0,1:57:08.69,1:57:10.02,中文,,0,0,0,,他由我监护\N{\r外文}I have him in custody.
Dialogue: 0,1:57:11.48,1:57:13.61,中文,,0,0,0,,我控制住他了 没关系\N{\r外文}I got him! It's all right.
Dialogue: 0,1:57:15.61,1:57:17.49,中文,,0,0,0,,没关系 我控制住他了\N{\r外文}It's all right. I got him.
Dialogue: 0,1:57:21.20,1:57:23.25,中文,,0,0,0,,我想做官方纪录\N{\r外文}I want it on the record.
Dialogue: 0,1:57:23.87,1:57:27.58,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰克·阿巴戈内尔自愿被捕 明白吗\N{\r外文}Frank Abagnale surrendered of his own accord. Understood?
Dialogue: 0,1:57:28.75,1:57:31.42,中文,,0,0,0,,你们要把他带哪里去 我应该跟着\N{\r外文}Where are you taking him? I'm supposed to go.
Dialogue: 0,1:57:33.34,1:57:35.93,中文,,0,0,0,,让我上车\N{\r外文}Let me in the car!
Dialogue: 0,1:57:41.68,1:57:45.43,中文,,0,0,0,,不要担心 我会把你引渡回美国的\N{\r外文}Don't worry. I'll have you extradited back to the United States.
Dialogue: 0,1:58:06.75,1:58:07.83,中文,,0,0,0,,卡尔\N{\r外文}Carl.
Dialogue: 0,1:58:11.50,1:58:15.26,中文,,0,0,0,,你得记着 我们一落地就让我给父亲打电话\N{\r外文}You have to remember to let me call my father when we land.
Dialogue: 0,1:58:15.34,1:58:20.09,中文,,0,0,0,,我想在他从电视或什么上看见我之前 跟他谈谈\N{\r外文}I want to talk to him before he sees me on television or something like that.
Dialogue: 0,1:58:30.40,1:58:31.81,中文,,0,0,0,,卡尔 看\N{\r外文}Carl, look.
Dialogue: 0,1:58:32.15,1:58:34.15,中文,,0,0,0,,那是纽约机场\N{\r外文}That's LaGuardia right there.
Dialogue: 0,1:58:34.23,1:58:35.61,中文,,0,0,0,,44号跑道\N{\r外文}Runway 44.
Dialogue: 0,1:58:35.74,1:58:37.90,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰克 你父亲死了\N{\r外文}Frank, your father is dead.
Dialogue: 0,1:58:38.74,1:58:40.11,中文,,0,0,0,,对不起\N{\r外文}I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,1:58:41.03,1:58:44.83,中文,,0,0,0,,在快到家之前我什么都不想说\N{\r外文}I didn't want to say anything until we got closer to home.
Dialogue: 0,1:58:45.66,1:58:50.29,中文,,0,0,0,,他在大中心车站赶火车时掉下台阶\N{\r外文}He fell down some steps at Grand Central Station trying to catch a train.
Dialogue: 0,1:58:50.83,1:58:52.88,中文,,0,0,0,,我本不想亲自告诉你\N{\r外文}I didn't want to be the one to tell you.
Dialogue: 0,1:58:53.88,1:58:55.71,中文,,0,0,0,,你撒谎 是吗\N{\r外文}You're lying, right?
Dialogue: 0,1:58:57.51,1:58:59.80,中文,,0,0,0,,你说过我可以跟他交谈\N{\r外文}You said I could talk to him.
Dialogue: 0,1:58:59.93,1:59:02.72,中文,,0,0,0,,你怎么敢说那样的话\N{\r外文}Who are you to say something like that?
Dialogue: 0,1:59:03.64,1:59:05.89,中文,,0,0,0,,你说过我可以跟他交谈 他掉下去\N{\r外文}You said I could talk to him. He fell
Dialogue: 0,1:59:05.97,1:59:08.48,中文,,0,0,0,,摔断了脖子 我很难过\N{\r外文}and he broke his neck. I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,1:59:09.64,1:59:11.35,中文,,0,0,0,,我真的很难过\N{\r外文}I'm really sorry.
Dialogue: 0,1:59:22.41,1:59:23.82,中文,,0,0,0,,见鬼\N{\r外文}God damn it!
Dialogue: 0,1:59:25.83,1:59:27.70,中文,,0,0,0,,我要吐了\N{\r外文}I'm going to be sick.
Dialogue: 0,1:59:28.12,1:59:29.96,中文,,0,0,0,,没关系的 没事的\N{\r外文}It's all right. It's okay.
Dialogue: 0,1:59:30.04,1:59:33.67,中文,,0,0,0,,我要吐了 当然 去卫生间吧\N{\r外文}I'm going to be sick! Sure. Let's go to the bathroom.
Dialogue: 0,1:59:40.59,1:59:42.01,中文,,0,0,0,,见鬼\N{\r外文}God damn it!
Dialogue: 0,2:00:01.74,2:00:02.95,中文,,0,0,0,,爸爸\N{\r外文}Daddy.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:05.57,2:00:06.83,中文,,0,0,0,,各位 请回到座位上\N{\r外文}You'll have to take your seat, sir.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:06.91,2:00:09.50,中文,,0,0,0,,要着陆了 我告诉过你2次了\N{\r外文}I've told you twice. We're landing. All of you.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:09.58,2:00:11.37,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰克 好了\N{\r外文}Frank! Come on now.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:11.62,2:00:14.50,中文,,0,0,0,,我们6分钟后着陆 你得回到座位\N{\r外文}We're landing in six minutes. You need to be in your seats...
Dialogue: 0,2:00:14.58,2:00:17.00,中文,,0,0,0,,开门 系上安全带\N{\r外文}Open the door! ...with seat belts fastened.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:20.26,2:00:21.59,中文,,0,0,0,,你来\N{\r外文}You do it.
Dialogue: 0,2:00:51.16,2:00:52.37,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰克\N{\r外文}Frank!
Dialogue: 0,2:00:58.34,2:01:01.30,中文,,0,0,0,,好 请大家坐着别动\N{\r外文}All right, remain seated everyone, please.
Dialogue: 0,2:01:10.43,2:01:12.35,中文,,0,0,0,,请坐好\N{\r外文}Please remain seated.
Dialogue: 0,2:01:15.27,2:01:16.77,中文,,0,0,0,,天啊\N{\r外文}God Almighty.
Dialogue: 0,2:02:06.49,2:02:08.20,中文,,0,0,0,,你叫什么名字\N{\r外文}What's your name?
Dialogue: 0,2:02:12.20,2:02:13.58,中文,,0,0,0,,你妈妈在哪里\N{\r外文}Where's your mommy?
Dialogue: 0,2:02:38.89,2:02:40.65,中文,,0,0,0,,警官 我们干得好\N{\r外文}Sarge, we're good.
Dialogue: 0,2:02:50.74,2:02:51.82,中文,,0,0,0,,等等\N{\r外文}Hold up!
Dialogue: 0,2:02:55.45,2:02:57.83,中文,,0,0,0,,把手放在脑后\N{\r外文}Put your hands behind your head!
Dialogue: 0,2:02:57.91,2:02:59.08,中文,,0,0,0,,卡尔\N{\r外文}Carl.
Dialogue: 0,2:02:59.29,2:03:01.42,中文,,0,0,0,,请让我上车吧\N{\r外文}Get me in the car, please.
Dialogue: 0,2:03:04.13,2:03:05.55,中文,,0,0,0,,让他上车\N{\r外文}Put him in.
Dialogue: 0,2:03:22.48,2:03:25.82,中文,,0,0,0,,鉴于罪行的严重性\N{\r外文}Taking into account the gravity of these crimes,
Dialogue: 0,2:03:25.98,2:03:29.07,中文,,0,0,0,,放肆和逃避的行为\N{\r外文}your history of bold and elusive behaviour
Dialogue: 0,2:03:29.40,2:03:33.32,中文,,0,0,0,,及对美国法律的蔑视\N{\r外文}and your complete lack of respect for the laws of the United States,
Dialogue: 0,2:03:33.91,2:03:38.33,中文,,0,0,0,,我不得不驳回你作为少年犯对待的请求\N{\r外文}I have no choice but to ignore your request to be treated as a minor,
Dialogue: 0,2:03:38.87,2:03:43.50,中文,,0,0,0,,判你在亚特兰大的最严密监视的监狱 服刑12年\N{\r外文}and sentence you to 12 years in Atlanta's maximum security prison
Dialogue: 0,2:03:44.13,2:03:47.76,中文,,0,0,0,,并强烈推荐在整个服刑期间\N{\r外文}and recommend strongly that you be kept in isolation
Dialogue: 0,2:03:47.92,2:03:50.47,中文,,0,0,0,,对你进行隔离\N{\r外文}for the entirety of that sentence.
Dialogue: 0,2:04:32.55,2:04:34.18,中文,,0,0,0,,圣诞快乐 弗兰克\N{\r外文}Merry Christmas, Frank.
Dialogue: 0,2:04:37.22,2:04:39.39,中文,,0,0,0,,我给你带来了几本喜剧书\N{\r外文}I got you some comic books.
Dialogue: 0,2:04:39.56,2:04:41.27,中文,,0,0,0,,《闪电》
Dialogue: 0,2:04:46.31,2:04:48.73,中文,,0,0,0,,你女儿怎样 她叫什么名字\N{\r外文}How's your daughter? What was her name?
Dialogue: 0,2:04:49.11,2:04:50.32,中文,,0,0,0,,格雷斯\N{\r外文}Grace.
Dialogue: 0,2:04:52.03,2:04:55.16,中文,,0,0,0,,我不知道 她跟母亲在芝加哥生活 我不常见她\N{\r外文}I don't know. She lives with her mother in Chicago, I don't get to see her much.
Dialogue: 0,2:04:57.24,2:04:59.28,中文,,0,0,0,,箱子里是什么\N{\r外文}What's in the briefcase?
Dialogue: 0,2:05:00.29,2:05:02.58,中文,,0,0,0,,我是在去机场的路上\N{\r外文}I'm on my way to the airport.
Dialogue: 0,2:05:02.87,2:05:05.54,中文,,0,0,0,,是个在明尼苏达州活动的伪造支票者\N{\r外文}It's a paperhanger working his way through Minnesota.
Dialogue: 0,2:05:07.13,2:05:09.42,中文,,0,0,0,,天啊 他搞得我们发疯\N{\r外文}Jesus. He's driving us crazy.
Dialogue: 0,2:05:09.71,2:05:11.17,中文,,0,0,0,,你带来支票了吗\N{\r外文}You got any of the checks?
Dialogue: 0,2:05:11.51,2:05:14.13,中文,,0,0,0,,对 我带了张他在\N{\r外文}Yeah, I got a counterfeit he drew
Dialogue: 0,2:05:14.43,2:05:16.68,中文,,0,0,0,,大湖储贷银行填写的假支票\N{\r外文}in Great Lakes Savings and Loan.
Dialogue: 0,2:05:16.76,2:05:19.81,中文,,0,0,0,,他使用一台模版机和一台"木下"牌打字机\N{\r外文}He's using a stencil machine and an Underwood.
Dialogue: 0,2:05:20.26,2:05:21.85,中文,,0,0,0,,伪造者是名银行出纳\N{\r外文}It's a teller at the bank.
Dialogue: 0,2:05:22.27,2:05:23.56,中文,,0,0,0,,什么\N{\r外文}Say again?
Dialogue: 0,2:05:23.64,2:05:25.35,中文,,0,0,0,,肯定是出纳\N{\r外文}It's definitely a teller, Carl.
Dialogue: 0,2:05:25.44,2:05:28.36,中文,,0,0,0,,银行从来都是用手工封盖日期\N{\r外文}Banks always use hand stamps for the dates.
Dialogue: 0,2:05:28.44,2:05:31.61,中文,,0,0,0,,一遍遍使用 所以总有磨损\N{\r外文}They get used over and over again, so they always get worn out.
Dialogue: 0,2:05:31.69,2:05:35.24,中文,,0,0,0,,数字总是有断点 6 9\N{\r外文}And the numbers are always cracking. The sixes and the nines,
Dialogue: 0,2:05:35.32,2:05:37.11,中文,,0,0,0,,看 它们先磨损\N{\r外文}see, they go first.
Dialogue: 0,2:05:39.53,2:05:40.78,中文,,0,0,0,,谢谢\N{\r外文}Thanks.
Dialogue: 0,2:05:46.87,2:05:49.71,中文,,0,0,0,,我想让你给我看样东西\N{\r外文}I'd like you to take a look at something for me.
Dialogue: 0,2:05:53.96,2:05:55.97,中文,,0,0,0,,告诉我你是怎么想的\N{\r外文}Tell me what you think.
Dialogue: 0,2:05:59.47,2:06:01.01,中文,,0,0,0,,这是假的\N{\r外文}That's a fake.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:01.14,2:06:02.47,中文,,0,0,0,,你怎么知道 你还没看呢\N{\r外文}How do you know, you haven't looked at it?
Dialogue: 0,2:06:02.56,2:06:04.68,中文,,0,0,0,,没有撕开的边\N{\r外文}There's no perforated edge, right?
Dialogue: 0,2:06:04.81,2:06:07.73,中文,,0,0,0,,我是说 这张支票是手工裁剪的 不是从大张上撕下的\N{\r外文}I mean, this cheque was hand-cut, not fed.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:09.06,2:06:10.27,中文,,0,0,0,,并且\N{\r外文}Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:10.36,2:06:14.15,中文,,0,0,0,,纸是双层的 作为银行支票太重了\N{\r外文}Paper is double-bonded, much too heavy to be a bank cheque.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:15.32,2:06:19.32,中文,,0,0,0,,这磁墨应该是平的 我却能用手感觉到的凸起\N{\r外文}Magnetic ink, it's raised against my fingers instead of flat.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:21.03,2:06:25.33,中文,,0,0,0,,并且闻起来不像支票专用墨 是一种画图用墨\N{\r外文}And this doesn't smell like MICR, it's some kind of a drafting ink.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:25.41,2:06:28.21,中文,,0,0,0,,在文具店能买到这种墨\N{\r外文}The kind you get at a stationery store.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:33.50,2:06:34.76,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰克\N{\r外文}Frank,
Dialogue: 0,2:06:35.51,2:06:40.09,中文,,0,0,0,,你对在联邦调查局经济犯罪科工作 有没有兴趣\N{\r外文}would you be interested in working with the F.B.I.'s Financial Crimes Unit?
Dialogue: 0,2:06:40.43,2:06:43.85,中文,,0,0,0,,我在这里已经有工作了 你知道 我送信\N{\r外文}I already got a job here, you know. I deliver the mail.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:46.39,2:06:49.81,中文,,0,0,0,,我们能把你从监狱里放出来\N{\r外文}Frank, we have the power to take you out of prison.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:50.98,2:06:53.44,中文,,0,0,0,,你将在联邦调查局的监护下\N{\r外文}You'll be placed in the custody of the F.B.I. where you'd serve out
Dialogue: 0,2:06:53.52,2:06:56.24,中文,,0,0,0,,作为联邦政府的雇员服完剩下的刑\N{\r外文}the remainder of your sentence as an employee of the Federal Government.
Dialogue: 0,2:06:59.20,2:07:01.03,中文,,0,0,0,,在谁的监护下\N{\r外文}Under whose custody?
Dialogue: 0,2:07:07.42,2:07:09.34,中文,,0,0,0,,联邦调查局10名最大通缉犯
Dialogue: 0,2:07:09.87,2:07:11.08,中文,,0,0,0,,嗨\N{\r外文}Hi.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:11.21,2:07:14.88,中文,,0,0,0,,我叫弗兰克·阿巴戈内尔 我应该今天开始工作\N{\r外文}I'm Frank Abagnale. I'm supposed to start work here today.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:14.96,2:07:18.09,中文,,0,0,0,,是个安排英国处女岛度假的旅游公司\N{\r外文}It's a tour company operating out of the BVI.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:18.30,2:07:19.97,中文,,0,0,0,,先生 阿巴戈内尔来了\N{\r外文}Sir, Mr Abagnale is here.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:20.05,2:07:22.09,中文,,0,0,0,,我再给你回电话\N{\r外文}I'm gonna call you back.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:52.08,2:07:54.79,中文,,0,0,0,,你好 卡尔 欢迎来到联邦调查局\N{\r外文}Hello, Carl. Welcome to the F.B.I.
Dialogue: 0,2:07:55.42,2:07:57.96,中文,,0,0,0,,我带你看你工作的地方\N{\r外文}I'll show you where you're working.
Dialogue: 0,2:08:06.93,2:08:09.35,中文,,0,0,0,,我要在这里工作多久\N{\r外文}How long do I have to work here?
Dialogue: 0,2:08:09.47,2:08:12.06,中文,,0,0,0,,早上8点15分到晚上5点钟\N{\r外文}It's 8:15 in the morning to 5:00 in the afternoon,
Dialogue: 0,2:08:12.14,2:08:14.10,中文,,0,0,0,,午休45分钟\N{\r外文}45 minutes for lunch.
Dialogue: 0,2:08:15.94,2:08:17.69,中文,,0,0,0,,不 我是说 多久\N{\r外文}No. I mean, how long?
Dialogue: 0,2:08:19.36,2:08:20.78,中文,,0,0,0,,每天\N{\r外文}Every day.
Dialogue: 0,2:08:21.28,2:08:23.53,中文,,0,0,0,,每天直到我们放你走\N{\r外文}Every day, Frank, till we let you go.
Dialogue: 0,2:08:26.25,2:08:28.33,中文,,0,0,0,,支票欺诈科
Dialogue: 0,2:09:17.42,2:09:18.75,中文,,0,0,0,,嗨 卡尔\N{\r外文}Hey, Carl.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:21.34,2:09:22.59,中文,,0,0,0,,你好吗\N{\r外文}How are you doing?
Dialogue: 0,2:09:22.67,2:09:26.51,中文,,0,0,0,,还不坏 我在为周末整理桌子\N{\r外文}It's not a good time, Frank. I'm clearing my desk for the weekend.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:29.51,2:09:32.22,中文,,0,0,0,,你介意我明天来跟你一起工作吗\N{\r外文}You mind if I come to work with you tomorrow?
Dialogue: 0,2:09:32.35,2:09:34.18,中文,,0,0,0,,明天是星期六\N{\r外文}Tomorrow is Saturday.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:34.27,2:09:36.14,中文,,0,0,0,,我要飞到芝加哥看我女儿\N{\r外文}I'm flying to Chicago to see my daughter.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:36.23,2:09:37.56,中文,,0,0,0,,星期一回来\N{\r外文}I'll be back to work on Monday.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:37.69,2:09:41.07,中文,,0,0,0,,你去见格雷斯 对 是我的计划\N{\r外文}You're going to see Grace? Yeah, that's the plan.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:44.74,2:09:46.78,中文,,0,0,0,,星期一前我该干什么\N{\r外文}What should I do till Monday?
Dialogue: 0,2:09:46.86,2:09:50.20,中文,,0,0,0,,对不起 孩子 这我帮不了你 对不起\N{\r外文}I'm sorry, kid, I can't help you there. Excuse me.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:56.54,2:09:58.25,中文,,0,0,0,,这是汉莱提\N{\r外文}This is Hanratty.
Dialogue: 0,2:09:58.96,2:10:00.71,中文,,0,0,0,,好 接过来\N{\r外文}Yeah, put him on.
Dialogue: 0,2:10:08.89,2:10:10.26,中文,,0,0,0,,斯耶先生\N{\r外文}Mr Sawyer.
Dialogue: 0,2:10:10.97,2:10:12.43,中文,,0,0,0,,你好\N{\r外文}How are you?
Dialogue: 0,2:10:12.72,2:10:16.60,中文,,0,0,0,,我还有6张关于那家英国处女岛 旅游公司的支票\N{\r外文}I have half a dozen more cheques on that tour operator at the BVI.
Dialogue: 0,2:10:21.53,2:10:23.48,中文,,0,0,0,,被拘捕的
Dialogue: 0,2:10:56.93,2:10:58.94,中文,,0,0,0,,你怎么办到的 弗兰克\N{\r外文}How did you do it, Frank?
Dialogue: 0,2:11:00.77,2:11:03.44,中文,,0,0,0,,你是怎么通过路易斯安娜州的律师考试的\N{\r外文}How did you pass the bar in Louisiana?
Dialogue: 0,2:11:03.52,2:11:05.61,中文,,0,0,0,,你来这干什么\N{\r外文}What are you doing here?
Dialogue: 0,2:11:06.28,2:11:07.49,中文,,0,0,0,,听着\N{\r外文}Listen.
Dialogue: 0,2:11:08.20,2:11:10.11,中文,,0,0,0,,我很抱歉给你惹了这么多麻烦\N{\r外文}I'm sorry I put you through all this.
Dialogue: 0,2:11:10.20,2:11:12.99,中文,,0,0,0,,你要是回到欧洲 会死在坡皮监狱的\N{\r外文}You go back to Europe, you'll die in Perpignan Prison.
Dialogue: 0,2:11:13.08,2:11:14.03,中文,,0,0,0,,如果你想从美国逃跑\N{\r外文}You try to run here in the States,
Dialogue: 0,2:11:14.12,2:11:17.45,中文,,0,0,0,,我们就会把你 送回亚特兰大关50年\N{\r外文}we'll send you back to Atlanta for 50 years.
Dialogue: 0,2:11:17.54,2:11:19.00,中文,,0,0,0,,我知道\N{\r外文}I know that.
Dialogue: 0,2:11:20.67,2:11:23.17,中文,,0,0,0,,我花了4年时间设法把你放出来\N{\r外文}I spent four years trying to arrange your release.
Dialogue: 0,2:11:23.29,2:11:25.09,中文,,0,0,0,,我得向我的老板\N{\r外文}I had to convince my bosses at the F.B.I.
Dialogue: 0,2:11:25.17,2:11:28.05,中文,,0,0,0,,和首席检察官证明 你不会逃跑\N{\r外文}and the Attorney General of the United States you wouldn't run.
Dialogue: 0,2:11:28.55,2:11:30.30,中文,,0,0,0,,你为什么那样做呢\N{\r外文}Why did you do it?
Dialogue: 0,2:11:31.01,2:11:33.72,中文,,0,0,0,,你是个孩子 我不是你的孩子\N{\r外文}You're just a kid. I'm not your kid.
Dialogue: 0,2:11:34.14,2:11:36.52,中文,,0,0,0,,你说你要去芝加哥\N{\r外文}You said you were going to Chicago.
Dialogue: 0,2:11:36.68,2:11:40.48,中文,,0,0,0,,我女儿这个周末不能见我了 她去滑雪\N{\r外文}My daughter can't see me this weekend. She's going skiing.
Dialogue: 0,2:11:41.02,2:11:43.31,中文,,0,0,0,,你说她4岁 你撒谎\N{\r外文}You said she was four years old. You're lying.
Dialogue: 0,2:11:43.40,2:11:46.19,中文,,0,0,0,,我离开时她4岁 现在15岁了\N{\r外文}She was four when I left. Now she's 15.
Dialogue: 0,2:11:46.69,2:11:49.57,中文,,0,0,0,,我太太再结婚11年了\N{\r外文}My wife has been remarried for 11 years.
Dialogue: 0,2:11:49.65,2:11:52.07,中文,,0,0,0,,我有时见格雷斯\N{\r外文}I see Grace every now and again.
Dialogue: 0,2:11:52.82,2:11:55.33,中文,,0,0,0,,我不明白 你当然明白\N{\r外文}I don't understand. Sure you do.
Dialogue: 0,2:11:56.16,2:11:58.87,中文,,0,0,0,,有时说谎更容易\N{\r外文}Sometimes it's easier living the lie.
Dialogue: 0,2:12:02.17,2:12:04.50,中文,,0,0,0,,我今晚让你飞走\N{\r外文}I'm gonna let you fly tonight, Frank.
Dialogue: 0,2:12:05.34,2:12:09.51,中文,,0,0,0,,我甚至不会拦你的 因为我知道 你星期一会回来\N{\r外文}I won't even try to stop you, because I know you'll be back on Monday.
Dialogue: 0,2:12:09.59,2:12:10.76,中文,,0,0,0,,对\N{\r外文}Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,2:12:11.26,2:12:13.68,中文,,0,0,0,,你怎么知道我会回来\N{\r外文}How do you know I'll come back?
Dialogue: 0,2:12:16.05,2:12:17.18,中文,,0,0,0,,看\N{\r外文}Look.
Dialogue: 0,2:12:19.72,2:12:21.69,中文,,0,0,0,,没有人在追你\N{\r外文}Nobody is chasing you.
Dialogue: 0,2:12:42.12,2:12:44.54,中文,,0,0,0,,埃利斯 他还没来电话吗\N{\r外文}Alice, has he still not called?
Dialogue: 0,2:12:44.62,2:12:46.21,中文,,0,0,0,,对 还没有\N{\r外文}No, he hasn't.
Dialogue: 0,2:12:57.72,2:12:59.01,中文,,0,0,0,,早晨好\N{\r外文}Good morning.
Dialogue: 0,2:12:59.10,2:13:01.14,中文,,0,0,0,,我召集这次会议是为了研讨\N{\r外文}I've called this meeting to discuss
Dialogue: 0,2:13:01.22,2:13:03.56,中文,,0,0,0,,一种新型的支票欺诈和伪造手段\N{\r外文}a new type of cheque fraud and counterfeiting.
Dialogue: 0,2:13:03.64,2:13:05.85,中文,,0,0,0,,嫌疑犯涂改支票\N{\r外文}The unsub is washing and altering checks,
Dialogue: 0,2:13:05.94,2:13:07.52,中文,,0,0,0,,然后发送到亚利桑那州\N{\r外文}then passing them throughout Arizona.
Dialogue: 0,2:13:12.24,2:13:16.41,中文,,0,0,0,,这个嫌疑犯是个大赌徒 支票填5位数\N{\r外文}This unsub is a big dog, passing cheques as large as five figures.
Dialogue: 0,2:13:19.78,2:13:21.41,中文,,0,0,0,,对不起我迟到了\N{\r外文}Sorry I'm late.
Dialogue: 0,2:13:22.70,2:13:23.91,中文,,0,0,0,,对不起\N{\r外文}Sorry.
Dialogue: 0,2:13:28.13,2:13:31.00,中文,,0,0,0,,瑞特特工的桌子上有张伪造的支票\N{\r外文}We have a recovered cheque on Agent Reiter's desk.
Dialogue: 0,2:13:31.09,2:13:33.80,中文,,0,0,0,,我们走出会议室吧\N{\r外文}Why don't we step out to the bullpen?
Dialogue: 0,2:13:35.35,2:13:38.20,中文,,0,0,0,,福莱格斯达福联邦储蓄
Dialogue: 0,2:13:38.22,2:13:40.76,中文,,0,0,0,,每一行都被加重\N{\r外文}There's impressions on every line.
Dialogue: 0,2:13:42.43,2:13:45.44,中文,,0,0,0,,好像原来数额是60美元\N{\r外文}Looks like the original amount was for $60.
Dialogue: 0,2:13:48.98,2:13:50.90,中文,,0,0,0,,我能看一下吗\N{\r外文}Mind if I take a look?
Dialogue: 0,2:13:53.99,2:13:56.40,中文,,0,0,0,,一周前在福莱格斯达福兑现的\N{\r外文}Cashed in Flagstaff a week ago.
Dialogue: 0,2:13:59.16,2:14:01.24,中文,,0,0,0,,银行损失1万6千美元\N{\r外文}Cost the bank $16,000.
Dialogue: 0,2:14:02.91,2:14:04.96,中文,,0,0,0,,是张真支票 对\N{\r外文}It's a real cheque. Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,2:14:05.62,2:14:09.04,中文,,0,0,0,,被洗过了 原来的东西只剩下签名\N{\r外文}It's been washed. The only thing original is the signature.
Dialogue: 0,2:14:09.13,2:14:10.84,中文,,0,0,0,,但是很完美\N{\r外文}But it's perfect.
Dialogue: 0,2:14:11.25,2:14:14.17,中文,,0,0,0,,我是说 它不是用酸洗或漂白的\N{\r外文}I mean, this isn't hydrochloride or bleach.
Dialogue: 0,2:14:14.34,2:14:15.47,中文,,0,0,0,,不是\N{\r外文}No.
Dialogue: 0,2:14:15.59,2:14:17.13,中文,,0,0,0,,是什么新东西\N{\r外文}Something new.
Dialogue: 0,2:14:17.30,2:14:21.51,中文,,0,0,0,,一种能洗去手写墨水的洗指甲水\N{\r外文}A nail polish remover where the acetone removes the ink that's not been printed?
Dialogue: 0,2:14:25.43,2:14:27.23,中文,,0,0,0,,你是怎么做的\N{\r外文}How did you do it, Frank?
Dialogue: 0,2:14:28.65,2:14:31.82,中文,,0,0,0,,你是怎么骗过路易斯安娜州的律师考试的\N{\r外文}How did you cheat on the bar exam in Louisiana?
Dialogue: 0,2:14:36.99,2:14:38.61,中文,,0,0,0,,我没欺骗\N{\r外文}I didn't cheat.
Dialogue: 0,2:14:40.16,2:14:42.87,中文,,0,0,0,,我学了2周就通过了\N{\r外文}I studied for two weeks and I passed.
Dialogue: 0,2:14:45.00,2:14:46.59,中文,,0,0,0,,是真的吗\N{\r外文}Is that the truth?
Dialogue: 0,2:14:47.79,2:14:48.69,中文,,0,0,0,,是真的吗\N{\r外文}Is that the truth?
Dialogue: 0,2:14:48.79,2:14:51.96,中文,,0,0,0,,我肯定这家伙从邮箱里偷支票\N{\r外文}I'll bet this guy steals cheques out of mailboxes.
Dialogue: 0,2:14:52.04,2:14:55.17,中文,,0,0,0,,他洗掉他们的名字 换成自己的名字\N{\r外文}He washes off their names and puts on his own.
Dialogue: 0,2:14:56.63,2:14:58.76,中文,,0,0,0,,你说他是当地人\N{\r外文}You're saying he's a local?
Dialogue: 0,2:14:58.84,2:15:02.60,中文,,0,0,0,,如果是我的话 会先给银行打电话 查一下余额\N{\r外文}If it were me, I'd call the bank first. Check out the balance...
Dialogue: 0,2:15:02.68,2:15:04.97,中文,,0,0,0,,确保有可赚的钱\N{\r外文}Make sure there's enough money in there to make it worth your while.
Dialogue: 0,2:15:05.06,2:15:06.18,中文,,0,0,0,,很对\N{\r外文}Exactly.
Dialogue: 0,2:15:06.52,2:15:09.52,中文,,0,0,0,,我想这家伙非常狡猾\N{\r外文}You know, Carl, I think this guy is pretty smart.
Dialogue: 0,2:15:10.02,2:15:12.40,中文,,0,0,0,,我想现在我们要做的就是去抓住他\N{\r外文}Guess all we have to do now is catch him.
Dialogue: 0,2:15:13.53,2:15:15.99,中文,,0,0,0,,小弗兰克·阿巴戈内尔结婚26年
Dialogue: 0,2:15:16.16,2:15:18.87,中文,,0,0,0,,他有3个儿子 在中西部过着安静的生活
Dialogue: 0,2:15:19.04,2:15:22.66,中文,,0,0,0,,他1974年出狱后 弗兰克帮助联邦调查局捕获
Dialogue: 0,2:15:22.83,2:15:24.37,中文,,0,0,0,,一些世界上最狡猾的
Dialogue: 0,2:15:24.54,2:15:26.04,中文,,0,0,0,,支票伪造犯
Dialogue: 0,2:15:26.21,2:15:27.54,中文,,0,0,0,,被认为是世界上
Dialogue: 0,2:15:27.71,2:15:29.34,中文,,0,0,0,,银行欺诈和伪造案的
Dialogue: 0,2:15:29.51,2:15:31.38,中文,,0,0,0,,权威人士之一
Dialogue: 0,2:15:34.76,2:15:37.64,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰克设计了很多安全的支票
Dialogue: 0,2:15:37.80,2:15:41.85,中文,,0,0,0,,现在世界上的银行和500大财团每天都在使用
Dialogue: 0,2:15:43.64,2:15:46.08,中文,,0,0,0,,这些公司每年给小弗兰克·阿巴戈内尔
Dialogue: 0,2:15:46.25,2:15:48.14,中文,,0,0,0,,支付数百万美元
Dialogue: 0,2:15:49.40,2:15:54.32,中文,,0,0,0,,弗兰克和卡尔到今天一直是好朋友